#: tour-women
#. Title of a guided tour.
msgctxt "tour.women.title"
msgid "Women in the museum"
msgstr "Kobiety w muzeum"

#: tour-women
#. One sentence under the title of the tour, saying what it is.
msgctxt "tour.women.lead"
msgid "A guided walk through all seven halls. Fourteen displays, from braille pins to a room of screens, each with at least one woman on its label."
msgstr "Spacer z przewodnikiem przez wszystkie siedem sal. Czternaście wyświetlaczy, od brajlowskich trzpieni po pomieszczenie z ekranów, a w opisie każdego co najmniej jedna kobieta."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, before the first stop: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.women.start.title"
msgid "Before the first stop"
msgstr "Przed pierwszym przystankiem"

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, before the first stop: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 2. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.start.text.1"
msgid "Welcome to the museum. This tour follows the green line on the floor. It runs through all seven halls and stops at fourteen displays. Each has at least one woman on its label."
msgstr "Witaj w muzeum. To zwiedzanie prowadzi wzdłuż zielonej linii na podłodze. Linia biegnie przez wszystkie siedem sal i zatrzymuje się przy czternastu wyświetlaczach. Opis każdego z nich wymienia co najmniej jedną kobietę."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, before the first stop: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 2. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.start.text.2"
msgid "The tour waits at each stop. Press the key for the next stop when you are ready. The first is the braille display in hall 1, where the picture is made of pins."
msgstr "Zwiedzanie czeka na ciebie przy każdym przystanku. Gdy zechcesz iść dalej, naciśnij przycisk „Następny przystanek”. Pierwszy to monitor brajlowski w sali 1, gdzie obraz tworzą trzpienie."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Refreshable braille display: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.women.braille-display.title"
msgid "Read by touch"
msgstr "Czytane dotykiem"

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Refreshable braille display: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.braille-display.text.1"
msgid "This display is read by touch. Rows of pins rise and fall to spell a line of braille. The model is spelling the time. Watch the cells on the right. They change every second."
msgstr "Ten wyświetlacz czyta się dotykiem. Rzędy trzpieni podnoszą się i opadają, układając linijkę pisma Braille’a. Model wypisuje godzinę. Patrz na komórki po prawej. Zmieniają się co sekundę."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Refreshable braille display: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.braille-display.text.2"
msgid "Under each dot is a crystal that bends when a voltage reaches it, and a lever turns that small bend into the rise of a pin. Andrée Tretiakoff's name is on the patent for it, beside Oleg Tretiakoff's: a United States patent filed in 1975, which goes back to a French filing of August 1974."
msgstr "Pod każdym punktem jest kryształ, który wygina się, gdy dociera do niego napięcie, a dźwignia zamienia to niewielkie wygięcie w uniesienie trzpienia. Nazwisko Andrée Tretiakoff widnieje na patencie, obok nazwiska Olega Tretiakoffa: na patencie amerykańskim zgłoszonym w 1975 roku, który sięga francuskiego zgłoszenia z sierpnia 1974 roku."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Refreshable braille display: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.braille-display.text.3"
msgid "It is the only piece in the museum that needs no light at all. The next is the cathode ray tube in hall 2. The woman there is on no patent: a news agency kept her part."
msgstr "To jedyny eksponat w muzeum, który w ogóle nie potrzebuje światła. Następny jest kineskop w sali 2. Kobiety stamtąd nie ma na żadnym patencie: jej udział zachowała agencja prasowa."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Cathode ray tube: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.women.cathode-ray-tube.title"
msgid "A beam that draws"
msgstr "Wiązka, która rysuje"

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Cathode ray tube: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.cathode-ray-tube.text.1"
msgid "Look at the screen. The bright band moving down it is where one beam of electrons has just drawn its lines. The model slows it about 60 times. From the side you can see the copper coils that steer the beam."
msgstr "Spójrz na ekran. Jasny pas, który przesuwa się w dół, to miejsce, gdzie jedna wiązka elektronów właśnie narysowała swoje linie. Model spowalnia ją mniej więcej 60 razy. Z boku widać miedziane cewki, które sterują wiązką."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Cathode ray tube: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.cathode-ray-tube.text.2"
msgid "The plate on the block names Ferdinand Braun, who built his cathode ray tube in Strasbourg in 1897. Thirty years later, in San Francisco, the team of Philo Farnsworth sent a television picture made entirely by electronics. A California historical landmark calls it the first such picture. Elma Farnsworth, known as Pem, was on that team. She kept the logbooks, made technical drawings and welded parts of the tubes. Her face was among the first that the system sent. We know it because the Associated Press reported it, citing the historian Donald G. Godfrey."
msgstr "Tabliczka na postumencie wymienia Ferdinanda Brauna, który w 1897 roku zbudował w Strasburgu swoją lampę katodową. Trzydzieści lat później, w San Francisco, zespół Philo Farnswortha przesłał obraz telewizyjny wytworzony w całości elektronicznie. Kalifornijski pomnik historii nazywa go pierwszym takim obrazem. Elma Farnsworth, zwana Pem, należała do tego zespołu. Prowadziła dzienniki laboratoryjne, wykonywała rysunki techniczne i spawała części lamp. Jej twarz była wśród pierwszych, które przesłał ten system. Wiemy o tym, bo podała to Associated Press, powołując się na historyka Donalda G. Godfreya."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Cathode ray tube: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.cathode-ray-tube.text.3"
msgid "In hall 1 the picture was made of pins. Here one beam draws all of it. The next stop is the MicroLED wall in hall 3, where the picture is made of lamps."
msgstr "W sali 1 obraz tworzyły trzpienie. Tutaj cały obraz rysuje jedna wiązka. Następny przystanek to ściana MicroLED w sali 3, gdzie obraz tworzą lampki."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece MicroLED: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.women.microled.title"
msgid "A question at dinner"
msgstr "Pytanie przy kolacji"

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece MicroLED: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.microled.text.1"
msgid "The wall in front of you is made of LEDs, each too small to see. One tile is out and leans against the stand, with the suction lifter still on it. A wall like this is repaired one square at a time."
msgstr "Ściana przed tobą składa się z diod LED, z których każda jest zbyt mała, by ją zobaczyć. Jedna płytka jest wyjęta i opiera się o postument, wciąż z przyssawką do podnoszenia. Taką ścianę naprawia się po jednym kwadracie."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece MicroLED: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.microled.text.2"
msgid "Jingyu Lin and Hongxing Jiang are physicists. By their own account, their team at Kansas State University saw blue light from a microLED in August 1999. They published it in 2000. They are also a married couple, and the idea began as a question at their dinner table: what would happen to an LED shrunk to thousandths of a millimetre?"
msgstr "Jingyu Lin jest fizyczką, a Hongxing Jiang fizykiem. Według ich własnej relacji ich zespół na Uniwersytecie Stanowym Kansas zobaczył niebieskie światło mikrodiody LED w sierpniu 1999 roku. Opublikowali to w 2000 roku. Są też małżeństwem, a pomysł zrodził się z pytania przy ich stole w czasie kolacji: co stałoby się z diodą LED zmniejszoną do tysięcznych części milimetra?"

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece MicroLED: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.microled.text.3"
msgid "Stay in hall 3. The next stop, the quantum-dot display, works with crystals far smaller than these lamps."
msgstr "Zostań w sali 3. Następny przystanek, wyświetlacz z kropkami kwantowymi, działa dzięki kryształom o wiele mniejszym niż te lampki."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Quantum-dot display: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.women.quantum-dot.title"
msgid "Colour from size"
msgstr "Barwa z rozmiaru"

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Quantum-dot display: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.quantum-dot.text.1"
msgid "This is one pixel, cut open and greatly enlarged. Blue light rises from the lamps on the board. In the left well, large crystals turn it red. In the middle well, small ones turn it green. The right well has no crystals, and the blue passes through. The size of a crystal alone sets its colour."
msgstr "To jeden piksel, rozcięty i bardzo powiększony. Niebieskie światło wznosi się z lampek na płytce. W lewej komorze duże kryształy zmieniają je w czerwone. W środkowej komorze małe kryształy zmieniają je w zielone. Prawa komora nie ma kryształów i niebieskie światło przez nią przechodzi. Sam rozmiar kryształu wyznacza jego barwę."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Quantum-dot display: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.quantum-dot.text.2"
msgid "The crystals are called quantum dots. Most screens use them as this model does, to turn blue light into red and green. In 1994, at Berkeley, Vicki Colvin and two colleagues took another route. They made a layer of dots glow by passing a current through it. Her name stands first on the paper of 1994."
msgstr "Te kryształy nazywa się kropkami kwantowymi. Większość ekranów używa ich tak jak ten model, aby zmieniać niebieskie światło w czerwone i zielone. W 1994 roku w Berkeley Vicki Colvin i dwie współpracujące z nią osoby poszły inną drogą. Sprawiły, że warstwa kropek świeciła, gdy przepuszczały przez nią prąd. Jej nazwisko stoi na pierwszym miejscu w artykule z 1994 roku."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Quantum-dot display: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.quantum-dot.text.3"
msgid "The cathode ray tube, the LED wall and this pixel all make their own light. In hall 4 the sun, a lamp or a laser makes the light, and the display shapes it. Go to the shadow play, where the lamp is a flame behind a cloth."
msgstr "Lampa kineskopowa, ściana LED i ten piksel same wytwarzają światło. W sali 4 światło wytwarza słońce, lampa lub laser, a wyświetlacz je kształtuje. Podejdź do gry cieni, gdzie lampą jest płomień za płótnem."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Shadow play: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.women.shadow-play.title"
msgid "A flame and a cloth"
msgstr "Płomień i płótno"

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Shadow play: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.shadow-play.text.1"
msgid "Look at the cloth. A flame burns behind it, and three flat figures stand between the flame and the cloth: a tree, a deer and a bird. What you see are their shadows. Watch the bird. When it flies towards the lamp, its shadow grows and its edge goes soft."
msgstr "Spójrz na płótno. Za nim pali się płomień, a między płomieniem a płótnem stoją trzy płaskie figury: drzewo, jeleń i ptak. To, co widzisz, to ich cienie. Patrz na ptaka. Gdy leci w stronę lampy, jego cień rośnie, a krawędź się rozmywa."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Shadow play: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.shadow-play.text.2"
msgid "Nobody knows who first did this. It is recorded in Java and in China about a thousand years ago, and it is performed today. Holes cut through a figure let the light pass and draw an eye or a feather inside the shadow. In Berlin, Lotte Reiniger cut figures from black card and filmed them a frame at a time. Her Adventures of Prince Achmed, of 1926, is the oldest surviving animated feature, and her name is in its credits for the silhouettes. Stay a minute: the cloth plays a second act in her manner."
msgstr "Nikt nie wie, kto zrobił to pierwszy. Jest to poświadczone na Jawie i w Chinach około tysiąca lat temu i wystawia się to do dziś. Otwory wycięte w figurze przepuszczają światło i rysują w cieniu oko albo pióro. W Berlinie Lotte Reiniger wycinała figury z czarnego kartonu i filmowała je klatka po klatce. Jej Przygody księcia Achmeda z 1926 roku to najstarszy zachowany pełnometrażowy film animowany, a jej nazwisko widnieje w napisach przy sylwetkach. Zostań minutę: płótno pokaże drugi akt na jej sposób."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Shadow play: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.shadow-play.text.3"
msgid "The first stop needed no light at all. This one needs only a flame. The next stop, in this hall, draws with a beam of light. Go to the scanned laser."
msgstr "Pierwszy przystanek w ogóle nie potrzebował światła. Ten potrzebuje tylko płomienia. Następny przystanek, w tej sali, rysuje wiązką światła. Podejdź do skanowanej wiązki laserowej."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Scanned laser: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.women.scanned-laser.title"
msgid "Drawing with a laser"
msgstr "Rysowanie laserem"

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Scanned laser: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.scanned-laser.text.1"
msgid "Follow the beams from left to right. Three lasers merge into one white beam. Two small mirrors on fast motors steer it, and your eye joins the moving dot into a drawing on the wall."
msgstr "Prześledź wiązki od lewej do prawej. Trzy lasery łączą się w jedną białą wiązkę. Sterują nią dwa małe lusterka na szybkich silnikach, a twoje oko łączy poruszający się punkt w rysunek na ścianie."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Scanned laser: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.scanned-laser.text.2"
msgid "The plate names Joseph Ostoja-Kotkowski, who staged an early laser show in Adelaide in 1968. Elsa Garmire, a physicist at the California Institute of Technology, made laser images. The filmmaker Ivan Dryer filmed them from late 1970. The two started the company that made Laserium, and Garmire was its president. Laserium opened at Griffith Observatory in Los Angeles in 1973."
msgstr "Tabliczka wymienia Josepha Ostoję-Kotkowskiego, który w 1968 roku zorganizował w Adelajdzie wczesny pokaz laserowy. Elsa Garmire, fizyczka z California Institute of Technology, tworzyła obrazy laserowe. Filmowiec Ivan Dryer filmował je od końca 1970 roku. Razem założyli firmę, która stworzyła Laserium, a Garmire była jej prezeską. Laserium otwarto w Griffith Observatory w Los Angeles w 1973 roku."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Scanned laser: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.scanned-laser.text.3"
msgid "In hall 2 a beam of electrons drew the picture inside a tube. This beam is light, and it can draw on anything: clouds, buildings, smoke. A few steps on, in the same hall, a picture is cut to fit a set of white plaster shapes."
msgstr "W sali 2 wiązka elektronów rysowała obraz wewnątrz lampy. Ta wiązka jest światłem i może rysować na wszystkim: na chmurach, budynkach, dymie. Kilka kroków dalej, w tej samej sali, obraz jest przycięty do zestawu białych gipsowych brył."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Projection mapping: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.women.projection-mapping.title"
msgid "A picture cut to fit"
msgstr "Obraz przycięty na miarę"

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Projection mapping: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.projection-mapping.text.1"
msgid "Find the switch marked Daylight and turn it off. By day this picture is barely visible. The projector on the tripod is an ordinary one. The work is in the picture, which is cut to fit the shapes it lands on. Each shape gets its own pattern, and no light falls on the floor."
msgstr "Znajdź przełącznik oznaczony napisem „Światło dzienne” i wyłącz go. W dzień ten obraz jest ledwo widoczny. Projektor na statywie jest zwyczajny. Cała praca tkwi w obrazie, który jest przycięty do brył, na które pada. Każda bryła dostaje własny wzór i żadne światło nie pada na podłogę."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Projection mapping: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.projection-mapping.text.2"
msgid "In 1969 the Haunted Mansion at Disneyland used this for its singing busts. The faces of singers were filmed, and the film was projected onto plaster busts of the same faces. In the same house a crystal ball holds a blank head. Leota Toombs, an artist at the Disney design workshop, gave it her face. No paper or patent carries her name here. The film on that head is of her."
msgstr "W 1969 roku Haunted Mansion w Disneylandzie wykorzystał to w swoich śpiewających popiersiach. Sfilmowano twarze śpiewaków, a film rzutowano na gipsowe popiersia z tymi samymi twarzami. W tym samym domu kryształowa kula kryje pustą głowę. Leota Toombs, artystka z pracowni projektowej Disneya, dała mu swoją twarz. Żaden artykuł ani patent nie nosi tu jej nazwiska. Film na tej głowie to ona."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Projection mapping: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.projection-mapping.text.3"
msgid "Before you go on, turn the daylight back on. The next stop is in hall 5, where the displays behave like print: they need the light of the room. Go to the electrophoretic ink, the page of an e-reader."
msgstr "Zanim pójdziesz dalej, włącz z powrotem światło dzienne. Następny przystanek jest w sali 5, gdzie wyświetlacze zachowują się jak druk: potrzebują światła pomieszczenia. Podejdź do atramentu elektroforetycznego, strony czytnika e-booków."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Electrophoretic ink: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.women.electrophoretic-ink.title"
msgid "A page that bends"
msgstr "Strona, która się wygina"

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Electrophoretic ink: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.electrophoretic-ink.text.1"
msgid "This is the page of an e-reader. It makes no light. Millions of capsules hold black and white pigment, and a voltage pulls one colour to the top. Watch the page for a moment. Every 15 seconds it resets, with a flash of black and then of white. In between, it holds the page with no power."
msgstr "To strona czytnika e-booków. Nie wytwarza światła. Miliony kapsułek zawierają czarny i biały pigment, a napięcie przyciąga jeden kolor na wierzch. Popatrz chwilę na stronę. Co 15 sekund odświeża się błyskiem czerni, a potem bieli. W międzyczasie utrzymuje stronę bez zasilania."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Electrophoretic ink: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.electrophoretic-ink.text.2"
msgid "The plate names Barrett Comiskey, J. D. Albert and Joseph Jacobson, who developed this ink at the MIT Media Lab from the middle of the 1990s. In 2001, at Bell Laboratories, John Rogers and Zhenan Bao laid it on a sheet of plastic. With a rubber stamp they printed 256 plastic transistors on the sheet, one for each dot of the picture. The page could bend. Bao is a chemist who designs plastics that carry a current."
msgstr "Tabliczka wymienia Barretta Comiskeya, J. D. Alberta i Josepha Jacobsona, którzy od połowy lat 90. rozwijali ten atrament w MIT Media Lab. W 2001 roku w Bell Laboratories John Rogers i Zhenan Bao położyli go na arkuszu plastiku. Gumową pieczątką nadrukowali na arkuszu 256 plastikowych tranzystorów, po jednym na każdy punkt obrazu. Strona mogła się zginać. Bao jest chemiczką, która projektuje tworzywa przewodzące prąd."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Electrophoretic ink: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.electrophoretic-ink.text.3"
msgid "The ink is slow, which suits a page. The next stop, in this hall, is a display of the same kind that became fast enough for video. Go to the electrowetting display."
msgstr "Atrament jest powolny, co pasuje do strony. Następny przystanek, w tej sali, to wyświetlacz tego samego rodzaju, który stał się na tyle szybki, by pokazywać wideo. Podejdź do wyświetlacza elektrozwilżającego."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Electrowetting display: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.women.electrowetting.title"
msgid "Oil and water"
msgstr "Olej i woda"

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Electrowetting display: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.electrowetting.text.1"
msgid "These are 12 cells, greatly enlarged. Each holds a drop of dyed oil under water. With no voltage, the oil spreads out and the cell shows its colour. With a voltage, the water pushes the oil into a corner. Watch one cell switch. The oil does not disappear. It gathers in the corner and stands higher."
msgstr "To 12 komórek, bardzo powiększonych. W każdej jest kropla barwionego oleju pod wodą. Bez napięcia olej się rozlewa i komórka pokazuje swój kolor. Pod napięciem woda spycha olej do kąta. Patrz, jak przełącza się jedna komórka. Olej nie znika. Zbiera się w kącie i wznosi się wyżej."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Electrowetting display: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.electrowetting.text.2"
msgid "At the first stop a voltage bent a crystal and lifted a pin. Here a voltage makes water push oil aside. Susan Hackwood and Gerardo Beni proposed this display at Bell Laboratories in 1981, in a paper and a patent the same year. Hackwood's name went further: Cambridge's Centre for Science and Policy credits her with naming the effect, electrowetting. The year on the plate, 2003, is when a laboratory in the Netherlands made it fast enough for video."
msgstr "Na pierwszym przystanku napięcie wyginało kryształ i unosiło trzpień. Tu napięcie sprawia, że woda odpycha olej. Susan Hackwood i Gerardo Beni zaproponowali ten wyświetlacz w Bell Laboratories w 1981 roku, w artykule i patencie z tego samego roku. Nazwisko Hackwood poszło dalej: Centre for Science and Policy w Cambridge przypisuje jej nazwę zjawiska, elektrozwilżanie. Rok na tabliczce, 2003, to rok, w którym laboratorium w Holandii uczyniło je dość szybkim dla wideo."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Electrowetting display: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.electrowetting.text.3"
msgid "There is one more stop in this hall. Go to the electrochromic display, a printed label that shows the minutes."
msgstr "W tej sali jest jeszcze jeden przystanek. Podejdź do wyświetlacza elektrochromowego, drukowanej etykiety, która pokazuje minuty."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Electrochromic display: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.women.electrochromic.title"
msgid "Layer by layer"
msgstr "Warstwa po warstwie"

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Electrochromic display: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.electrochromic.text.1"
msgid "This printed label shows the minutes past the hour. In this hall a voltage has moved pigment, and then oil. Here it moves atoms. It pushes charged atoms into the printed film, and the film darkens. Wait for the minute to change. The old numeral fades, and the new one darkens over several seconds. The pane of glass behind the label carries the same film."
msgstr "Ta drukowana etykieta pokazuje minuty po pełnej godzinie. W tej sali napięcie przesuwało pigment, a potem olej. Tutaj przesuwa atomy. Wpycha naładowane atomy do drukowanej powłoki, a powłoka ciemnieje. Poczekaj, aż zmieni się minuta. Stara cyfra blednie, a nowa ciemnieje przez kilka sekund. Szyba za etykietą ma taką samą powłokę."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Electrochromic display: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.electrochromic.text.2"
msgid "The plate names S. K. Deb. His work on films of tungsten oxide, begun in the 1960s, is where these displays began. At the Massachusetts Institute of Technology, Paula Hammond supervised Dean DeLongchamp, who built such films in another way: one molecular layer at a time. His thesis of 2003 found them generally better in contrast and in switching than films made in other ways. By combining materials he also made films of more than one colour. The thesis carries his name. Hers is on it as the one who supervised it."
msgstr "Tabliczka wymienia S. K. Deba. Jego prace nad powłokami z tlenku wolframu, rozpoczęte w latach 60. XX wieku, dały początek tym wyświetlaczom. W Massachusetts Institute of Technology Paula Hammond była promotorką Deana DeLongchampa, który budował takie powłoki w inny sposób: po jednej warstwie cząsteczek naraz. Jego rozprawa z 2003 roku uznała je za ogólnie lepsze pod względem kontrastu i przełączania niż powłoki wykonane innymi metodami. Łącząc materiały, uzyskał też powłoki w więcej niż jednej barwie. Praca nosi jego nazwisko. Jej nazwisko widnieje na niej jako promotorki."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Electrochromic display: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.electrochromic.text.3"
msgid "That was the last display that works like print. Next is hall 6, Mid-air. Go to the illusion transmitter, where a picture hangs in the air."
msgstr "To był ostatni wyświetlacz, który działa jak druk. Dalej jest sala 6, W powietrzu. Podejdź do przekaźnika iluzji, gdzie obraz wisi w powietrzu."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Illusion transmitter: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.women.illusion-transmitter.title"
msgid "A bulb that is not there"
msgstr "Żarówka, której nie ma"

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Illusion transmitter: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.illusion-transmitter.text.1"
msgid "Look at the two boxes. On the left, a real bulb hangs hidden under the socket, and a curved mirror stands its picture in the empty socket above. On the right there is no bulb, only the picture, sent across by a camera and a second mirror. Watch the left bulb go dark. The picture on the right follows."
msgstr "Spójrz na dwie skrzynki. Po lewej prawdziwa żarówka wisi ukryta pod oprawką, a zakrzywione lustro stawia jej obraz w pustej oprawce powyżej. Po prawej nie ma żarówki, jest tylko obraz, przesłany przez kamerę i drugie lustro. Patrz, jak lewa żarówka gaśnie. Obraz po prawej robi to samo."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Illusion transmitter: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.illusion-transmitter.text.2"
msgid "In hall 3 a question was asked at a dinner table. This one was asked at an exhibition, in 1976. Valerie Thomas saw a curved mirror make a bulb seem to glow after it had been taken out of its socket, and she asked whether the picture could be sent. When she invented the illusion transmitter, she was managing the image-processing systems for Landsat at NASA. Four years after that exhibition, the patent was granted in her name."
msgstr "W sali 3 pytanie padło przy stole w czasie kolacji. To padło na wystawie, w 1976 roku. Valerie Thomas zobaczyła, jak zakrzywione lustro sprawia, że żarówka zdaje się świecić, choć wyjęto ją z oprawki, i zapytała, czy taki obraz da się przesłać. Gdy wynalazła przekaźnik iluzji, kierowała systemami przetwarzania obrazu dla programu Landsat w NASA. Cztery lata po tej wystawie patent przyznano na jej nazwisko."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Illusion transmitter: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.illusion-transmitter.text.3"
msgid "Stay in hall 6 for the static-volume display, where the picture fills a block of space."
msgstr "Zostań w sali 6 i podejdź do wyświetlacza objętościowego statycznego, gdzie obraz wypełnia bryłę przestrzeni."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Static-volume display: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.women.static-volume.title"
msgid "Drawing inside glass"
msgstr "Rysowanie wewnątrz szkła"

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Static-volume display: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.static-volume.text.1"
msgid "Start with the stack of clear sheets. The figure in it is a knot. One sheet at a time turns milky and catches its slice of the picture. Nothing moves."
msgstr "Zacznij od stosu przezroczystych arkuszy. Figura w nim to węzeł. Arkusze po kolei stają się mleczne i każdy chwyta swój plaster obrazu. Nic się nie porusza."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Static-volume display: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.static-volume.text.2"
msgid "Now look beside the stack, at the block of glass. It glows only where two invisible beams cross, and the model draws them in red. A beam of electrons drew in hall 2, and a laser in hall 4. Here the point where two beams cross does the drawing, in three dimensions."
msgstr "Teraz spójrz obok stosu, na blok szkła. Świeci tylko tam, gdzie krzyżują się dwie niewidzialne wiązki, a model rysuje je na czerwono. W sali 2 rysowała wiązka elektronów, a w sali 4 laser. Tutaj rysuje punkt, w którym krzyżują się dwie wiązki, i to w trzech wymiarach."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Static-volume display: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.static-volume.text.3"
msgid "Elizabeth Downing and three colleagues drew coloured points of light inside glass in this way. Their paper appeared in Science in 1996 with Downing's name first. The prototype was a cube about 15 millimetres on each side, and the model shows it many times that size. The next stop is holography, in hall 7."
msgstr "Elizabeth Downing wraz z trzema współpracującymi z nią osobami rysowała w ten sposób barwne punkty światła wewnątrz szkła. Ich artykuł ukazał się w Science w 1996 roku, z nazwiskiem Downing na pierwszym miejscu. Prototyp był sześcianem o boku około 15 milimetrów, a model pokazuje go wielokrotnie powiększonym. Następny przystanek to holografia w sali 7."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Holography: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.women.holography.title"
msgid "The light itself"
msgstr "Samo światło"

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Holography: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.holography.text.1"
msgid "Look through the glass plate. A toy engine seems to stand behind it. Move to one side, and you see around the engine. It is not behind the glass. A hologram records the light itself. In hall 4 a laser drew the picture. Here a laser only lights the plate, and the plate sends out the same light waves that the engine did."
msgstr "Spójrz przez szklaną płytę. Wydaje się, że stoi za nią zabawkowa lokomotywa. Przesuń się w bok, a zajrzysz za lokomotywę. Nie ma jej za szkłem. Hologram zapisuje samo światło. W sali 4 obraz rysował laser. Tutaj laser tylko oświetla płytę, a płyta wysyła te same fale świetlne, które wysyłała lokomotywa."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Holography: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.holography.text.2"
msgid "Dennis Gabor conceived holography in 1947 and published it in 1948. Twenty years after that, Margaret Benyon, a painter, began to make holograms as art, and showed them a year later. Her record is her exhibitions. A hologram like this one is static. In 1989, at the MIT Media Lab, Mary Lou Jepsen wrote a master's thesis that sets out the design and the building of a holographic video display."
msgstr "Dennis Gabor wymyślił holografię w 1947 roku i opublikował ją w 1948. Dwadzieścia lat później malarka Margaret Benyon zaczęła tworzyć hologramy jako sztukę, a rok później je wystawiła. Jej śladem są jej wystawy. Hologram taki jak ten jest statyczny. W 1989 roku w MIT Media Lab Mary Lou Jepsen napisała pracę magisterską, która przedstawia projekt i budowę holograficznego wyświetlacza wideo."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece Holography: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.holography.text.3"
msgid "This hologram needs no glasses. The last stop, in the same hall, puts screens all round the visitor. Go to the CAVE."
msgstr "Ten hologram nie wymaga okularów. Ostatni przystanek, w tej samej sali, otacza cię ekranami ze wszystkich stron. Przejdź do CAVE."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece CAVE: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.women.cave.title"
msgid "A room drawn for one head"
msgstr "Pomieszczenie rysowane dla jednej głowy"

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece CAVE: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.cave.text.1"
msgid "Stand at the open side of the room. Three walls and the floor are screens. The figure inside wears shutter glasses, and the picture is drawn for its eyes. So from where you stand, the scene breaks at the corners. Press the Take the figure's place button, and it joins up."
msgstr "Stań przy otwartym boku pomieszczenia. Trzy ściany i podłoga są ekranami. Manekin w środku ma okulary migawkowe, a obraz jest rysowany dla jego oczu. Dlatego z miejsca, w którym stoisz, scena łamie się w narożnikach. Naciśnij przycisk „Zajmij miejsce manekina”, a scena się połączy."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece CAVE: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.cave.text.2"
msgid "The plate names three people of the Electronic Visualization Laboratory, at the University of Illinois at Chicago. Carolina Cruz-Neira is the first author of both papers that set out the room. The sources then part ways. A SIGGRAPH biography of 1997 calls the room her doctoral research. One of 2022 says she invented it."
msgstr "Opis wymienia trzy osoby z Electronic Visualization Laboratory na Uniwersytecie Illinois w Chicago. Carolina Cruz-Neira jest pierwszą autorką obu prac, które przedstawiają to pomieszczenie. Tu źródła się rozchodzą. Biografia SIGGRAPH z 1997 roku nazywa je jej badaniami doktorskimi. Biografia z 2022 roku mówi, że to ona je wynalazła."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, at the piece CAVE: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.cave.text.3"
msgid "A headset, nearby in this hall, turns its screens with the head. Here the screens stay still, and the visitor walks among them. That was the last stop of the green line."
msgstr "Zestaw nagłowny, który stoi niedaleko w tej sali, obraca ekrany razem z głową. Tutaj ekrany stoją w miejscu, a osoba w środku chodzi między nimi. To był ostatni przystanek zielonej linii."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, after the last stop: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.women.end.title"
msgid "The end of the green line"
msgstr "Koniec zielonej linii"

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, after the last stop: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.end.text.1"
msgid "That is the end of the green line. It began with pins that are read by touch. It ends with a room whose walls are screens."
msgstr "To koniec zielonej linii. Zaczęła się od trzpieni, które czyta się dotykiem. Kończy się pomieszczeniem, którego ściany są ekranami."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, after the last stop: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.end.text.2"
msgid "Seventeen women are named at these fourteen stops. Some are on patents, some lead a paper, and one is known from a news report. In all, the labels in these halls name more than a hundred people."
msgstr "Na tych czternastu przystankach wymieniono siedemnaście kobiet. Niektóre są na patentach, inne podpisują artykuł jako pierwsze, a jedną znamy z doniesienia agencji. W sumie opisy w tych salach wymieniają ponad sto osób."

#: tour-women
#. Guided tour, after the last stop: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.women.end.text.3"
msgid "The line passed more than forty other displays on the way. Leave the tour, and the halls are yours to walk. Every piece has its label, and its people are named on it. Thank you for taking the tour."
msgstr "Po drodze linia minęła ponad czterdzieści innych wyświetlaczy. Zakończ zwiedzanie, a sale są do twojej dyspozycji. Każdy eksponat ma swój opis, a w nim nazwiska jego ludzi. Dziękuję za wspólne zwiedzanie."

#: tour-black
#. Title of a guided tour.
msgctxt "tour.black.title"
msgid "Black inventors and artists"
msgstr "Czarnoskórzy wynalazcy i artyści"

#: tour-black
#. One sentence under the title of the tour, saying what it is.
msgctxt "tour.black.lead"
msgid "A guided walk through five halls. Nine displays, from a television tube to a headset, each with a Black inventor or artist on its label."
msgstr "Spacer z przewodnikiem przez pięć sal. Dziewięć wyświetlaczy, od lampy telewizyjnej po zestaw nagłowny, a w opisie każdego czarnoskóra wynalazczyni lub wynalazca, artystka lub artysta."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, before the first stop: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.black.start.title"
msgid "Before the first stop"
msgstr "Przed pierwszym przystankiem"

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, before the first stop: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.start.text.1"
msgid "This tour follows the blue line on the floor. It stops at nine displays in five halls. At each one the label names a Black inventor or a Black artist."
msgstr "To zwiedzanie prowadzi wzdłuż niebieskiej linii na podłodze. Zatrzymuje się przy dziewięciu wyświetlaczach w pięciu salach. Przy każdym z nich opis wymienia czarnoskórą osobę: wynalazcę, wynalazczynię, artystę lub artystkę."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, before the first stop: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.start.text.2"
msgid "Some of them made the display. Some made a part that it could not do without. Some put it to a new use, or made art with it. At each stop I will say which."
msgstr "Niektórzy z nich stworzyli wyświetlacz. Niektórzy wykonali część, bez której nie mógłby się obejść. Niektórzy znaleźli dla niego nowe zastosowanie albo tworzyli z nim sztukę. Na każdym przystanku powiem, o który przypadek chodzi."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, before the first stop: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.start.text.3"
msgid "The first stop is in hall 2. Go to the cathode ray tube."
msgstr "Pierwszy przystanek jest w sali 2. Podejdź do lampy kineskopowej."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Cathode ray tube: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.black.cathode-ray-tube.title"
msgid "A camera at the door"
msgstr "Kamera przy drzwiach"

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Cathode ray tube: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.cathode-ray-tube.text.1"
msgid "Look at the screen. The bright band moving down it is where one beam of electrons has just drawn its lines. The model slows it about 60 times."
msgstr "Spójrz na ekran. Jasny pas, który przesuwa się w dół, to miejsce, gdzie jedna wiązka elektronów właśnie narysowała swoje linie. Model spowalnia ją mniej więcej 60 razy."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Cathode ray tube: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.cathode-ray-tube.text.2"
msgid "The plate on the block names Ferdinand Braun, who built his cathode ray tube in Strasbourg in 1897. Two people on this label put the tube to work. Marie Van Brittan Brown was a nurse in New York, and her husband Albert was an electronics technician. In 1966 they built a security system for their home. A camera slid between four peepholes in the door, and a television monitor showed who was calling. They patented it in 1969, with both their names on the patent. Mark Dean was an engineer at IBM. His name is on three patents for the IBM personal computer. Two are for the adapters that drove its monitors, one monochrome and one colour."
msgstr "Tabliczka na postumencie wymienia Ferdinanda Brauna, który w 1897 roku zbudował w Strasburgu swoją lampę katodową. Dwie osoby z tego opisu zaprzęgły lampę do pracy. Marie Van Brittan Brown była pielęgniarką w Nowym Jorku, a jej mąż Albert technikiem elektronikiem. W 1966 roku zbudowali system zabezpieczeń dla swojego domu. Kamera przesuwała się między czterema wizjerami w drzwiach, a monitor telewizyjny pokazywał, kto przyszedł. Opatentowali go w 1969 roku, z nazwiskami obojga na patencie. Mark Dean był inżynierem w IBM. Jego nazwisko widnieje na trzech patentach komputera osobistego IBM. Dwa dotyczą kart, które sterowały jego monitorami, monochromatycznym i kolorowym."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Cathode ray tube: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.cathode-ray-tube.text.3"
msgid "The next stop is in this hall as well. There the patent is nearly ninety years older than the display. Go to the Numitron, the glass bulb with seven small filaments."
msgstr "Następny przystanek też jest w tej sali. Tam patent jest prawie dziewięćdziesiąt lat starszy od wyświetlacza. Podejdź do Numitronu, szklanej bańki z siedmioma małymi żarnikami."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Numitron: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.black.numitron.title"
msgid "The filament came first"
msgstr "Najpierw był żarnik"

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Numitron: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.numitron.text.1"
msgid "Look at the glass bulb. Inside are seven tiny lamp filaments, arranged as the seven bars that form a digit. Current through the right filaments makes them glow in the shape of a numeral."
msgstr "Spójrz na szklaną bańkę. W środku jest siedem maleńkich żarników, ułożonych jak siedem odcinków tworzących cyfrę. Prąd płynący przez odpowiednie żarniki sprawia, że świecą w kształcie cyfry."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Numitron: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.numitron.text.2"
msgid "Lewis Latimer did not make this display. It is from 1970, and he worked nearly ninety years earlier. But a display made of filaments needs filaments that last. In 1882 Latimer patented a way of making the carbon filaments of early electric lamps so that fewer broke in the furnace."
msgstr "Lewis Latimer nie zrobił tego wyświetlacza. Wyświetlacz pochodzi z 1970 roku, a Latimer pracował prawie dziewięćdziesiąt lat wcześniej. Ale wyświetlacz z żarników potrzebuje trwałych żarników. W 1882 roku Latimer opatentował sposób wytwarzania węglowych żarników do wczesnych żarówek, dzięki któremu mniej z nich pękało w piecu."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Numitron: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.numitron.text.3"
msgid "Here the filament is the light. At the next stop, also in this hall, the light comes from a coating that is struck by electrons. Go to the field emission display."
msgstr "Tutaj światłem jest żarnik. Na następnym przystanku, także w tej sali, światło pochodzi z powłoki, w którą uderzają elektrony. Podejdź do wyświetlacza z emisją polową."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Field emission display: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.black.field-emission.title"
msgid "A tube made flat"
msgstr "Spłaszczona lampa"

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Field emission display: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.field-emission.text.1"
msgid "The model shows one corner of a panel, opened and greatly enlarged. Follow the layers upward. First come the tips, then the gate with a hole over each tip. Above them is the front plate with its glowing coating. The lit dots count seconds."
msgstr "Model pokazuje jeden róg panelu, otwarty i bardzo powiększony. Prześledź warstwy od dołu do góry. Najpierw są ostrza, potem bramka z otworem nad każdym ostrzem. Nad nimi jest przednia płyta ze świecącą powłoką. Świecące punkty odliczają sekundy."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Field emission display: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.field-emission.text.2"
msgid "This display is a cathode ray tube flattened to a few millimetres, with a tiny source of electrons behind every dot. The way of making the tips was patented at Stanford Research Institute. Akintunde Akinwande was educated in Nigeria and at Stanford. He joined Honeywell in 1986 and worked there on thin-film field emitters and displays. At MIT he worked with Luis Fernando Velásquez-García on arrays of emitters, each switched by its own transistor."
msgstr "Ten wyświetlacz to lampa kineskopowa spłaszczona do kilku milimetrów, z maleńkim źródłem elektronów za każdym punktem. Sposób wytwarzania ostrzy opatentowano w Stanford Research Institute. Akintunde Akinwande kształcił się w Nigerii i na Uniwersytecie Stanforda. W 1986 roku dołączył do firmy Honeywell i pracował tam nad cienkowarstwowymi emiterami polowymi i wyświetlaczami. W MIT pracował z Luisem Fernandem Velásquezem-Garcíą nad matrycami emiterów, z których każdy ma własny tranzystor."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Field emission display: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.field-emission.text.3"
msgid "These three displays made their own light. In the next one a projector makes it, and the picture is cut to fit. Walk on to hall 4 and go to the projection mapping."
msgstr "Te trzy wyświetlacze wytwarzały własne światło. W następnym wytwarza je projektor, a obraz jest docięty na miarę. Przejdź do sali 4, do mappingu projekcyjnego."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Projection mapping: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.black.projection-mapping.title"
msgid "A head in a crystal ball"
msgstr "Głowa w kryształowej kuli"

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Projection mapping: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.projection-mapping.text.1"
msgid "Look at the white plaster shapes and the projector on its tripod. Each shape receives its own pattern, and no light falls on the floor. By day the picture is barely visible, so switch the daylight off."
msgstr "Spójrz na białe gipsowe bryły i projektor na statywie. Każda bryła dostaje własny wzór i żadne światło nie pada na podłogę. W dzień obraz jest ledwo widoczny, więc wyłącz światło dzienne."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Projection mapping: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.projection-mapping.text.2"
msgid "The year on the plate, 1969, belongs to the Haunted Mansion at Disneyland. There a filmed face is projected onto a blank head inside a crystal ball. The head is called Madame Leota. Lanny Smoot is a Disney research fellow, and his name is on more than 100 patents. He is credited with making Madame Leota float in her séance room."
msgstr "Rok na tabliczce, 1969, należy do Haunted Mansion w Disneylandzie. Tam sfilmowaną twarz rzutuje się na pustą głowę w kryształowej kuli. Ta głowa nazywa się Madame Leota. Lanny Smoot jest pracownikiem naukowym Disneya, a jego nazwisko widnieje na ponad 100 patentach. Przypisuje mu się to, że Madame Leota unosi się w powietrzu w swoim pokoju seansów."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Projection mapping: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.projection-mapping.text.3"
msgid "So far every picture needed a lamp or a flame, or made its own light. In hall 5 the pictures use the light of the room. Go to the electrochromic display."
msgstr "Dotąd każdy obraz potrzebował lampy lub płomienia albo sam wytwarzał światło. W sali 5 obrazy korzystają ze światła pomieszczenia. Podejdź do wyświetlacza elektrochromowego."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Electrochromic display: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.black.electrochromic.title"
msgid "One layer at a time"
msgstr "Po jednej warstwie"

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Electrochromic display: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.electrochromic.text.1"
msgid "Look at the printed label that shows the minutes in bars. Wait for the minute to change. The old digit fades and the new digit darkens slowly, over several seconds. The window pane behind the label is the same film on glass."
msgstr "Spójrz na drukowaną etykietę, która pokazuje minuty za pomocą odcinków. Poczekaj, aż zmieni się minuta. Stara cyfra blednie, a nowa powoli ciemnieje, przez kilka sekund. Szyba za etykietą to ta sama powłoka na szkle."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Electrochromic display: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.electrochromic.text.2"
msgid "The plate names S. K. Deb. These displays grew from his work on tungsten oxide films, begun in the 1960s. At MIT, Paula Hammond supervised Dean DeLongchamp, who built electrochromic films one molecular layer at a time. His thesis of 2003 found them generally better in contrast and in switching than films made in other ways. By combining materials he also made films of more than one colour."
msgstr "Tabliczka wymienia S. K. Deba. Te wyświetlacze wyrosły z jego prac nad powłokami z tlenku wolframu, rozpoczętych w latach 60. XX wieku. W MIT Paula Hammond była promotorką Deana DeLongchampa, który budował powłoki elektrochromowe po jednej warstwie cząsteczek naraz. Jego rozprawa z 2003 roku uznała je za ogólnie lepsze pod względem kontrastu i przełączania niż powłoki wykonane innymi metodami. Łącząc materiały, uzyskał też powłoki w więcej niż jednej barwie."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Electrochromic display: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.electrochromic.text.3"
msgid "This film keeps its colour with the power off. The next picture is not on a surface at all. Go to hall 6 and find the illusion transmitter."
msgstr "Ta powłoka zachowuje barwę bez zasilania. Następny obraz w ogóle nie leży na powierzchni. Przejdź do sali 6 i znajdź przekaźnik iluzji."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Illusion transmitter: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.black.illusion-transmitter.title"
msgid "A picture standing in the air"
msgstr "Obraz stojący w powietrzu"

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Illusion transmitter: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.illusion-transmitter.text.1"
msgid "On the left a real bulb hangs hidden under the socket, and its picture stands in the empty socket above. On the right there is no bulb at all. Watch the left bulb go dark: the picture on the right follows a moment later."
msgstr "Po lewej prawdziwa żarówka wisi ukryta pod oprawką, a jej obraz stoi w pustej oprawce powyżej. Po prawej nie ma żadnej żarówki. Patrz, jak lewa żarówka gaśnie: obraz po prawej robi to samo chwilę później."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Illusion transmitter: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.illusion-transmitter.text.2"
msgid "Here the plate names the person this tour came for. Valerie Thomas was born in Maryland in 1943. By one account she was one of only two women in her class to major in physics at Morgan State University. She joined NASA as a data analyst and invented the illusion transmitter there. The patent is in her name, and the plate gives its year, 1980."
msgstr "Tutaj tabliczka wymienia osobę, do której zmierzało to zwiedzanie. Valerie Thomas urodziła się w stanie Maryland w 1943 roku. Według jednej relacji była jedną z zaledwie dwóch kobiet na swoim roku, które studiowały fizykę jako kierunek główny na Morgan State University. Dołączyła do NASA jako analityczka danych i tam wynalazła przekaźnik iluzji. Patent jest na jej nazwisko, a tabliczka podaje jego rok, 1980."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Illusion transmitter: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.illusion-transmitter.text.3"
msgid "A curved mirror gave that picture its depth. In hall 7 depth comes from giving each eye its own picture. Go to the stereoscope."
msgstr "Zakrzywione lustro nadało temu obrazowi głębię. W sali 7 głębia bierze się z tego, że każde oko dostaje własny obraz. Podejdź do stereoskopu."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Stereoscope and 3D glasses: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.black.stereoscope.title"
msgid "Two pictures, two eyes"
msgstr "Dwa obrazy, dwoje oczu"

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Stereoscope and 3D glasses: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.stereoscope.text.1"
msgid "A hand-held viewer stands on a post, with a stereo card in its holder. Press the Look in button to put an eye to the lens: the flat card becomes a scene with depth. The red and cyan glasses in front do the same job with colour."
msgstr "Na słupku stoi ręczna przeglądarka ze stereoskopową kartą w uchwycie. Naciśnij przycisk „Zajrzyj”, aby przyłożyć oko do soczewki: płaska karta staje się sceną z głębią. Czerwono-cyjanowe okulary z przodu robią to samo za pomocą barwy."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Stereoscope and 3D glasses: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.stereoscope.text.2"
msgid "The plate names Charles Wheatstone, who published the stereoscope in London in 1838. Two people on this label came much later. Charles Harrison was an industrial designer in Chicago. In 1957 or 1958 he redesigned the View-Master, a stereoscope for the hand, in light moulded plastic. His record is the object itself: sold from 1962, it went from a photographer's accessory to a children's toy. Kenneth Dunkley is a physicist in Pennsylvania, and his record is a patent. His patent of 1989 is for viewing glasses with no lenses: two pinholes and two empty frames. The patent says that they give an ordinary flat picture the look of depth."
msgstr "Tabliczka wymienia Charlesa Wheatstone’a, który przedstawił stereoskop w publikacji w Londynie w 1838 roku. Dwie osoby z tego opisu przyszły dużo później. Charles Harrison był projektantem przemysłowym w Chicago. W 1957 lub 1958 roku na nowo zaprojektował View-Mastera, ręczny stereoskop, w lekkim formowanym plastiku. Jego śladem jest sam przedmiot: sprzedawany od 1962 roku, z akcesorium fotografa stał się zabawką dla dzieci. Kenneth Dunkley jest fizykiem w Pensylwanii, a jego śladem jest patent. Jego patent z 1989 roku dotyczy okularów do oglądania bez soczewek: dwa otworki i dwie puste oprawki. Patent mówi, że nadają one zwykłemu płaskiemu obrazowi wygląd głębi."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Stereoscope and 3D glasses: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.stereoscope.text.3"
msgid "The stereoscope needs a viewer in front of the eyes. The next stop does without one. Stay in this hall and go to the lenticular display."
msgstr "Stereoskop wymaga przeglądarki przed oczami. Następny przystanek obywa się bez niej. Zostań w tej sali i podejdź do wyświetlacza soczewkowego."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Lenticular display: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.black.lenticular.title"
msgid "Words that change as you walk"
msgstr "Słowa, które zmieniają się, gdy idziesz"

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Lenticular display: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.lenticular.text.1"
msgid "Look at the card. It shows an eye, printed in nine views. Turn the model: the eye follows you across the room and jumps from one view to the next."
msgstr "Spójrz na kartę. Pokazuje oko, wydrukowane w dziewięciu widokach. Obróć model: oko podąża za tobą przez pomieszczenie i przeskakuje z jednego widoku na następny."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Lenticular display: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.lenticular.text.2"
msgid "A sheet of tiny ribbed lenses lies over a picture made of strips, and each rib shows a different strip depending on where you stand. The plate names Walter Hess, who filed his patent in 1912. Hank Willis Thomas is an artist in New York, and here the work is the record. His lenticular prints carry text that changes as the visitor walks past. In one of them, Black Imitates White becomes White Imitates Black."
msgstr "Arkusz drobnych soczewek z żeberkami leży na obrazie złożonym z pasków, a każde żeberko pokazuje inny pasek, zależnie od tego, gdzie stoisz. Tabliczka wymienia Waltera Hessa, który złożył wniosek patentowy w 1912 roku. Hank Willis Thomas jest artystą w Nowym Jorku, a tu śladem jest samo dzieło. Jego druki lentikularne niosą tekst, który zmienia się, gdy zwiedzający przechodzi obok. W jednym z nich Black Imitates White zmienia się w White Imitates Black."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Lenticular display: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.lenticular.text.3"
msgid "One stop is left, in this hall. Go to the head-mounted display."
msgstr "Został jeden przystanek, w tej sali. Podejdź do wyświetlacza nagłownego."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Head-mounted display: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.black.head-mounted.title"
msgid "Goggles for a surgeon"
msgstr "Gogle dla chirurga"

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Head-mounted display: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.head-mounted.text.1"
msgid "The model shows a headset on a dummy head. Beside it are the parts for one eye: a lens and the small screen behind it. Press the Put it on button to see what the wearer sees."
msgstr "Model pokazuje zestaw nagłowny na głowie manekina. Obok są części dla jednego oka: soczewka i mały ekran za nią. Naciśnij przycisk „Załóż”, aby zobaczyć to, co widzi osoba, która go nosi."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Head-mounted display: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.head-mounted.text.2"
msgid "The plate names Ivan Sutherland and Bob Sproull, who built a headset that showed graphics drawn by a computer, at Harvard University in 1968. Some sources call it the first virtual reality headset, and others an early one. Samuel Achilefu was born in Nigeria. His team at Washington University in St. Louis built goggles with a screen for surgeons. A dye makes cancer cells glow on that screen. The university dates their first use in an operation to 2014."
msgstr "Tabliczka wymienia Ivana Sutherlanda i Boba Sproulla, którzy w 1968 roku na Uniwersytecie Harvarda zbudowali zestaw nagłowny pokazujący grafikę rysowaną przez komputer. Jedne źródła nazywają go pierwszym zestawem wirtualnej rzeczywistości, inne jednym z wczesnych. Samuel Achilefu urodził się w Nigerii. Jego zespół na Washington University in St. Louis zbudował dla chirurgów gogle z ekranem. Barwnik sprawia, że komórki nowotworowe świecą na tym ekranie. Uniwersytet datuje ich pierwsze użycie podczas operacji na 2014 rok."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, at the piece Head-mounted display: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.head-mounted.text.3"
msgid "That was the last stop of the blue line."
msgstr "To był ostatni przystanek niebieskiej linii."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, after the last stop: the title of this part.
msgctxt "tour.black.end.title"
msgid "The end of the blue line"
msgstr "Koniec niebieskiej linii"

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, after the last stop: what the guide says, paragraph 1 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.end.text.1"
msgid "That is the end of the blue line. It began with a camera at a front door. It ends with goggles in an operating theatre."
msgstr "To koniec niebieskiej linii. Zaczęła się od kamery przy drzwiach wejściowych. Kończy się goglami na sali operacyjnej."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, after the last stop: what the guide says, paragraph 2 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.end.text.2"
msgid "Eleven people are named at these nine stops. Each of them is on this line because a source describes that person as Black, as African American, or as born and raised in an African country. The People page gives the source for every name."
msgstr "Na tych dziewięciu przystankach wymieniono jedenaście osób. Każda z nich jest na tej linii dlatego, że źródło opisuje tę osobę jako czarnoskórą, jako afroamerykańską albo jako urodzoną i wychowaną w kraju afrykańskim. Strona Ludzie podaje źródło dla każdego nazwiska."

#: tour-black
#. Guided tour, after the last stop: what the guide says, paragraph 3 of 3. It is read aloud, so keep the sentences short and write years as figures. The parts call back to each other, so use the same words for the same thing throughout.
msgctxt "tour.black.end.text.3"
msgid "The green line on the floor is another tour, about the women in the museum. Leave this tour, and the halls are yours to walk. Thank you for taking it."
msgstr "Zielona linia na podłodze to inne zwiedzanie, o kobietach w muzeum. Zakończ to zwiedzanie, a sale są do twojej dyspozycji. Dziękuję za wspólne zwiedzanie."

#: people
#. About Kenyon Taylor, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.kenyon-taylor.about.1"
msgid "John Vardalas, in a history of Ferranti Canada published by IEEE Canada, calls him the man who first directed its electronics group. In 1954 he was the group's manager."
msgstr "John Vardalas w historii Ferranti Canada wydanej przez IEEE Canada nazywa go człowiekiem, który jako pierwszy kierował grupą elektroniczną firmy. W 1954 roku był kierownikiem tej grupy."

#: people
#. About Kenyon Taylor, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.kenyon-taylor.about.2"
msgid "The same history credits him with the flip-disc display, devised at Ferranti Canada. Its discs were black on one side and white on the other, and each flipped magnetically where two electrical pulses met."
msgstr "Ta sama historia przypisuje mu wyświetlacz z obrotowymi krążkami, wymyślony w Ferranti Canada. Jego krążki były z jednej strony czarne, a z drugiej białe, i każdy obracał się magnetycznie w miejscu, gdzie spotykały się dwa impulsy elektryczne."

#: people
#. About Kenyon Taylor, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.kenyon-taylor.about.3"
msgid "A United States patent for magnetically operated signs, granted in 1967 and assigned to Ferranti Packard Electric of Toronto, names him as Maurice Kenyon Taylor, with Donald Winrow. Both inventors lived in Ontario."
msgstr "Patent Stanów Zjednoczonych na znaki sterowane magnetycznie, udzielony w 1967 roku i scedowany na firmę Ferranti Packard Electric z Toronto, wymienia go jako Maurice'a Kenyona Taylora, razem z Donaldem Winrowem. Obaj wynalazcy mieszkali w Ontario."

#: people
#. About Ferdinand Braun, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ferdinand-braun.about.1"
msgid "Born in Fulda, he studied at Marburg and Berlin and taught physics at Karlsruhe, Tübingen and Strasbourg. In 1897 he built a cathode ray oscillograph, which Britannica calls the first oscilloscope, or Braun tube."
msgstr "Urodzony w Fuldzie, studiował w Marburgu i Berlinie, a fizyki uczył w Karlsruhe, Tybindze i Strasburgu. W 1897 roku zbudował oscylograf katodowy, który Britannica nazywa pierwszym oscyloskopem, czyli lampą Brauna."

#: people
#. About Ferdinand Braun, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ferdinand-braun.about.2"
msgid "He shared the Nobel Prize in Physics of 1909 with Guglielmo Marconi, for work on wireless telegraphy."
msgstr "Podzielił z Guglielmem Marconim Nagrodę Nobla w dziedzinie fizyki z 1909 roku za prace nad telegrafią bezprzewodową."

#: people
#. About Ferdinand Braun, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ferdinand-braun.about.3"
msgid "The Nobel Foundation says he went to New York as a witness in a patent case. Britannica says he was detained there as a German citizen after the United States entered the First World War. He died in Brooklyn."
msgstr "Fundacja Noblowska podaje, że pojechał do Nowego Jorku jako świadek w sprawie patentowej. Britannica podaje, że po przystąpieniu Stanów Zjednoczonych do pierwszej wojny światowej został tam zatrzymany jako obywatel niemiecki. Zmarł na Brooklynie."

#: people
#. About Robert H. Anderson, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.robert-h-anderson.about.1"
msgid "A physicist born in Jersey City, New Jersey, he joined Tektronix in 1959, in the research group led by Dick Ropiequet."
msgstr "Fizyk urodzony w Jersey City w stanie New Jersey, w 1959 roku dołączył do firmy Tektronix, do grupy badawczej kierowanej przez Dicka Ropiequeta."

#: people
#. About Robert H. Anderson, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.robert-h-anderson.about.2"
msgid "Before storage tubes, engineers caught a passing signal by photographing the oscilloscope screen. He set himself the task of a simple storage tube, one that holds the trace on its screen. It had no internal storage target, which earlier tubes had used."
msgstr "Zanim pojawiły się lampy pamięciowe, inżynierowie utrwalali przelotny sygnał, fotografując ekran oscyloskopu. Postawił sobie za zadanie stworzenie prostej lampy pamięciowej, która zatrzymuje ślad na ekranie. Nie miała ona wewnętrznej tarczy pamięciowej, której używały wcześniejsze lampy."

#: people
#. About Robert H. Anderson, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.robert-h-anderson.about.3"
msgid "The IEEE Annals of the History of Computing says he simplified Andrew Haeff's design into a direct viewing bistable storage tube."
msgstr "„IEEE Annals of the History of Computing” podaje, że uprościł projekt Andrew Haeffa, tworząc bistabilną lampę pamięciową z bezpośrednią obserwacją."

#: people
#. About Robert H. Anderson, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.robert-h-anderson.about.4"
msgid "The Type 564 oscilloscope of 1963 was built around his tube, and Tektronix later used such tubes in its 4000 series of computer terminals. He left Tektronix in 1969."
msgstr "Wokół jego lampy zbudowano oscyloskop Type 564 z 1963 roku, a firma Tektronix używała później takich lamp w terminalach komputerowych serii 4000. Odszedł z firmy Tektronix w 1969 roku."

#: people
#. About Donald Bitzer, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.donald-bitzer.about.1"
msgid "He took bachelor's and master's degrees in electrical engineering at the University of Illinois in 1955 and 1956, and a doctorate there in 1960."
msgstr "Na Uniwersytecie Illinois uzyskał tytuły licencjata i magistra elektrotechniki w 1955 i 1956 roku, a w 1960 roku doktorat."

#: people
#. About Donald Bitzer, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.donald-bitzer.about.2"
msgid "In 1963, needing a display for PLATO, the university's teaching network, he set the graduate student Robert Willson to explore the problem. Gene Slottow joined about a year later, and the three made the plasma display panel."
msgstr "W 1963 roku, potrzebując wyświetlacza dla PLATO, uniwersyteckiej sieci dydaktycznej, polecił doktorantowi Robertowi Willsonowi zbadać ten problem. Około rok później dołączył Gene Slottow i we trzech stworzyli wyświetlacz plazmowy."

#: people
#. About Donald Bitzer, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.donald-bitzer.about.3"
msgid "Each cell of the panel stayed lit until new information was called for. The university says this let PLATO work without costly magnetic memory."
msgstr "Każda komórka wyświetlacza świeciła, dopóki nie zażądano nowych informacji. Uniwersytet podaje, że dzięki temu system PLATO mógł działać bez kosztownej pamięci magnetycznej."

#: people
#. About Donald Bitzer, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.donald-bitzer.about.4"
msgid "The three received an Emmy Award from the National Academy of Television Arts and Sciences in 2002. He later became a Distinguished University Research Professor at North Carolina State University."
msgstr "W 2002 roku cała trójka otrzymała nagrodę Emmy od National Academy of Television Arts and Sciences. Później został profesorem z tytułem Distinguished University Research Professor na North Carolina State University."

#: people
#. About Gene Slottow, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.gene-slottow.about.1"
msgid "H. Gene Slottow received his doctorate at the University of Illinois in 1964 and became a professor there."
msgstr "H. Gene Slottow uzyskał doktorat na Uniwersytecie Illinois w 1964 roku i został tam profesorem."

#: people
#. About Gene Slottow, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.gene-slottow.about.2"
msgid "He joined Donald Bitzer and the graduate student Robert Willson about a year after Willson began work on a display for PLATO, the university's teaching network, in 1963. The three made the plasma display panel, which kept its picture without constant refreshing."
msgstr "Dołączył do Donalda Bitzera i doktoranta Roberta Willsona mniej więcej rok po tym, jak Willson rozpoczął w 1963 roku pracę nad wyświetlaczem dla PLATO, uniwersyteckiej sieci dydaktycznej. We trzech stworzyli wyświetlacz plazmowy, który utrzymywał obraz bez ciągłego odświeżania."

#: people
#. About Gene Slottow, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.gene-slottow.about.3"
msgid "He died in 1989, three years after retiring from the university's electrical and computer engineering faculty. The Emmy Award the three received in 2002 came after his death."
msgstr "Zmarł w 1989 roku, trzy lata po przejściu na emeryturę z wydziału elektrotechniki i inżynierii komputerowej uniwersytetu. Nagroda Emmy, którą cała trójka otrzymała w 2002 roku, przyszła już po jego śmierci."

#: people
#. About Robert Willson, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.robert-willson.about.1"
msgid "A graduate student of Donald Bitzer and Gene Slottow at the University of Illinois, he took his doctorate there in 1966."
msgstr "Był doktorantem Donalda Bitzera i Gene'a Slottowa na Uniwersytecie Illinois i uzyskał tam doktorat w 1966 roku."

#: people
#. About Robert Willson, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.robert-willson.about.2"
msgid "In 1963 Bitzer set him to explore a display for PLATO, the university's teaching network, that could show images laid over each other. Slottow joined the discussion of Willson's results about a year later, and the three made the plasma display panel."
msgstr "W 1963 roku Bitzer polecił mu zbadać kwestię wyświetlacza dla PLATO, uniwersyteckiej sieci dydaktycznej, który mógłby pokazywać nałożone na siebie obrazy. Około rok później Slottow włączył się do omawiania wyników Willsona i we trzech stworzyli wyświetlacz plazmowy."

#: people
#. About Robert Willson, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.robert-willson.about.3"
msgid "He shared the Emmy Award of 2002 with them, and later worked as an engineer with Analex Corporation in Alexandria, Virginia."
msgstr "Podzielił z nimi nagrodę Emmy z 2002 roku, a później pracował jako inżynier w Analex Corporation w Aleksandrii w stanie Wirginia."

#: people
#. About Nicholas Sheridon, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.nicholas-sheridon.about.1"
msgid "Nicholas Sheridon, a physicist, joined the Xerox Palo Alto Research Center in 1975. Instead of replacing paper with the computer monitor, he proposed replacing the monitor with something like paper, and soon had a crude working model."
msgstr "Nicholas Sheridon, fizyk, w 1975 roku rozpoczął pracę w Xerox Palo Alto Research Center. Zamiast zastępować papier monitorem komputerowym, zaproponował zastąpienie monitora czymś na kształt papieru i wkrótce miał prymitywny działający model."

#: people
#. About Nicholas Sheridon, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.nicholas-sheridon.about.2"
msgid "He called it Gyricon, from the Greek for rotating image. Thousands of tiny plastic spheres, each with a black half carrying a small charge, sat in a clear sheet of silicone rubber and turned when an electric field came near."
msgstr "Nazwał go Gyricon, od greckiego określenia obracającego się obrazu. Tysiące maleńkich plastikowych kulek, z których każda miała czarną połówkę z niewielkim ładunkiem, tkwiło w przezroczystej warstwie kauczuku silikonowego i obracało się, gdy zbliżało się pole elektryczne."

#: people
#. About Nicholas Sheridon, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.nicholas-sheridon.about.3"
msgid "MIT Technology Review records that the circuit boards behind his prototype were stiff, so it was more like a rigid electronic clipboard than a sheet of paper. In 1977 Xerox stopped his work on electronic paper."
msgstr "„MIT Technology Review” odnotowuje, że płytki drukowane w jego prototypie były sztywne, więc przypominał on raczej sztywną elektroniczną podkładkę z klipsem niż kartkę papieru. W 1977 roku Xerox wstrzymał jego prace nad papierem elektronicznym."

#: people
#. About Nicholas Sheridon, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.nicholas-sheridon.about.4"
msgid "Xerox returned him to electronic paper in the mid 1990s, and he refined the way the spheres were made. By 2001 he was head of research at Gyricon Media, a company Xerox had spun off."
msgstr "W połowie lat 90. Xerox przywrócił go do prac nad papierem elektronicznym, a on udoskonalił sposób wytwarzania kulek. W 2001 roku kierował badaniami w Gyricon Media, firmie wydzielonej przez Xerox."

#: people
#. About Martin Schadt, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.martin-schadt.about.1"
msgid "A physicist, he was by his own account among the first physicists hired at the research laboratories of Hoffmann-La Roche in Basel, together with Wolfgang Helfrich."
msgstr "Był fizykiem i, według własnej relacji, jednym z pierwszych fizyków zatrudnionych w laboratoriach badawczych Hoffmann-La Roche w Bazylei, razem z Wolfgangiem Helfrichem."

#: people
#. About Martin Schadt, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.martin-schadt.about.2"
msgid "He wrote that in the autumn of 1970 he and Helfrich studied twisted layers of liquid crystal there. They filed a patent that December and published in February 1971. Kent State University dates James Fergason's finding of the same effect to 1969."
msgstr "Napisał, że jesienią 1970 roku on i Helfrich badali tam skręcone warstwy ciekłego kryształu. W grudniu tego roku zgłosili patent, a w lutym 1971 roku opublikowali wyniki. Kent State University datuje odkrycie tego samego efektu przez Jamesa Fergasona na 1969 rok."

#: people
#. About Martin Schadt, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.martin-schadt.about.3"
msgid "In 1972 he built a prototype of a display that used the effect."
msgstr "W 1972 roku zbudował prototyp wyświetlacza wykorzystującego ten efekt."

#: people
#. About Wolfgang Helfrich, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.wolfgang-helfrich.about.1"
msgid "A physicist at Hoffmann-La Roche in Basel, he studied twisted layers of liquid crystal with Martin Schadt from the autumn of 1970, by Schadt's account. They filed a patent that December. Kent State University dates James Fergason's finding of the same effect to 1969."
msgstr "Jako fizyk w Hoffmann-La Roche w Bazylei od jesieni 1970 roku badał razem z Martinem Schadtem skręcone warstwy ciekłego kryształu, według relacji Schadta. W grudniu tego roku zgłosili patent. Kent State University datuje odkrycie tego samego efektu przez Jamesa Fergasona na 1969 rok."

#: people
#. About Wolfgang Helfrich, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.wolfgang-helfrich.about.2"
msgid "He left for the Freie Universität Berlin after Roche temporarily stopped its liquid crystal research."
msgstr "Przeszedł na Wolny Uniwersytet Berliński, gdy firma Roche czasowo wstrzymała badania nad ciekłymi kryształami."

#: people
#. About Fritz Fischer, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.fritz-fischer.about.1"
msgid "A physicist, he took up the new chair of technical physics at ETH Zurich, the Swiss Federal Institute of Technology, in 1933. The Neue Deutsche Biographie gives his birthplace as Oberdiessbach in the Emmental, Switzerland."
msgstr "Był fizykiem. W 1933 roku objął nową katedrę fizyki technicznej w ETH Zurich, Szwajcarskiej Federalnej Wyższej Szkole Technicznej. Neue Deutsche Biographie podaje jako miejsce jego urodzenia Oberdiessbach w Emmentalu w Szwajcarii."

#: people
#. About Fritz Fischer, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.fritz-fischer.about.2"
msgid "He applied for a patent on the Eidophor, a projector for television pictures on a large screen, in November 1939. According to Baumann, writing in 1953, Fischer built the first prototype, which first ran in 1944."
msgstr "W listopadzie 1939 roku złożył wniosek patentowy na Eidophor, projektor do wyświetlania obrazu telewizyjnego na dużym ekranie. Według Baumanna, piszącego w 1953 roku, Fischer zbudował pierwszy prototyp, który po raz pierwszy zadziałał w 1944 roku."

#: people
#. About Fritz Fischer, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.fritz-fischer.about.3"
msgid "The Neue Deutsche Biographie says others completed the work after his death and developed it further for colour television."
msgstr "Neue Deutsche Biographie podaje, że po jego śmierci inni dokończyli prace i rozwinęli je dalej z myślą o telewizji kolorowej."

#: people
#. About Joseph Ostoja-Kotkowski, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.joseph-ostoja-kotkowski.about.1"
msgid "Born in Golub, Poland, he studied under Olgierd Vetesko in Poland and at the art academy of Düsseldorf in Germany. He migrated to Melbourne in 1949 and moved to South Australia in 1954, living at Stirling in the Adelaide Hills from 1955."
msgstr "Urodzony w Golubiu w Polsce, uczył się u Olgierda Vetesko w Polsce i w akademii sztuki w Düsseldorfie w Niemczech. W 1949 roku wyemigrował do Melbourne, a w 1954 roku przeniósł się do Australii Południowej, gdzie od 1955 roku mieszkał w Stirling w Adelaide Hills."

#: people
#. About Joseph Ostoja-Kotkowski, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.joseph-ostoja-kotkowski.about.2"
msgid "The History Trust of South Australia says that work in the outback at the Leigh Creek coalfields in 1954 and 1955 set his artistic direction. On a Churchill Fellowship at Stanford University in 1967 he came across the laser."
msgstr "History Trust of South Australia podaje, że praca w australijskim interiorze, na polach węglowych Leigh Creek w 1954 i 1955 roku, wyznaczyła jego kierunek artystyczny. Podczas stypendium Churchill Fellowship na Uniwersytecie Stanforda w 1967 roku zetknął się z laserem."

#: people
#. About Joseph Ostoja-Kotkowski, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.joseph-ostoja-kotkowski.about.3"
msgid "Back in Adelaide the Weapons Research Laboratory at Salisbury helped him make a laser beam that swept in time with voices or electronic music. The History Trust says Sound and Image may have been the first use of a laser in a theatre."
msgstr "Po powrocie do Adelaide Weapons Research Laboratory w Salisbury pomogło mu stworzyć wiązkę laserową, która poruszała się w rytm głosów lub muzyki elektronicznej. History Trust podaje, że „Sound and Image” mogło być pierwszym użyciem lasera w teatrze."

#: people
#. About Joseph Ostoja-Kotkowski, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.joseph-ostoja-kotkowski.about.4"
msgid "In 1971 he designed a chromasonic tower at the Australian National University in Canberra. He later staged a laser kinetic show at Ballarat in 1984, and Synchronos '91 in Warsaw in 1991."
msgstr "W 1971 roku zaprojektował wieżę chromasoniczną na Australijskim Uniwersytecie Narodowym w Canberze. Później wystawił laserowy pokaz kinetyczny w Ballarat w 1984 roku oraz Synchronos '91 w Warszawie w 1991 roku."

#: people
#. About Joseph Plateau, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.joseph-plateau.about.1"
msgid "He was a Belgian, born in Brussels."
msgstr "Był Belgiem, urodził się w Brukseli."

#: people
#. About Joseph Plateau, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.joseph-plateau.about.2"
msgid "The Science Museum Group credits him with the first demonstration of the illusion of a moving picture, with the phenakistoscope of 1832."
msgstr "Science Museum Group przypisuje mu pierwszy pokaz złudzenia ruchomego obrazu, za pomocą fenakistiskopu z 1832 roku."

#: people
#. About Gabriel Lippmann, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.gabriel-lippmann.about.1"
msgid "He received the Nobel Prize in Physics of 1908 for a way of photographing colours by the interference of light."
msgstr "Otrzymał Nagrodę Nobla w dziedzinie fizyki z 1908 roku za metodę fotografowania barw dzięki interferencji światła."

#: people
#. About Gabriel Lippmann, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.gabriel-lippmann.about.2"
msgid "In the same year he published his idea of integral photography in the Journal de Physique."
msgstr "W tym samym roku opublikował w „Journal de Physique” swoją koncepcję fotografii integralnej."

#: people
#. About Gino Valle, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.gino-valle.about.1"
msgid "An architect and industrial designer from Udine, he graduated from the University Institute of Architecture in Venice in 1948 and held a Fulbright scholarship at the Harvard Graduate School of Design in 1951. He taught architecture in Venice from 1954 to 2001."
msgstr "Architekt i projektant przemysłowy z Udine, w 1948 roku ukończył Uniwersytecki Instytut Architektury w Wenecji, a w 1951 roku był stypendystą Fulbrighta w Harvard Graduate School of Design. Od 1954 do 2001 roku wykładał architekturę w Wenecji."

#: people
#. About Gino Valle, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.gino-valle.about.2"
msgid "For Solari he designed the Cifra 5 clock of 1954 and 1955, which won the Compasso d'Oro in 1956. Finestre sull'Arte says he enlisted John Myer, who suggested the two numbered rollers inside it."
msgstr "Dla firmy Solari zaprojektował zegar Cifra 5 z 1954 i 1955 roku, który w 1956 roku zdobył Compasso d'Oro. „Finestre sull'Arte” podaje, że pozyskał do pracy Johna Myera, który zaproponował umieszczenie w nim dwóch ponumerowanych walców."

#: people
#. About Gino Valle, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.gino-valle.about.3"
msgid "His alphanumeric boards for airports and stations won a second Compasso d'Oro in 1962. His Cifra 3 clock of 1966, with lettering by Massimo Vignelli, entered the permanent collection of the Museum of Modern Art in New York in 1968."
msgstr "Jego alfanumeryczne tablice dla lotnisk i dworców zdobyły drugie Compasso d'Oro w 1962 roku. Jego zegar Cifra 3 z 1966 roku, z liternictwem Massima Vignellego, trafił w 1968 roku do stałej kolekcji Muzeum Sztuki Nowoczesnej w Nowym Jorku."

#: people
#. About John Myer, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.john-myer.about.1"
msgid "The ADI Design Museum lists him among the four designers of the Cifra 5 clock, with Gino Valle, Nani Valle and Michele Provinciali."
msgstr "ADI Design Museum wymienia go jako jednego z czterech projektantów zegara Cifra 5. Pozostali to Gino Valle, Nani Valle i Michele Provinciali."

#: people
#. About John Myer, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.john-myer.about.2"
msgid "According to Finestre sull'Arte, more than fifty flaps for the minutes could not be fitted into the clock. Valle enlisted Myer, who suggested two numbered rollers, to make use of the combinations of their numbers."
msgstr "Według „Finestre sull'Arte” w zegarze nie dało się zmieścić ponad pięćdziesięciu klapek dla minut. Valle pozyskał do pracy Myera, który zaproponował dwa ponumerowane walce, by wykorzystać kombinacje ich liczb."

#: people
#. About Paul Nipkow, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.paul-nipkow.about.1"
msgid "Born in Lauenburg in Pomerania, he began studying natural sciences in Berlin in 1882, where Adolf Slaby and Hermann Helmholtz were among his teachers. Lack of money ended his studies."
msgstr "Urodzony w Lęborku na Pomorzu, w 1882 roku zaczął studiować nauki przyrodnicze w Berlinie, gdzie wśród jego nauczycieli byli Adolf Slaby i Hermann Helmholtz. Studia przerwał mu brak pieniędzy."

#: people
#. About Paul Nipkow, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.paul-nipkow.about.2"
msgid "His patent for an electric telescope took effect from 6 January 1884. The German Patent and Trade Mark Office says he probably never tried to build it, and that it could hardly have worked at the time."
msgstr "Jego patent na elektryczny teleskop obowiązywał od 6 stycznia 1884 roku. Niemiecki Urząd Patentów i Znaków Towarowych podaje, że prawdopodobnie nigdy nie próbował go zbudować i że w tamtych czasach urządzenie raczej nie mogłoby działać."

#: people
#. About Paul Nipkow, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.paul-nipkow.about.3"
msgid "He worked as an engineer of railway signals for Zimmermann & Buchloh near Berlin. After 1933 the Nazi government used him in its propaganda, and the patent office records that the world's first regular television station was named after him."
msgstr "Pracował jako inżynier sygnalizacji kolejowej w firmie Zimmermann & Buchloh pod Berlinem. Po 1933 roku rząd nazistowski wykorzystywał go w swojej propagandzie, a urząd patentowy odnotowuje, że jego nazwiskiem nazwano pierwszą na świecie regularną stację telewizyjną."

#: people
#. About John Logie Baird, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.john-logie-baird.about.1"
msgid "Born in Helensburgh, he studied at the Glasgow and West of Scotland Technical College. The Science Museum Group says the First World War interrupted his course and he never graduated. In 1915 he joined the Clyde Valley Electrical Power Company."
msgstr "Urodzony w Helensburgh, studiował w Glasgow and West of Scotland Technical College. Science Museum Group podaje, że pierwsza wojna światowa przerwała mu studia i nigdy ich nie ukończył. W 1915 roku rozpoczął pracę w Clyde Valley Electrical Power Company."

#: people
#. About John Logie Baird, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.john-logie-baird.about.2"
msgid "Working in Hastings, he transmitted the silhouette of a Maltese cross in 1924. In 1927 he sent a picture about 705 kilometres from London to Glasgow by telephone line, and in 1928 to New York by short-wave radio."
msgstr "Pracując w Hastings, w 1924 roku przesłał sylwetkę krzyża maltańskiego. W 1927 roku nadał obraz na odległość około 705 kilometrów, z Londynu do Glasgow, linią telefoniczną, a w 1928 roku do Nowego Jorku drogą radiową na falach krótkich."

#: people
#. About John Logie Baird, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.john-logie-baird.about.3"
msgid "The BBC tried his mechanical system against the electronic one of Marconi-EMI and had dropped his by 1937. In the 1940s he worked on colour and stereoscopic television."
msgstr "BBC porównywało jego system mechaniczny z elektronicznym systemem Marconi-EMI i do 1937 roku zrezygnowało z jego systemu. W latach 40. pracował nad telewizją kolorową i stereoskopową."

#: people
#. About Daniel Rozin, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.daniel-rozin.about.1"
msgid "He took a degree at the Bezalel Academy of Art and Design in Jerusalem and then spent about ten years as an industrial designer for a large company in Israel."
msgstr "Uzyskał dyplom Akademii Sztuki i Projektowania Bezalel w Jerozolimie, a następnie przez około dziesięć lat pracował jako projektant przemysłowy w dużej firmie w Izraelu."

#: people
#. About Daniel Rozin, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.daniel-rozin.about.2"
msgid "He came to the Interactive Telecommunications Program at New York University for a master's degree, stayed on after graduating, and teaches there as an arts professor in the Tisch School of the Arts."
msgstr "Przyjechał na Interactive Telecommunications Program na Uniwersytecie Nowojorskim, by zdobyć tytuł magistra, po studiach został tam i wykłada jako profesor sztuk w Tisch School of the Arts."

#: people
#. About Daniel Rozin, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.daniel-rozin.about.3"
msgid "In an interview for the Interactive Telecommunications Program he said Wooden Mirror took close to a year to build and one afternoon to program. A camera and hundreds of motors make its wooden pieces follow the movement of the person in front of it."
msgstr "W wywiadzie dla Interactive Telecommunications Program powiedział, że budowa „Wooden Mirror” zajęła blisko rok, a zaprogramowanie jedno popołudnie. Kamera i setki silników sprawiają, że drewniane elementy lustra podążają za ruchami osoby stojącej przed nim."

#: people
#. About Daniel Rozin, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.daniel-rozin.about.4"
msgid "His work has been shown at the Victoria and Albert Museum in London and the Israel Museum in Jerusalem. His awards include the Prix Ars Electronica and the Rothschild Prize."
msgstr "Jego prace pokazywano w Victoria and Albert Museum w Londynie i w Muzeum Izraela w Jerozolimie. Wśród jego nagród są Prix Ars Electronica i Nagroda Rothschilda."

#: people
#. About Daniel Leithinger, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.daniel-leithinger.about.1"
msgid "He took bachelor's and master's degrees at the Upper Austria University of Applied Sciences in Hagenberg in 2005 and 2007, and his doctorate at the MIT Media Lab in 2015."
msgstr "Tytuły licencjata i magistra uzyskał w Upper Austria University of Applied Sciences w Hagenbergu w 2005 i 2007 roku, a doktorat w MIT Media Lab w 2015 roku."

#: people
#. About Daniel Leithinger, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.daniel-leithinger.about.2"
msgid "The Tangible Media Group credits inFORM, a shape display that renders three-dimensional content physically, to him, Sean Follmer and Hiroshi Ishii, and marks him and Follmer as equal contributors. He wrote its paper of 2013 with Follmer, Ishii and two others."
msgstr "Tangible Media Group przypisuje inFORM, wyświetlacz kształtu, który fizycznie odtwarza trójwymiarowe treści, jemu, Seanowi Follmerowi i Hiroshiemu Ishiiemu, a jego i Follmera wskazuje jako równorzędnych współtwórców. Artykuł o inFORM z 2013 roku napisał z Follmerem, Ishiim i dwiema innymi osobami."

#: people
#. About Daniel Leithinger, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.daniel-leithinger.about.3"
msgid "From 2018 to 2023 he was an assistant professor of computer science at the University of Colorado Boulder, where he led the THING Lab at the ATLAS Institute. He then became a Design Tech Innovation Fellow at Cornell University."
msgstr "Od 2018 do 2023 roku był adiunktem informatyki na Uniwersytecie Kolorado w Boulder, gdzie kierował THING Lab w ATLAS Institute. Następnie otrzymał stanowisko Design Tech Innovation Fellow na Uniwersytecie Cornella."

#: people
#. About Daniel Leithinger, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.daniel-leithinger.about.4"
msgid "In 2015 he co-founded Lumii, now Fathom Optics, to develop 3D displays that need no glasses."
msgstr "W 2015 roku współzałożył firmę Lumii, dziś Fathom Optics, by rozwijać wyświetlacze 3D niewymagające okularów."

#: people
#. About Sean Follmer, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.sean-follmer.about.1"
msgid "He took a degree in engineering at Stanford University in 2009, then a master's in 2011 and a doctorate in 2015 at the MIT Media Lab."
msgstr "W 2009 roku uzyskał dyplom z inżynierii na Uniwersytecie Stanforda, a następnie magisterium w 2011 roku i doktorat w 2015 roku w MIT Media Lab."

#: people
#. About Sean Follmer, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.sean-follmer.about.2"
msgid "The Tangible Media Group credits inFORM, a shape display that renders three-dimensional content physically, to him, Daniel Leithinger and Hiroshi Ishii, and marks him and Leithinger as equal contributors."
msgstr "Tangible Media Group przypisuje inFORM, wyświetlacz kształtu, który fizycznie odtwarza trójwymiarowe treści, jemu, Danielowi Leithingerowi i Hiroshiemu Ishiiemu, a jego i Leithingera wskazuje jako równorzędnych współtwórców."

#: people
#. About Sean Follmer, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.sean-follmer.about.3"
msgid "He returned to Stanford, where he is an associate professor of mechanical engineering and directs the Shape Lab. His research includes haptics, shape-changing interfaces and interfaces for people who are blind or visually impaired."
msgstr "Wrócił na Uniwersytet Stanforda, gdzie jest profesorem nadzwyczajnym inżynierii mechanicznej i kieruje Shape Lab. Jego badania obejmują haptykę, interfejsy zmieniające kształt oraz interfejsy dla osób niewidomych lub słabowidzących."

#: people
#. About Hiroshi Ishii, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.hiroshi-ishii.about.1"
msgid "He took degrees in electronic and computer engineering at Hokkaido University, ending with a doctorate in 1992. From 1988 to 1994 he led a research group at NTT Human Interface Laboratories, whose team built TeamWorkStation and ClearBoard."
msgstr "Studiował inżynierię elektroniczną i komputerową na Uniwersytecie Hokkaido, kończąc doktoratem w 1992 roku. Od 1988 do 1994 roku kierował grupą badawczą w NTT Human Interface Laboratories, której zespół zbudował TeamWorkStation i ClearBoard."

#: people
#. About Hiroshi Ishii, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.hiroshi-ishii.about.2"
msgid "He joined the MIT Media Lab in October 1995 and set up the Tangible Media Group to pursue an idea he called Tangible Bits, in which people handle digital information through physical objects."
msgstr "W październiku 1995 roku dołączył do MIT Media Lab i założył Tangible Media Group, by rozwijać ideę, którą nazwał Tangible Bits: ludzie posługują się w niej informacją cyfrową za pośrednictwem fizycznych przedmiotów."

#: people
#. About Hiroshi Ishii, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.hiroshi-ishii.about.3"
msgid "In 2006 the Association for Computing Machinery's group on computer and human interaction elected him to its CHI Academy, for creating tangible user interfaces as a field. He became an associate director of the Media Lab in May 2008."
msgstr "W 2006 roku grupa Association for Computing Machinery zajmująca się interakcją człowieka z komputerem wybrała go do swojej CHI Academy za stworzenie dziedziny namacalnych interfejsów użytkownika. W maju 2008 roku został jednym z zastępców dyrektora Media Lab."

#: people
#. About Oleg Tretiakoff, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.oleg-tretiakoff.about.1"
msgid "With Andrée Tretiakoff, both of Sceaux in France, he filed a United States patent in 1975, granted in 1977, for a braille panel. Each dot was a rod that a thin piezoelectric strip pushed up or drew down as it bent."
msgstr "Razem z Andrée Tretiakoff złożył w 1975 roku w Stanach Zjednoczonych wniosek patentowy na panel brajlowski, a patent udzielono w 1977 roku. Oboje mieszkali w Sceaux we Francji. Każdy punkt był trzpieniem, który cienki pasek piezoelektryczny, wyginając się, wypychał w górę lub cofał w dół."

#: people
#. About Oleg Tretiakoff, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.oleg-tretiakoff.about.2"
msgid "The American Printing House for the Blind credits the pair with the first commercially available paperless braille machine, the Digicassette, introduced in Paris in 1976. It kept text on cassette tape and raised one line of braille at a time."
msgstr "American Printing House for the Blind przypisuje tej parze pierwsze dostępne na rynku bezpapierowe urządzenie brajlowskie, Digicassette, zaprezentowane w Paryżu w 1976 roku. Przechowywało ono tekst na kasecie magnetofonowej i unosiło po jednym wierszu brajla naraz."

#: people
#. About Oleg Tretiakoff, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.oleg-tretiakoff.about.3"
msgid "A later patent of theirs, granted in 1981, was assigned to Triformation Systems. The American Printing House says braille displays of the following decades largely refined the Tretiakoff design."
msgstr "Ich późniejszy patent, udzielony w 1981 roku, został scedowany na Triformation Systems. American Printing House podaje, że monitory brajlowskie kolejnych dziesięcioleci w dużej mierze udoskonalały konstrukcję Tretiakoffów."

#: people
#. About Oleg Tretiakoff, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.oleg-tretiakoff.about.4"
msgid "Their patent of 1981 said braille books were heavy, bulky and expensive to produce, which limited blind people's access to written information. It claims the priority of a French application of 22 August 1974, for a pocket electronic calculator for blind users."
msgstr "Ich patent z 1981 roku stwierdzał, że książki brajlowskie są ciężkie, nieporęczne i drogie w produkcji, co ograniczało osobom niewidomym dostęp do informacji pisanej. Zastrzega on pierwszeństwo francuskiego zgłoszenia z 22 sierpnia 1974 roku, dotyczącego kieszonkowego kalkulatora elektronicznego dla niewidomych użytkowników."

#: people
#. About Andrée Tretiakoff, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.andree-tretiakoff.about.1"
msgid "She and Oleg Tretiakoff, both of Sceaux in France, filed a United States patent in 1975, granted in 1977. In it, six rods per braille cell were raised and lowered by bending piezoelectric strips."
msgstr "Ona i Oleg Tretiakoff, oboje mieszkający w Sceaux we Francji, złożyli w 1975 roku w Stanach Zjednoczonych wniosek patentowy, a patent udzielono w 1977 roku. Według niego sześć trzpieni w każdej komórce brajlowskiej podnosiły i opuszczały wyginające się paski piezoelektryczne."

#: people
#. About Andrée Tretiakoff, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.andree-tretiakoff.about.2"
msgid "The American Printing House for the Blind credits the pair with the first commercially available paperless braille machine, the Digicassette, introduced in Paris in 1976. It stored text on cassette tape and raised one line of braille at a time."
msgstr "American Printing House for the Blind przypisuje tej parze pierwsze dostępne na rynku bezpapierowe urządzenie brajlowskie, Digicassette, zaprezentowane w Paryżu w 1976 roku. Zapisywało ono tekst na kasecie magnetofonowej i unosiło po jednym wierszu brajla naraz."

#: people
#. About Andrée Tretiakoff, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.andree-tretiakoff.about.3"
msgid "Their second United States patent, granted in 1981, was assigned to Triformation Systems and also covered braille data on magnetic tape. The American Printing House, which spells her name Andie, says braille displays of the following decades largely refined the Tretiakoff design."
msgstr "Ich drugi patent w Stanach Zjednoczonych, udzielony w 1981 roku, został scedowany na Triformation Systems i obejmował również zapis danych brajlowskich na taśmie magnetycznej. American Printing House, który zapisuje jej imię jako Andie, podaje, że monitory brajlowskie kolejnych dziesięcioleci w dużej mierze udoskonalały konstrukcję Tretiakoffów."

#: people
#. About Andrée Tretiakoff, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.andree-tretiakoff.about.4"
msgid "Their patent of 1981 said braille books were heavy, bulky and expensive to produce, which limited blind people's access to written information. It claims the priority of a French application of 22 August 1974, for a pocket electronic calculator for blind users."
msgstr "Ich patent z 1981 roku stwierdzał, że książki brajlowskie są ciężkie, nieporęczne i drogie w produkcji, co ograniczało osobom niewidomym dostęp do informacji pisanej. Zastrzega on pierwszeństwo francuskiego zgłoszenia z 22 sierpnia 1974 roku, dotyczącego kieszonkowego kalkulatora elektronicznego dla niewidomych użytkowników."

#: people
#. About Klaus Peter Schönherr, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.klaus-peter-schonherr.about.1"
msgid "He founded Schoenherr GmbH in 1974, according to a collector's history of the Braillotron calculator. The same history says that in 1975 he invented a patented braille element able to show and erase characters."
msgstr "W 1974 roku założył firmę Schoenherr GmbH, jak podaje historia kalkulatora Braillotron spisana przez kolekcjonera. Ta sama historia podaje, że w 1975 roku wynalazł opatentowany element brajlowski, zdolny wyświetlać i wymazywać znaki."

#: people
#. About Klaus Peter Schönherr, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.klaus-peter-schonherr.about.2"
msgid "In 1977 Computerwoche reported a braille terminal from the firm, in use at the computing centre of the University of Tübingen since December 1976. The terminal widened the braille cell to eight dots, to cover a set of 96 characters."
msgstr "W 1977 roku tygodnik „Computerwoche” informował o terminalu brajlowskim tej firmy, używanym od grudnia 1976 roku w centrum obliczeniowym Uniwersytetu w Tybindze. Terminal poszerzał komórkę brajlowską do ośmiu punktów, by objąć zestaw 96 znaków."

#: people
#. About Klaus Peter Schönherr, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.klaus-peter-schonherr.about.3"
msgid "The collector's history says he received the Louis Braille Prize in 1980 and died in an accident in 1981. The American Printing House for the Blind says his company later became Handy Tech."
msgstr "Historia spisana przez kolekcjonera podaje, że w 1980 roku otrzymał Nagrodę Louisa Braille'a, a w 1981 roku zginął w wypadku. American Printing House for the Blind podaje, że jego firma przekształciła się później w Handy Tech."

#: people
#. About James Bryce, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.james-bryce.about.1"
msgid "He joined the Computing-Tabulating-Recording Company in 1917, became its chief engineer in 1923, and in 1926 organised the IBM Patent Department. He held more than 500 patents in the United States and abroad."
msgstr "W 1917 roku rozpoczął pracę w Computing-Tabulating-Recording Company, w 1923 roku został jej głównym inżynierem, a w 1926 roku zorganizował dział patentowy IBM. Miał ponad 500 patentów w Stanach Zjednoczonych i za granicą."

#: people
#. About James Bryce, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.james-bryce.about.2"
msgid "His work included an automatic multiplying punch and the use of electron tubes for arithmetic. In 1936 the US Patent Office named him among ten living inventors at its centenary."
msgstr "Jego prace obejmowały automatyczny dziurkacz mnożący i zastosowanie lamp elektronowych do obliczeń arytmetycznych. W 1936 roku amerykański Urząd Patentowy z okazji swojego stulecia wymienił go wśród dziesięciu żyjących wynalazców."

#: people
#. About James Bryce, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.james-bryce.about.3"
msgid "The American Printing House for the Blind records a braille display begun by Bryce at IBM. It read text from perforated paper tape and raised the characters on a moving plastic belt. Arnold Grunwald later took it up at Argonne National Laboratory."
msgstr "American Printing House for the Blind odnotowuje monitor brajlowski, nad którym Bryce rozpoczął prace w IBM. Odczytywał on tekst z perforowanej taśmy papierowej i unosił znaki na ruchomym plastikowym pasie. Arnold Grunwald przejął go później w Argonne National Laboratory."

#: people
#. About Horst Hörtner, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.horst-hortner.about.1"
msgid "In 1990 he co-founded the media art group x-space in Graz. He joined Ars Electronica in 1995 as technical director to help set up the Ars Electronica Center, which opened in 1996."
msgstr "W 1990 roku był współzałożycielem grupy sztuki mediów x-space w Grazu. W 1995 roku dołączył do Ars Electronica jako dyrektor techniczny, by pomóc w utworzeniu Ars Electronica Center, otwartego w 1996 roku."

#: people
#. About Horst Hörtner, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.horst-hortner.about.2"
msgid "With Gerfried Stocker he founded the Futurelab, which he ran as managing director from 1996 to 2024 and has since served as senior director. He has also been chief technology officer of Ars Electronica since 2020."
msgstr "Wraz z Gerfriedem Stockerem założył Futurelab, którym kierował jako dyrektor zarządzający od 1996 do 2024 roku, a od tego czasu jest jego starszym dyrektorem. Od 2020 roku jest także dyrektorem ds. technologii Ars Electronica."

#: people
#. About Horst Hörtner, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.horst-hortner.about.3"
msgid "He was granted patents on drone swarm flight. Ars Electronica names him as inventor of the spaxel, or space pixel, a lit drone of its swarm, which made its debut at the Cloud of Sound event, Klangwolke, in Linz in 2012."
msgstr "Uzyskał patenty dotyczące lotu roju dronów. Ars Electronica wskazuje go jako wynalazcę spaxela, czyli piksela przestrzennego, podświetlonego drona z jej roju, który zadebiutował podczas wydarzenia Cloud of Sound, Klangwolke, w Linzu w 2012 roku."

#: people
#. About Kenjiro Takayanagi, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.kenjiro-takayanagi.about.1"
msgid "Born in what is now Hamamatsu, he trained at the teacher training school of the Tokyo Higher Technical School. In 1924 he became an assistant professor at the new Hamamatsu Higher Technical College and began his television research there."
msgstr "Urodzony na terenie dzisiejszego Hamamatsu, kształcił się w szkole przygotowującej nauczycieli przy Tokijskiej Wyższej Szkole Technicznej. W 1924 roku został adiunktem w nowej Wyższej Szkole Technicznej w Hamamatsu i rozpoczął tam badania nad telewizją."

#: people
#. About Kenjiro Takayanagi, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.kenjiro-takayanagi.about.2"
msgid "The picture he sent on 25 December 1926 was the Japanese character イ, read i. The IEEE records that in 1935 he made an Iconoscope and showed a television system that was electronic in both camera and receiver."
msgstr "Obraz, który przesłał 25 grudnia 1926 roku, przedstawiał japoński znak イ, czytany jako i. IEEE odnotowuje, że w 1935 roku zbudował ikonoskop i pokazał system telewizyjny elektroniczny zarówno po stronie kamery, jak i odbiornika."

#: people
#. About Kenjiro Takayanagi, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.kenjiro-takayanagi.about.3"
msgid "At NHK his group set up a television station in 1939. In the Second World War he worked on radar and night vision equipment. He joined the Victor Company of Japan. Hayakawa Electric, now Sharp, made and sold his team's television set in 1953."
msgstr "W NHK jego grupa uruchomiła w 1939 roku stację telewizyjną. Podczas drugiej wojny światowej pracował nad radarem i sprzętem noktowizyjnym. Rozpoczął pracę w Victor Company of Japan. Firma Hayakawa Electric, dziś Sharp, wyprodukowała i wprowadziła do sprzedaży telewizor jego zespołu w 1953 roku."

#: people
#. About Kenjiro Takayanagi, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.kenjiro-takayanagi.about.4"
msgid "The IEEE dedicated a Milestone to his work at Hamamatsu in 2009. He received the Order of Culture in 1981."
msgstr "W 2009 roku IEEE poświęcił jego pracy w Hamamatsu wyróżnienie Milestone. W 1981 roku otrzymał Order Kultury."

#: people
#. About Philo Farnsworth, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.philo-farnsworth.about.1"
msgid "Born in Beaver City, Utah, he sketched an electronic camera tube for his school science teacher, Justin Tolman, in 1922. He enrolled briefly at Brigham Young University and left for lack of money."
msgstr "Urodzony w Beaver City w stanie Utah, w 1922 roku naszkicował elektronową lampę kamerową dla swojego szkolnego nauczyciela przedmiotów przyrodniczych, Justina Tolmana. Na krótko zapisał się na Uniwersytet Brighama Younga i zrezygnował z braku pieniędzy."

#: people
#. About Philo Farnsworth, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.philo-farnsworth.about.2"
msgid "Backed by the fundraisers George Everson and Leslie Gorrell, he set up a laboratory one floor above the street at 202 Green Street, San Francisco. On 7 September 1927 it sent the image of a line drawn on a slide."
msgstr "Dzięki funduszom, które zbierali George Everson i Leslie Gorrell, urządził laboratorium na pierwszym piętrze budynku przy 202 Green Street w San Francisco. 7 września 1927 roku laboratorium przesłało obraz linii narysowanej na przezroczu."

#: people
#. About Philo Farnsworth, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.philo-farnsworth.about.3"
msgid "The Radio Corporation of America challenged his patent in 1932. The Patent Office ruled for him in 1935, and upheld its ruling in 1936. The Linda Hall Library says Tolman's copy of the 1922 sketch helped. In 1939 the company agreed to pay him royalties."
msgstr "W 1932 roku Radio Corporation of America zakwestionowała jego patent. Urząd patentowy przyznał mu rację w 1935 roku i podtrzymał tę decyzję w 1936 roku. Linda Hall Library podaje, że pomogła należąca do Tolmana kopia szkicu z 1922 roku. W 1939 roku firma zgodziła się płacić mu tantiemy."

#: people
#. About Philo Farnsworth, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.philo-farnsworth.about.4"
msgid "He bought a radio plant at Fort Wayne, Indiana, hoping to make television receivers. It was sold to International Telephone and Telegraph in 1949. He was that company's consultant until 1967 and later worked on nuclear fusion as a source of power."
msgstr "Kupił zakład radiowy w Fort Wayne w stanie Indiana, licząc na produkcję odbiorników telewizyjnych. W 1949 roku zakład sprzedano International Telephone and Telegraph. Do 1967 roku był konsultantem tej firmy, a później pracował nad fuzją jądrową jako źródłem energii."

#: people
#. About Elma Farnsworth, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.elma-farnsworth.about.1"
msgid "In Philo Farnsworth's laboratory in San Francisco she kept the logbooks. The Television Academy says she learned to use precision tools to construct the elements of the first tubes, and spot welded them."
msgstr "W laboratorium Philo Farnswortha w San Francisco prowadziła dzienniki laboratoryjne. Television Academy podaje, że nauczyła się posługiwać precyzyjnymi narzędziami, by konstruować elementy pierwszych lamp, i zgrzewała je punktowo."

#: people
#. About Elma Farnsworth, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.elma-farnsworth.about.2"
msgid "The Associated Press, citing a biography by Donald G. Godfrey, reported that Philo Farnsworth gave her equal credit in his invention. After he died in 1971 she spent decades pressing for his place in the history of television."
msgstr "Agencja Associated Press, powołując się na biografię autorstwa Donalda G. Godfreya, podała, że Philo Farnsworth przypisywał jej równy udział w swoim wynalazku. Po jego śmierci w 1971 roku przez dziesięciolecia zabiegała o jego miejsce w historii telewizji."

#: people
#. About Elma Farnsworth, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.elma-farnsworth.about.3"
msgid "The Television Academy credits her efforts in part for his entry to the National Inventors Hall of Fame. In 1990 she published Distant Vision, a book about her husband and his work."
msgstr "Television Academy uznaje, że jego przyjęcie do National Inventors Hall of Fame było po części zasługą jej starań. W 1990 roku opublikowała „Distant Vision”, książkę o mężu i jego pracy."

#: people
#. About Elma Farnsworth, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.elma-farnsworth.about.4"
msgid "In 1996 the Academy's Archive of American Television recorded a seven hour interview with her. The Academy gives her year of birth as 1907, the Associated Press as 1908. She died in Bountiful, Utah, in 2006."
msgstr "W 1996 roku należące do Akademii Archive of American Television nagrało z nią siedmiogodzinny wywiad. Akademia podaje jako rok jej urodzenia 1907, a Associated Press 1908. Zmarła w Bountiful w stanie Utah w 2006 roku."

#: people
#. About Marie Van Brittan Brown, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.marie-van-brittan-brown.about.1"
msgid "Born in Jamaica, in Queens, New York City, she worked long hours as a nurse and came home late at night. The Lemelson-MIT Program says she feared she was vulnerable in a neighbourhood with high crime, and wanted to see who was knocking."
msgstr "Urodzona w Jamaica, w dzielnicy Queens w Nowym Jorku, pracowała po wiele godzin jako pielęgniarka i późno w nocy wracała do domu. Lemelson-MIT Program podaje, że obawiała się, iż w okolicy o wysokiej przestępczości jest narażona na niebezpieczeństwo, i chciała widzieć, kto puka do drzwi."

#: people
#. About Marie Van Brittan Brown, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.marie-van-brittan-brown.about.2"
msgid "She and her husband, Albert Brown, filed a patent for their home security system as joint inventors on 1 August 1966. The Lemelson-MIT Program credits the invention to her, with his assistance."
msgstr "Ona i jej mąż, Albert Brown, zgłosili 1 sierpnia 1966 roku jako współwynalazcy patent na swój domowy system bezpieczeństwa. Lemelson-MIT Program przypisuje wynalazek jej, dokonany przy jego pomocy."

#: people
#. About Marie Van Brittan Brown, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.marie-van-brittan-brown.about.3"
msgid "Besides the camera and monitors, the system had two-way microphones for speaking to the caller, a remote control to unlock the door from a distance, and an emergency button that raised an alarm with police or security."
msgstr "Oprócz kamery i monitorów system miał dwukierunkowe mikrofony do rozmowy z osobą przy drzwiach, pilota do zdalnego otwierania zamka i przycisk alarmowy, który powiadamiał policję lub ochronę."

#: people
#. About Marie Van Brittan Brown, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.marie-van-brittan-brown.about.4"
msgid "The New York Times reported on it, and she received an award from the National Scientists Committee. The Lemelson-MIT Program counts 32 later patent applications that cite the patent."
msgstr "Pisał o nim „The New York Times”, a ona otrzymała nagrodę od National Scientists Committee. Lemelson-MIT Program wylicza 32 późniejsze zgłoszenia patentowe, które powołują się na ten patent."

#: people
#. About Albert Brown, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.albert-brown.about.1"
msgid "He and Marie Van Brittan Brown filed United States patent 3,482,037 as joint inventors on 1 August 1966. It was granted on 2 December 1969. Both were listed as living in Jamaica, in Queens, New York City."
msgstr "On i Marie Van Brittan Brown zgłosili 1 sierpnia 1966 roku jako współwynalazcy patent Stanów Zjednoczonych 3,482,037. Udzielono go 2 grudnia 1969 roku. Oboje figurowali w nim jako mieszkańcy Jamaica w dzielnicy Queens w Nowym Jorku."

#: people
#. About Albert Brown, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.albert-brown.about.2"
msgid "The patent describes a control unit with a microphone and loudspeaker, and a door fitted with a radio-controlled lock. The Lemelson-MIT Program says his wife made the invention with his assistance."
msgstr "Patent opisuje jednostkę sterującą z mikrofonem i głośnikiem oraz drzwi wyposażone w zamek sterowany radiowo. Lemelson-MIT Program podaje, że wynalazku dokonała jego żona, przy jego pomocy."

#: people
#. About Mark Dean, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.mark-dean.about.1"
msgid "He studied at the University of Tennessee on its Minority Engineering Scholarship Program, graduated in 1979 and joined IBM at Boca Raton, Florida, that year. He also took a master's degree at Florida Atlantic University and a doctorate in electrical engineering at Stanford."
msgstr "Studiował na Uniwersytecie Tennessee w ramach programu stypendialnego Minority Engineering Scholarship Program, ukończył studia w 1979 roku i w tym samym roku rozpoczął pracę w IBM w Boca Raton na Florydzie. Uzyskał też tytuł magistra na Florida Atlantic University i doktorat z elektrotechniki na Uniwersytecie Stanforda."

#: people
#. About Mark Dean, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.mark-dean.about.2"
msgid "He developed the IBM PC AT, according to the University of Tennessee Libraries. In 1997 the National Inventors Hall of Fame elected him and Dennis Moeller for the ISA bus, which IBM describes as a way of connecting printers, video cards and disk drives."
msgstr "Opracował komputer IBM PC AT, jak podają Biblioteki Uniwersytetu Tennessee. W 1997 roku National Inventors Hall of Fame przyjęła jego i Dennisa Moellera za magistralę ISA, którą IBM opisuje jako sposób podłączania drukarek, kart graficznych i napędów dysków."

#: people
#. About Mark Dean, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.mark-dean.about.3"
msgid "IBM named him a Fellow in 1995 and records him as the first Black American to hold the title. His team built an experimental processor running at a billion cycles a second, dated 1994 by the University of Tennessee Libraries and 1998 by IBM."
msgstr "IBM nadał mu tytuł Fellow w 1995 roku i odnotowuje go jako pierwszego czarnoskórego Amerykanina z tym tytułem. Jego zespół zbudował eksperymentalny procesor pracujący z szybkością miliarda cykli na sekundę, datowany przez Biblioteki Uniwersytetu Tennessee na 1994 rok, a przez IBM na 1998 rok."

#: people
#. About Mark Dean, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.mark-dean.about.4"
msgid "He became director of IBM's Almaden Research Center and then IBM's chief technology officer for the Middle East and Africa. He left IBM in 2013 to join the University of Tennessee College of Engineering as John Fisher Distinguished Professor."
msgstr "Został dyrektorem Almaden Research Center IBM, a następnie dyrektorem ds. technologii IBM na Bliski Wschód i Afrykę. W 2013 roku odszedł z IBM i przeszedł na Wydział Inżynierii Uniwersytetu Tennessee jako profesor z tytułem John Fisher Distinguished Professor."

#: people
#. About Guillermo González Camarena, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.guillermo-gonzalez-camarena.about.1"
msgid "Born in Guadalajara, he built a radio transmitter at the age of eight. He graduated in 1939 from the Escuela Superior de Ingeniería Mecánica y Eléctrica of the Instituto Politécnico Nacional in Mexico City."
msgstr "Urodzony w Guadalajarze, w wieku ośmiu lat zbudował nadajnik radiowy. W 1939 roku ukończył Escuela Superior de Ingeniería Mecánica y Eléctrica przy Instituto Politécnico Nacional w mieście Meksyk."

#: people
#. About Guillermo González Camarena, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.guillermo-gonzalez-camarena.about.2"
msgid "He called his colour method the Sistema Tricromático Secuencial de Campos, Spanish for trichromatic field sequential system. The Gaceta UNAM says he launched colour television in Mexico years before the NTSC standard was adopted there."
msgstr "Swoją metodę barwną nazwał Sistema Tricromático Secuencial de Campos, co po hiszpańsku oznacza trójchromatyczny sekwencyjny system pól. „Gaceta UNAM” podaje, że wprowadził telewizję kolorową w Meksyku na lata przed przyjęciem tam standardu NTSC."

#: people
#. About Guillermo González Camarena, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.guillermo-gonzalez-camarena.about.3"
msgid "The NTSC standard used in the United States prevailed over his, and in the 1960s he devised a simpler two colour system."
msgstr "Standard NTSC stosowany w Stanach Zjednoczonych zwyciężył nad jego systemem, a w latach 60. opracował on prostszy system dwubarwny."

#: people
#. About Guillermo González Camarena, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.guillermo-gonzalez-camarena.about.4"
msgid "The Mexico City station XHGC, Channel 5, carries his initials, G and C."
msgstr "Stacja XHGC, Kanał 5, w mieście Meksyk nosi jego inicjały, G i C."

#: people
#. About A. Frankenstein, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.a-frankenstein.about.1"
msgid "According to Histoire de la télévision, A. Frankenstein was named with W. von Jaworski on German patent 172 376, dated 20 August 1904. The patent describes selenium cells, mirrors and turning discs of red, blue and yellow glass."
msgstr "Według „Histoire de la télévision” nazwisko A. Frankenstein figuruje obok nazwiska W. von Jaworski w niemieckim patencie 172 376 z 20 sierpnia 1904 roku. Patent opisuje komórki selenowe, lustra i obracające się tarcze z czerwonego, niebieskiego i żółtego szkła."

#: people
#. About A. Frankenstein, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.a-frankenstein.about.2"
msgid "The VDE, the German association of electrical engineers, places television proposals by Jaworsky and Frankenstein, among others, in 1903. Jaworsky is its spelling of the same co-applicant's name."
msgstr "VDE, niemieckie stowarzyszenie elektrotechników, umieszcza w 1903 roku propozycje telewizji przypisywane między innymi nazwiskom Jaworsky i Frankenstein. Jaworsky to stosowana przez VDE pisownia nazwiska tej samej osoby współzgłaszającej patent."

#: people
#. About W. von Jaworski, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.w-von-jaworski.about.1"
msgid "Histoire de la télévision lists W. von Jaworski, ahead of A. Frankenstein, on German patent 172 376, dated 20 August 1904. It describes selenium cells, mirrors and turning discs of red, blue and yellow glass."
msgstr "„Histoire de la télévision” wymienia nazwisko W. von Jaworski przed nazwiskiem A. Frankenstein w niemieckim patencie 172 376 z 20 sierpnia 1904 roku. Patent opisuje komórki selenowe, lustra i obracające się tarcze z czerwonego, niebieskiego i żółtego szkła."

#: people
#. About W. von Jaworski, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.w-von-jaworski.about.2"
msgid "The VDE, the German association of electrical engineers, places television proposals by Jaworsky and Frankenstein, among others, in 1903, spelling the name with a final y. Neither source gives a first name."
msgstr "VDE, niemieckie stowarzyszenie elektrotechników, umieszcza w 1903 roku propozycje telewizji przypisywane między innymi nazwiskom Jaworsky i Frankenstein, a pierwsze z tych nazwisk zapisuje z końcowym y. Żadne z obu źródeł nie podaje imienia."

#: people
#. About Peter Goldmark, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.peter-goldmark.about.1"
msgid "Born in Budapest, he studied at the universities of Berlin and Vienna and moved to the United States in 1933. In 1936 he joined CBS as chief engineer of its television department."
msgstr "Urodzony w Budapeszcie, studiował na uniwersytetach w Berlinie i Wiedniu, a w 1933 roku przeniósł się do Stanów Zjednoczonych. W 1936 roku dołączył do CBS jako główny inżynier działu telewizyjnego."

#: people
#. About Peter Goldmark, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.peter-goldmark.about.2"
msgid "In 1940 he tested his colour system from the top of the Chrysler Building. The Federal Communications Commission approved it. It served in closed circuit work such as surgery, and sent pictures back from Apollo 15."
msgstr "W 1940 roku testował swój system barwny ze szczytu Chrysler Building. Federalna Komisja Łączności go zatwierdziła. Służył on w systemach o obiegu zamkniętym, na przykład podczas operacji chirurgicznych, i przesyłał obrazy z misji Apollo 15."

#: people
#. About Peter Goldmark, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.peter-goldmark.about.3"
msgid "The Museum of Broadcast Communications records that the CBS station in New York broadcast regularly in colour from 25 June 1951 and stopped on 19 October 1951, citing too few colour receivers. Lemelson-MIT says the system was never commercially used."
msgstr "Museum of Broadcast Communications odnotowuje, że nowojorska stacja CBS nadawała regularnie w kolorze od 25 czerwca 1951 roku i przestała 19 października 1951 roku, powołując się na zbyt małą liczbę odbiorników kolorowych. Lemelson-MIT podaje, że system nigdy nie był wykorzystywany komercyjnie."

#: people
#. About Peter Goldmark, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.peter-goldmark.about.4"
msgid "The National Inventors Hall of Fame credits him with the long playing record of 1948 and records 77 patents. Lemelson-MIT credits Goldmark and his team. He received the National Medal of Science in 1977 and entered the Hall of Fame in 2007."
msgstr "National Inventors Hall of Fame przypisuje mu płytę długogrającą z 1948 roku i odnotowuje 77 patentów. Lemelson-MIT przypisuje zasługę Goldmarkowi i jego zespołowi. W 1977 roku otrzymał National Medal of Science, a w 2007 roku został przyjęty do Hall of Fame."

#: people
#. About Andrew Haeff, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.andrew-haeff.about.1"
msgid "Born in Moscow, he qualified as an engineer at the Russian Polytechnic Institute in Harbin in 1928 and took master's and doctoral degrees at the California Institute of Technology in 1929 and 1932. He worked at the RCA research laboratories from 1934 to 1941."
msgstr "Urodzony w Moskwie, w 1928 roku uzyskał dyplom inżyniera w Rosyjskim Instytucie Politechnicznym w Harbinie, a w 1929 i 1932 roku tytuł magistra i doktorat w California Institute of Technology. Od 1934 do 1941 roku pracował w laboratoriach badawczych RCA."

#: people
#. About Andrew Haeff, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.andrew-haeff.about.2"
msgid "He then joined the Naval Research Laboratory as a consultant in electronics. He was granted a patent for the Memory Tube in August 1947, and a tube of his type was used in the Whirlwind computer at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology."
msgstr "Następnie dołączył do Naval Research Laboratory jako konsultant ds. elektroniki. W sierpniu 1947 roku uzyskał patent na Memory Tube, a lampę jego typu zastosowano w komputerze Whirlwind w Massachusetts Institute of Technology."

#: people
#. About Andrew Haeff, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.andrew-haeff.about.3"
msgid "In 1950 he moved to Hughes Aircraft, where he set up its Electron Tube Laboratory, developed the Typotron for computer output, and became vice president and director of research. The IEEE History Center records him as first to receive the Harry Diamond Memorial Award."
msgstr "W 1950 roku przeszedł do Hughes Aircraft, gdzie założył Electron Tube Laboratory, opracował Typotron do wyprowadzania danych z komputera i został wiceprezesem oraz dyrektorem ds. badań. IEEE History Center odnotowuje go jako pierwszego laureata Harry Diamond Memorial Award."

#: people
#. About Andrew Haeff, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.andrew-haeff.about.4"
msgid "IEEE Spectrum calls him Andrei Haeff. The IEEE Annals of the History of Computing says Robert H. Anderson of Tektronix later simplified his design into a direct viewing storage tube."
msgstr "„IEEE Spectrum” używa formy Andrei Haeff. „IEEE Annals of the History of Computing” podaje, że Robert H. Anderson z firmy Tektronix uprościł później jego projekt, tworząc lampę pamięciową z bezpośrednią obserwacją."

#: people
#. About David Hagelbarger, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.david-hagelbarger.about.1"
msgid "He was a researcher at Bell Telephone Laboratories. The Computer Museum in Boston, in its report for winter 1987 to 1988, recorded his gift of a prototype Nixie tube made at AT&T Bell Laboratories and called him its inventor."
msgstr "Był badaczem w Bell Telephone Laboratories. Computer Museum w Bostonie w swoim sprawozdaniu za zimę z przełomu 1987 i 1988 roku odnotowało jego dar, prototypową lampę Nixie wykonaną w AT&T Bell Laboratories, i nazwało go jej wynalazcą."

#: people
#. About David Hagelbarger, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.david-hagelbarger.about.2"
msgid "The Computer History Museum now holds it as a gift of AT&T Bell Labs. Its catalogue says the Nixie was invented at Burroughs, and a donor's note gives the design to the Haydu brothers, about 1948, who sold the patent to Burroughs in 1952."
msgstr "Computer History Museum przechowuje ją dziś jako dar AT&T Bell Labs. Jego katalog podaje, że lampę Nixie wynaleziono w firmie Burroughs, a notatka dołączona do daru przypisuje jej konstrukcję braciom Haydu, około 1948 roku, którzy w 1952 roku sprzedali patent firmie Burroughs."

#: people
#. About David Hagelbarger, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.david-hagelbarger.about.3"
msgid "A 1987 profile of Claude Shannon in Omni says Hagelbarger invented a machine that tried to guess whether a player would choose heads or tails. Shannon built a simpler version that beat it."
msgstr "Profil Claude'a Shannona opublikowany w 1987 roku w „Omni” podaje, że Hagelbarger wynalazł maszynę, która próbowała odgadnąć, czy gracz wybierze orła, czy reszkę. Shannon zbudował prostszą wersję, która ją pokonała."

#: people
#. About Tadashi Nakamura, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.tadashi-nakamura.about.1"
msgid "Born in Ise City, he set up Ise Electronics Corporation there in September 1966, to make and sell display devices. The company dates the basic structure of the display to 1966 and a single digit tube to 1967."
msgstr "Urodzony w mieście Ise, we wrześniu 1966 roku założył tam Ise Electronics Corporation, by produkować i sprzedawać urządzenia wyświetlające. Firma datuje podstawową konstrukcję wyświetlacza na 1966 rok, a lampę jednocyfrową na 1967 rok."

#: people
#. About Tadashi Nakamura, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.tadashi-nakamura.about.2"
msgid "He began delivering prototype samples to Hayakawa Electric, now Sharp, in March 1967, and the DG12B tube, made in quantity by Ise Electronics, went into Sharp's CS-16A. The patents were licensed to NEC and Futaba to meet demand."
msgstr "W marcu 1967 roku zaczął dostarczać prototypowe próbki firmie Hayakawa Electric, dziś Sharp, a lampa DG12B, produkowana seryjnie przez Ise Electronics, trafiła do modelu CS-16A firmy Sharp. Patentów udzielono w licencji firmom NEC i Futaba, by sprostać popytowi."

#: people
#. About Tadashi Nakamura, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.tadashi-nakamura.about.3"
msgid "The Society for Information Display gave him a Special Recognition Award in 1979 and the Karl Ferdinand Braun Prize in 1991, shared with Kentaro Kiyozumi."
msgstr "Society for Information Display przyznało mu Special Recognition Award w 1979 roku i Karl Ferdinand Braun Prize w 1991 roku, wspólnie z Kentaro Kiyozumi."

#: people
#. About Tadashi Nakamura, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.tadashi-nakamura.about.4"
msgid "On 4 November 2025 the Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers named the display one of its Milestones in engineering history, with a plaque at the company's main building in Taiki, Mie Prefecture. Its citation says he invented the display in 1967."
msgstr "4 listopada 2025 roku Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers uznał ten wyświetlacz za jeden ze swoich kamieni milowych w historii inżynierii (Milestones), umieszczając tablicę w głównym budynku firmy w Taiki w prefekturze Mie. Uzasadnienie wyróżnienia podaje, że wynalazł ten wyświetlacz w 1967 roku."

#: people
#. About Tadashi Sasaki, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.tadashi-sasaki.about.1"
msgid "Born in Shimane Prefecture, he graduated in electrical engineering from Kyoto Imperial University in 1938. At Kawanishi Machine Works he researched and produced vacuum tubes, and he worked on radar during the Second World War."
msgstr "Urodzony w prefekturze Shimane, w 1938 roku ukończył elektrotechnikę na Cesarskim Uniwersytecie w Kioto. W Kawanishi Machine Works prowadził badania nad lampami próżniowymi i je produkował, a podczas drugiej wojny światowej pracował nad radarem."

#: people
#. About Tadashi Sasaki, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.tadashi-sasaki.about.2"
msgid "He moved to Hayakawa Electric, now Sharp, in 1964 at the request of its management. The Semiconductor History Museum of Japan says he took the lead in its calculator development."
msgstr "W 1964 roku przeszedł do firmy Hayakawa Electric, dziś Sharp, na prośbę jej kierownictwa. Semiconductor History Museum of Japan podaje, że przewodził tam pracom nad kalkulatorami."

#: people
#. About Tadashi Sasaki, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.tadashi-sasaki.about.3"
msgid "With North American Rockwell the company put the QT-8D microCompet, built on large-scale integrated circuits, on the market in 1969. He then worked on calculators that combined CMOS logic chips with liquid crystal displays, which reached mass production in 1973."
msgstr "Wspólnie z North American Rockwell firma wprowadziła w 1969 roku na rynek QT-8D microCompet, zbudowany na układach scalonych wielkiej skali integracji. Następnie pracował nad kalkulatorami łączącymi układy logiczne CMOS z wyświetlaczami ciekłokrystalicznymi, które weszły do produkcji masowej w 1973 roku."

#: people
#. About Tadashi Sasaki, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.tadashi-sasaki.about.4"
msgid "He became senior managing director and executive vice president of the company, and later served it as an adviser. In 1994 he founded the International Center for Materials Research. The Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers made him an honorary member in 2003."
msgstr "Został starszym dyrektorem zarządzającym i wiceprezesem wykonawczym firmy, a później był jej doradcą. W 1994 roku założył International Center for Materials Research. W 2003 roku Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers nadał mu członkostwo honorowe."

#: people
#. About Lewis Latimer, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.lewis-latimer.about.1"
msgid "Born in Chelsea, Massachusetts, to parents who had escaped enslavement in Virginia, he left school at about nine, by the account of the United States Patent and Trademark Office. He served in the United States Navy during the American Civil War."
msgstr "Urodził się w Chelsea w stanie Massachusetts jako syn rodziców, którzy uciekli z niewoli w Wirginii. Według relacji Urzędu Patentów i Znaków Towarowych Stanów Zjednoczonych opuścił szkołę w wieku około dziewięciu lat. Podczas wojny secesyjnej służył w Marynarce Wojennej Stanów Zjednoczonych."

#: people
#. About Lewis Latimer, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.lewis-latimer.about.2"
msgid "At a Boston patent law firm he taught himself drafting, and the partners made him their draftsman at $5 less than his predecessor. The National Inventors Hall of Fame says he drew the plans for Alexander Graham Bell's first telephone patent application, of 1876."
msgstr "W bostońskiej kancelarii prawa patentowego sam nauczył się rysunku technicznego, a wspólnicy zatrudnili go jako kreślarza za 5 dolarów mniej, niż płacili osobie zajmującej to stanowisko przed nim. National Inventors Hall of Fame podaje, że wykonał rysunki do pierwszego wniosku patentowego Alexandra Grahama Bella na telefon, z 1876 roku."

#: people
#. About Lewis Latimer, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.lewis-latimer.about.3"
msgid "In 1880 he became assistant manager and mechanical draftsman to Hiram Maxim, and oversaw the installation of lighting plants in the United States, Canada and England. The patent office says Maxim took credit for Latimer's filament work, and many workers resented a Black supervisor."
msgstr "W 1880 roku został zastępcą kierownika i kreślarzem technicznym u Hirama Maxima oraz nadzorował instalację elektrowni oświetleniowych w Stanach Zjednoczonych, Kanadzie i Anglii. Urząd patentowy podaje, że Maxim przypisał sobie zasługi za prace Latimera nad żarnikiem, a wielu pracowników nie chciało zaakceptować czarnoskórego przełożonego."

#: people
#. About Lewis Latimer, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.lewis-latimer.about.4"
msgid "He then worked for Thomas Edison as a patent investigator and expert witness. He patented a railroad car toilet with Charles W. Brown in 1874 and a cooling and disinfecting apparatus in 1886, and taught drawing and English to immigrants in New York."
msgstr "Następnie pracował dla Thomasa Edisona jako specjalista od badań patentowych i biegły sądowy. Wraz z Charlesem W. Brownem opatentował w 1874 roku toaletę do wagonów kolejowych, a w 1886 roku urządzenie chłodząco-dezynfekujące. W Nowym Jorku uczył imigrantów rysunku i angielskiego."

#: people
#. About Tsutae Shinoda, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.tsutae-shinoda.about.1"
msgid "He entered the engineering faculty of Hiroshima University in 1968, where his graduation research on protective layers for plasma panels was supervised by Heiju Uchiike. He joined Fujitsu Laboratories in 1973 and worked on AC plasma panels."
msgstr "W 1968 roku rozpoczął studia na wydziale inżynierii Uniwersytetu Hiroszimy, gdzie pod kierunkiem Heiju Uchiike przygotował pracę dyplomową o warstwach ochronnych do paneli plazmowych. W 1973 roku dołączył do Fujitsu Laboratories i pracował nad zmiennoprądowymi panelami plazmowymi."

#: people
#. About Tsutae Shinoda, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.tsutae-shinoda.about.2"
msgid "After colour trials begun in 1979, he separated the electrodes that chose a cell from those that lit it, in 1982. In 1988 he put the phosphor layer behind the discharge. In 1990 he devised ribs in stripes on one of the two plates."
msgstr "Po próbach z kolorem rozpoczętych w 1979 roku, w 1982 roku oddzielił elektrody wybierające komórkę od tych, które ją zapalały. W 1988 roku umieścił warstwę luminoforu za wyładowaniem. W 1990 roku opracował żebra w układzie pasów na jednej z dwóch płyt."

#: people
#. About Tsutae Shinoda, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.tsutae-shinoda.about.3"
msgid "The 21-inch model used his stripe rib structure, which eased the way to larger, sharper panels. The Society for Information Display gave him its Karl Ferdinand Braun Award in 2003 for the 21-inch and 42-inch colour panels."
msgstr "Model 21-calowy wykorzystywał jego pasową strukturę żeber, która ułatwiła drogę do większych i ostrzejszych paneli. Society for Information Display przyznało mu w 2003 roku Karl Ferdinand Braun Award za kolorowe panele 21-calowe i 42-calowe."

#: people
#. About Tsutae Shinoda, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.tsutae-shinoda.about.4"
msgid "The Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers made him an honorary member in 2007, and recognised the colour plasma display as one of its Milestones in engineering history in May 2025."
msgstr "W 2007 roku Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers nadał mu członkostwo honorowe, a w maju 2025 roku uznał kolorowy wyświetlacz plazmowy za jeden ze swoich kamieni milowych w historii inżynierii (Milestones)."

#: people
#. About Charles Spindt, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.charles-spindt.about.1"
msgid "Born in San Jose, California, he left architecture studies at Berkeley for the United States Air Force and flew as an all-weather fighter interceptor pilot. He then took a degree in electrical engineering at San Jose State."
msgstr "Urodzony w San Jose w Kalifornii, porzucił studia architektoniczne w Berkeley dla Sił Powietrznych Stanów Zjednoczonych i latał jako pilot myśliwca przechwytującego do działań w każdych warunkach pogodowych. Następnie uzyskał dyplom z elektrotechniki w San Jose State."

#: people
#. About Charles Spindt, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.charles-spindt.about.2"
msgid "He joined Stanford Research Institute, now SRI International, in 1959, hired by Kenneth Shoulders. The International Vacuum Nanoelectronics Conference says he worked out in 1966 how to make the cathode named after him, an array of microscopic tips emitting electrons at under 100 volts."
msgstr "W 1959 roku rozpoczął pracę w Stanford Research Institute, dziś SRI International, zatrudniony przez Kennetha Shouldersa. International Vacuum Nanoelectronics Conference podaje, że w 1966 roku opracował sposób wytwarzania katody nazwanej jego nazwiskiem, matrycy mikroskopijnych ostrzy emitujących elektrony przy napięciu poniżej 100 woltów."

#: people
#. About Charles Spindt, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.charles-spindt.about.3"
msgid "He published it in the Journal of Applied Physics in 1968. SRI's own history dates the cathode to 1973. He, Shoulders and Louis Heynick were named on patents for its structures, granted in 1973, and for methods of making them, granted in 1974."
msgstr "Opublikował jej opis w „Journal of Applied Physics” w 1968 roku. Własna historia SRI datuje katodę na 1973 rok. On, Shoulders i Louis Heynick zostali wymienieni w patentach na jej struktury, udzielonych w 1973 roku, i na metody ich wytwarzania, udzielonych w 1974 roku."

#: people
#. About Charles Spindt, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.charles-spindt.about.4"
msgid "He co-founded the vacuum microelectronics conference of the Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers in 1988 and won the Jan Rajchman Prize of the Society for Information Display in 1996. He retired from SRI in 2002. The conference reported his death at 92."
msgstr "W 1988 roku współzałożył konferencję Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers poświęconą mikroelektronice próżniowej, a w 1996 roku zdobył Jan Rajchman Prize przyznawaną przez Society for Information Display. W 2002 roku przeszedł na emeryturę z SRI. Konferencja podała, że zmarł w wieku 92 lat."

#: people
#. About Kenneth Shoulders, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.kenneth-shoulders.about.1"
msgid "Born in Texas, he was on the research staff of the Massachusetts Institute of Technology from 1955 to 1958. There he studied microfabrication for field emission amplifiers and magnetic film memories, often working with Dudley A. Buck."
msgstr "Urodzony w Teksasie, od 1955 do 1958 roku należał do personelu badawczego Massachusetts Institute of Technology. Badał tam mikrowytwarzanie wzmacniaczy z emisją polową i pamięci z warstwami magnetycznymi, często pracując z Dudleyem A. Buckiem."

#: people
#. About Kenneth Shoulders, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.kenneth-shoulders.about.2"
msgid "Stanford Research Institute hired him in 1958 as a senior research engineer. He worked on very small devices, field emission elements among them, and built the vacuum systems for evaporation and multi beam exposure used to develop the Spindt cathode array."
msgstr "W 1958 roku Stanford Research Institute zatrudnił go jako starszego inżyniera badawczego. Pracował nad bardzo małymi urządzeniami, w tym elementami z emisją polową, i zbudował systemy próżniowe do naparowywania i naświetlania wieloma wiązkami, wykorzystane do opracowania matrycy katod Spindta."

#: people
#. About Kenneth Shoulders, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.kenneth-shoulders.about.3"
msgid "With Charles Spindt and Louis Heynick he was named on United States patents for field emission cathode structures, granted in 1973, and for methods of producing them, granted in 1974."
msgstr "Wraz z Charlesem Spindtem i Louisem Heynickiem został wymieniony w patentach Stanów Zjednoczonych na struktury katod z emisją polową, udzielonych w 1973 roku, i na metody ich wytwarzania, udzielonych w 1974 roku."

#: people
#. About Kenneth Shoulders, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.kenneth-shoulders.about.4"
msgid "He hired Charles Spindt at the institute in 1959. After leaving it he studied charge clusters at a private laboratory in Bodega, California. His papers are held by the Science History Institute in Philadelphia."
msgstr "W 1959 roku zatrudnił w instytucie Charlesa Spindta. Po odejściu z instytutu badał klastry ładunków w prywatnym laboratorium w Bodega w Kalifornii. Jego dokumenty przechowuje Science History Institute w Filadelfii."

#: people
#. About Louis Heynick, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.louis-heynick.about.1"
msgid "Louis N. Heynick was named with Charles Spindt and Kenneth Shoulders on the United States patent for field emission cathode structures with a cellular array of emission sites. It was filed in February 1970 and issued in August 1973, assigned to Stanford Research Institute."
msgstr "Louis N. Heynick został wymieniony razem z Charlesem Spindtem i Kennethem Shouldersem w patencie Stanów Zjednoczonych na struktury katod z emisją polową z komórkową matrycą punktów emisji. Wniosek złożono w lutym 1970 roku, a patent wydano w sierpniu 1973 roku i scedowano na Stanford Research Institute."

#: people
#. About Louis Heynick, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.louis-heynick.about.2"
msgid "The same three were named on a second patent, granted in 1974, for methods of producing such structures."
msgstr "Ci sami trzej wynalazcy zostali wymienieni w drugim patencie, udzielonym w 1974 roku, na metody wytwarzania takich struktur."

#: people
#. About Louis Heynick, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.louis-heynick.about.3"
msgid "In March 1983, with Peter Polson, he wrote a review of the biological effects of radiofrequency radiation for the United States Air Force School of Aerospace Medicine, as a project of SRI International, the later name of Stanford Research Institute."
msgstr "W marcu 1983 roku napisał wspólnie z Peterem Polsonem przegląd biologicznych skutków promieniowania o częstotliwości radiowej dla United States Air Force School of Aerospace Medicine, w ramach projektu SRI International, jak później nazywał się Stanford Research Institute."

#: people
#. About Akintunde Akinwande, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.akintunde-akinwande.about.1"
msgid "He took a bachelor's degree in electrical and electronic engineering at the University of Ife, Nigeria, in 1978, and a master's in 1981 and a doctorate in 1986 in electrical engineering at Stanford University."
msgstr "W 1978 roku uzyskał licencjat z elektrotechniki i elektroniki na Uniwersytecie Ife w Nigerii, a w 1981 roku magisterium i w 1986 roku doktorat z elektrotechniki na Uniwersytecie Stanforda."

#: people
#. About Akintunde Akinwande, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.akintunde-akinwande.about.2"
msgid "At Honeywell he began with research on complementary field effect transistors in gallium arsenide. He then moved to its silicon microstructures group, where he worked on pressure sensors, accelerometers, and thin-film field emission and display devices."
msgstr "W firmie Honeywell zaczynał od badań nad komplementarnymi tranzystorami polowymi z arsenku galu. Następnie przeszedł do jej grupy mikrostruktur krzemowych, gdzie pracował nad czujnikami ciśnienia, akcelerometrami oraz cienkowarstwowymi urządzeniami z emisją polową i urządzeniami wyświetlającymi."

#: people
#. About Akintunde Akinwande, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.akintunde-akinwande.about.3"
msgid "He moved to the Microsystems Technology Laboratories at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology in January 1995. There his research has covered vacuum microelectronics, flat panel displays, large area electronics, field emission and field ionisation devices, mass spectrometry and electric propulsion."
msgstr "W styczniu 1995 roku przeszedł do Microsystems Technology Laboratories w Massachusetts Institute of Technology. Jego badania obejmują tam mikroelektronikę próżniową, wyświetlacze płaskie, elektronikę wielkopowierzchniową, urządzenia z emisją polową i jonizacją polową, spektrometrię mas oraz napęd elektryczny."

#: people
#. About Akintunde Akinwande, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.akintunde-akinwande.about.4"
msgid "He received a National Science Foundation CAREER award in 1996. At MIT he is the Thomas and Gerd Perkins Professor of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science. He directs Empowering the Teachers, a teaching fellowship for young Nigerian faculty in science and engineering."
msgstr "W 1996 roku otrzymał nagrodę CAREER od National Science Foundation. W MIT jest profesorem elektrotechniki i informatyki na stanowisku Thomas and Gerd Perkins Professor. Kieruje Empowering the Teachers, programem stypendiów dydaktycznych dla młodej nigeryjskiej kadry akademickiej w dziedzinie nauk ścisłych i inżynierii."

#: people
#. About Howard Borden, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.howard-borden.about.1"
msgid "Howard C. Borden began work as a mechanical engineer in 1939. He studied mechanical engineering at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology and electronics at the United States Navy Radio Materiel School, and took a BA in economics at Stanford University in 1961."
msgstr "Howard C. Borden rozpoczął pracę jako inżynier mechanik w 1939 roku. Studiował inżynierię mechaniczną w Massachusetts Institute of Technology i elektronikę w United States Navy Radio Materiel School, a w 1961 roku uzyskał licencjat z ekonomii na Uniwersytecie Stanforda."

#: people
#. About Howard Borden, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.howard-borden.about.2"
msgid "After Navy service and more engineering work he bought an appliance store, added television to its trade and saw it grow. He joined Hewlett-Packard in 1966. By 1969 he had spent 11 years in electro optical and mechanical research and development."
msgstr "Po służbie w marynarce wojennej i dalszej pracy inżynierskiej kupił sklep z artykułami gospodarstwa domowego, rozszerzył jego ofertę o telewizory i patrzył, jak się rozwija. W 1966 roku dołączył do firmy Hewlett-Packard. Do 1969 roku przepracował 11 lat w badaniach i rozwoju w dziedzinie elektrooptyki i mechaniki."

#: people
#. About Howard Borden, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.howard-borden.about.3"
msgid "In February 1969 he and Gerald Pighini wrote the Hewlett-Packard Journal article on the company's 5082-7000 solid-state display. Both were managers of solid-state displays at HP Associates, whose group made the light emitting diodes and tested and assembled the displays."
msgstr "W lutym 1969 roku on i Gerald Pighini napisali artykuł w „Hewlett-Packard Journal” o półprzewodnikowym wyświetlaczu 5082-7000 firmy. Obaj kierowali działem wyświetlaczy półprzewodnikowych w HP Associates, której zespół produkował diody elektroluminescencyjne oraz testował i montował wyświetlacze."

#: people
#. About Howard Borden, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.howard-borden.about.4"
msgid "The article credits the development work to John Atalla's solid-state laboratory at Hewlett-Packard Laboratories."
msgstr "Artykuł przypisuje prace rozwojowe laboratorium półprzewodnikowemu Johna Atalli w Hewlett-Packard Laboratories."

#: people
#. About Gerald Pighini, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.gerald-pighini.about.1"
msgid "Gerald P. Pighini took a bachelor's degree in metallurgical engineering at the Brooklyn Polytechnic Institute in 1955 and worked in solid-state electronics from then on. Before Hewlett-Packard he was chief manufacturing engineer for a maker of semiconductor devices."
msgstr "Gerald P. Pighini uzyskał licencjat z inżynierii metalurgicznej w Brooklyn Polytechnic Institute w 1955 roku i od tego czasu pracował w elektronice półprzewodnikowej. Przed przejściem do Hewlett-Packard był głównym inżynierem produkcji u producenta przyrządów półprzewodnikowych."

#: people
#. About Gerald Pighini, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.gerald-pighini.about.2"
msgid "He joined Hewlett-Packard in 1965 as chief engineer of Hewlett-Packard Associates and became its production manager for semiconductors. He then managed solid-state displays, and co-wrote a paper on growing large wafers of gallium arsenide phosphide for making LEDs."
msgstr "Do Hewlett-Packard dołączył w 1965 roku jako główny inżynier Hewlett-Packard Associates i został tam kierownikiem produkcji półprzewodników. Następnie kierował działem wyświetlaczy półprzewodnikowych i był współautorem artykułu o hodowli dużych płytek z fosforoarsenku galu do produkcji diod LED."

#: people
#. About Gerald Pighini, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.gerald-pighini.about.3"
msgid "With Howard Borden he wrote the article in the Hewlett-Packard Journal of February 1969 that introduced the company's Model 5082-7000 numeric indicator, built from gallium arsenide phosphide LEDs and an integrated circuit. The article credits the development work to colleagues."
msgstr "Wraz z Howardem Bordenem napisał artykuł w „Hewlett-Packard Journal” z lutego 1969 roku, który przedstawiał wskaźnik numeryczny firmy Model 5082-7000, zbudowany z diod LED z fosforoarsenku galu i układu scalonego. Artykuł przypisuje prace rozwojowe współpracownikom."

#: people
#. About Isamu Akasaki, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.isamu-akasaki.about.1"
msgid "He graduated from Kyoto University in 1952 and joined the research staff of Kobe Kogyo Corporation. From 1959 he taught in the electronics department of Nagoya University, which awarded him a doctorate in engineering in 1964."
msgstr "W 1952 roku ukończył Uniwersytet w Kioto i wstąpił do zespołu badawczego Kobe Kogyo Corporation. Od 1959 roku wykładał na wydziale elektroniki Uniwersytetu Nagoya, który w 1964 roku nadał mu stopień doktora nauk technicznych."

#: people
#. About Isamu Akasaki, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.isamu-akasaki.about.2"
msgid "From 1964 he headed a fundamental research laboratory at Matsushita Research Institute Tokyo, and later its semiconductor department. He returned to Nagoya University as professor of electronics in 1981, and from 1992 was also a professor at Meijo University."
msgstr "Od 1964 roku kierował laboratorium badań podstawowych w Matsushita Research Institute Tokyo, a później jego działem półprzewodników. W 1981 roku wrócił na Uniwersytet Nagoya jako profesor elektroniki, a od 1992 roku był także profesorem na Uniwersytecie Meijo."

#: people
#. About Isamu Akasaki, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.isamu-akasaki.about.3"
msgid "At Nagoya in the 1980s he and Hiroshi Amano grew thin films of gallium nitride crystal of high quality by metal organic vapour phase epitaxy. From 1987 to 1990 he led a project to develop gallium nitride blue LEDs."
msgstr "W latach 80. w Nagoi on i Hiroshi Amano wyhodowali wysokiej jakości cienkie warstwy kryształu azotku galu metodą epitaksji z fazy gazowej ze związków metaloorganicznych. Od 1987 do 1990 roku kierował projektem opracowania niebieskich diod LED z azotku galu."

#: people
#. About Hiroshi Amano, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.hiroshi-amano.about.1"
msgid "Born in Hamamatsu, he studied electrical engineering at Nagoya University and joined the nitride semiconductor group of Isamu Akasaki as an undergraduate in 1982. He took his degrees there in 1983, 1985 and 1989."
msgstr "Urodzony w Hamamatsu, studiował elektrotechnikę na Uniwersytecie Nagoya i w 1982 roku, jako student pierwszego stopnia, dołączył do grupy półprzewodników azotkowych Isamu Akasakiego. Stopnie naukowe uzyskał tam w 1983, 1985 i 1989 roku."

#: people
#. About Hiroshi Amano, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.hiroshi-amano.about.2"
msgid "In 1985, in Akasaki's group, he grew smooth gallium nitride crystal on sapphire over a low temperature buffer layer. There in 1989 he made a gallium nitride LED with a p-n junction, which the Lindau Nobel Laureate Meetings records as the first."
msgstr "W 1985 roku w grupie Akasakiego wyhodował gładki kryształ azotku galu na szafirze, na niskotemperaturowej warstwie buforowej. Tam w 1989 roku wykonał diodę LED z azotku galu ze złączem p-n, którą Lindau Nobel Laureate Meetings odnotowują jako pierwszą."

#: people
#. About Hiroshi Amano, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.hiroshi-amano.about.3"
msgid "He was a research associate at Nagoya University from 1988 and became a professor at Meijo University in 2002. He returned to Nagoya University in 2010, and in 2015 became director of its Center for Integrated Research of Future Electronics."
msgstr "Od 1988 roku był asystentem naukowym na Uniwersytecie Nagoya, a w 2002 roku został profesorem na Uniwersytecie Meijo. W 2010 roku wrócił na Uniwersytet Nagoya, a w 2015 roku został dyrektorem jego Center for Integrated Research of Future Electronics."

#: people
#. About Shuji Nakamura, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.shuji-nakamura.about.1"
msgid "Born in Ehime, he studied electrical engineering at the University of Tokushima, taking degrees in 1977 and 1979 and a doctorate in 1994. He joined Nichia Chemical Industries in 1979 and spent 1988 at the University of Florida as a visiting research associate."
msgstr "Urodzony w Ehime, studiował elektrotechnikę na Uniwersytecie Tokushima, uzyskując stopnie w 1977 i 1979 roku oraz doktorat w 1994 roku. W 1979 roku rozpoczął pracę w Nichia Chemical Industries, a rok 1988 spędził na Uniwersytecie Florydy jako wizytujący pracownik naukowy."

#: people
#. About Shuji Nakamura, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.shuji-nakamura.about.2"
msgid "In 1989 he began work on blue LEDs made of gallium nitride and related nitrides. In 1990 he built a system for growing gallium nitride, called Two-Flow MOCVD, and in 1991 he made p-type gallium nitride films by heat treatment."
msgstr "W 1989 roku zaczął prace nad niebieskimi diodami LED z azotku galu i pokrewnych azotków. W 1990 roku zbudował system do hodowli azotku galu, nazwany Two-Flow MOCVD, a w 1991 roku wytworzył warstwy azotku galu typu p za pomocą obróbki cieplnej."

#: people
#. About Shuji Nakamura, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.shuji-nakamura.about.3"
msgid "Nichia began selling white LEDs based on his blue LEDs in 1996, and violet laser diodes for Blu-ray discs in 1999. From 2000 he was a professor of materials and of electrical and computer engineering at the University of California, Santa Barbara."
msgstr "W 1996 roku Nichia zaczęła sprzedawać białe diody LED oparte na jego niebieskich diodach, a w 1999 roku fioletowe diody laserowe do płyt Blu-ray. Od 2000 roku był profesorem inżynierii materiałowej oraz elektrotechniki i inżynierii komputerowej na Uniwersytecie Kalifornijskim w Santa Barbara."

#: people
#. About Ching Wan Tang, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ching-wan-tang.about.1"
msgid "He took a science degree at the University of British Columbia in 1970 and a doctorate in chemistry at Cornell University in 1975."
msgstr "W 1970 roku uzyskał dyplom z nauk ścisłych na Uniwersytecie Kolumbii Brytyjskiej, a w 1975 roku doktorat z chemii na Uniwersytecie Cornella."

#: people
#. About Ching Wan Tang, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ching-wan-tang.about.2"
msgid "He joined Eastman Kodak as a research scientist in 1975. With Steven Van Slyke he found a metal chelate that gave a lasting glow. The National Inventors Hall of Fame lists US patent 4,356,429 for the OLED and inducted him in 2018."
msgstr "W 1975 roku rozpoczął pracę w Eastman Kodak jako pracownik naukowy. Wraz ze Stevenem Van Slyke'em znalazł chelat metalu, który dawał trwałe świecenie. National Inventors Hall of Fame wymienia patent USA 4,356,429 na OLED, a w 2018 roku przyjęła go w swoje szeregi."

#: people
#. About Ching Wan Tang, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ching-wan-tang.about.3"
msgid "He retired from Kodak in 2006 as a Distinguished Fellow of the Kodak Research Laboratories and joined the chemical engineering department of the University of Rochester. He received the Wolf Prize in Chemistry in 2011 and the Kyoto Prize in 2019."
msgstr "W 2006 roku przeszedł na emeryturę w Kodaku jako Distinguished Fellow Kodak Research Laboratories i dołączył do wydziału inżynierii chemicznej Uniwersytetu w Rochester. W 2011 roku otrzymał Nagrodę Wolfa w dziedzinie chemii, a w 2019 roku Nagrodę Kioto."

#: people
#. About Steven Van Slyke, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.steven-van-slyke.about.1"
msgid "He studied chemistry at Ithaca College, graduating in 1978, and took a master's degree in materials science at the Rochester Institute of Technology. Kodak was his first job after college, and the National Inventors Hall of Fame dates his start there to 1979."
msgstr "Studiował chemię w Ithaca College, kończąc studia w 1978 roku, i uzyskał tytuł magistra materiałoznawstwa w Rochester Institute of Technology. Kodak był jego pierwszą pracą po studiach, a National Inventors Hall of Fame datuje rozpoczęcie przez niego pracy w tej firmie na 1979 rok."

#: people
#. About Steven Van Slyke, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.steven-van-slyke.about.2"
msgid "With Ching Wan Tang he searched Kodak's chemical library and found a metal chelate that gave a lasting glow. He then spent about fifteen years on the basic science of electroluminescence."
msgstr "Wraz z Ching Wan Tangiem przeszukał bibliotekę związków chemicznych Kodaka i znalazł chelat metalu, który dawał trwałe świecenie. Następnie przez około piętnaście lat zajmował się podstawami naukowymi elektroluminescencji."

#: people
#. About Steven Van Slyke, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.steven-van-slyke.about.3"
msgid "In the mid 1990s he moved to process engineering and helped license the technology for a car audio display of 1996. The Hall of Fame records 40 patents of his on OLED materials and device design, and inducted him with Tang in 2018."
msgstr "W połowie lat 90. przeszedł do inżynierii procesowej i pomógł udzielić licencji na technologię do samochodowego wyświetlacza audio z 1996 roku. Hall of Fame odnotowuje 40 jego patentów dotyczących materiałów OLED i konstrukcji urządzeń, a w 2018 roku przyjęła go razem z Tangiem."

#: people
#. About Steven Van Slyke, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.steven-van-slyke.about.4"
msgid "Kodak sold its OLED intellectual property in 2009. He then joined Kateeva, a start-up in Silicon Valley that worked on inkjet printing of OLED panels, as chief technology officer."
msgstr "W 2009 roku Kodak sprzedał swoją własność intelektualną dotyczącą OLED. Następnie dołączył jako dyrektor ds. technologii do Kateeva, start-upu z Doliny Krzemowej, który pracował nad drukiem atramentowym paneli OLED."

#: people
#. About Hongxing Jiang, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.hongxing-jiang.about.1"
msgid "He took a degree at Fudan University in Shanghai and a doctorate in physics at Syracuse University in 1986. After two years as a research associate at Michigan State University he joined the physics faculty of Kansas State University in 1988."
msgstr "Ukończył Uniwersytet Fudan w Szanghaju, a w 1986 roku uzyskał doktorat z fizyki na Syracuse University. Po dwóch latach jako asystent naukowy na Michigan State University w 1988 roku dołączył do kadry wydziału fizyki Kansas State University."

#: people
#. About Hongxing Jiang, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.hongxing-jiang.about.2"
msgid "At Kansas State, by their own account, he and Jingyu Lin saw blue light from a gallium nitride microLED 12 micrometres across in August 1999. In November 2000 they built a microdisplay of 10 by 10 microLEDs."
msgstr "Na Kansas State University, według ich własnej relacji, on i Jingyu Lin w sierpniu 1999 roku zobaczyli niebieskie światło z diody microLED z azotku galu o szerokości 12 mikrometrów. W listopadzie 2000 roku zbudowali mikrowyświetlacz złożony z 10 na 10 diod microLED."

#: people
#. About Hongxing Jiang, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.hongxing-jiang.about.3"
msgid "He directed the Kansas Advanced Semiconductor Coordinated Laboratory from 1998 to 2008, when he and Lin moved their group to Texas Tech University. His Texas Tech CV dates a microdisplay of 640 by 480 pixels, driven by a silicon chip, to 2009."
msgstr "Od 1998 do 2008 roku kierował Kansas Advanced Semiconductor Coordinated Laboratory, kiedy to on i Lin przenieśli swoją grupę na Texas Tech University. Jego CV z Texas Tech datuje mikrowyświetlacz o rozdzielczości 640 na 480 pikseli, sterowany krzemowym chipem, na 2009 rok."

#: people
#. About Hongxing Jiang, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.hongxing-jiang.about.4"
msgid "The pair's own account dates their report of an actively driven microdisplay to July 2011. Both held Horn professorships at Texas Tech. In 2021 the International SSL Alliance gave him an award citing the invention of the microLED."
msgstr "Własna relacja pary datuje ich doniesienie o aktywnie sterowanym mikrowyświetlaczu na lipiec 2011 roku. Oboje mieli na Texas Tech profesury Horn. W 2021 roku International SSL Alliance przyznał mu nagrodę, wskazując w uzasadnieniu wynalezienie microLED."

#: people
#. About Jingyu Lin, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.jingyu-lin.about.1"
msgid "She studied physics at the State University of New York College at Oneonta and at Syracuse University, where she took a doctorate in 1989. She was then a professor of physics at Kansas State University."
msgstr "Studiowała fizykę w State University of New York College at Oneonta i na Syracuse University, gdzie w 1989 roku uzyskała doktorat. Następnie była profesorką fizyki na Kansas State University."

#: people
#. About Jingyu Lin, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.jingyu-lin.about.2"
msgid "There, by their own account, she and Hongxing Jiang saw blue light from a gallium nitride microLED 12 micrometres across in August 1999. Everybody else was working on normal size LEDs, she told Texas Tech, so they thought smaller ones would have many uses."
msgstr "Tam, według ich własnej relacji, ona i Hongxing Jiang w sierpniu 1999 roku zobaczyli niebieskie światło z diody microLED z azotku galu o szerokości 12 mikrometrów. Wszyscy inni pracowali nad diodami LED normalnej wielkości, powiedziała uczelni Texas Tech, więc uznali, że mniejsze znajdą wiele zastosowań."

#: people
#. About Jingyu Lin, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.jingyu-lin.about.3"
msgid "They filed a patent together and in November 2000 built a 10 by 10 microdisplay. They wrote that no funding agency would then pay for a display driven by a silicon chip, until their company III-N Technology won funding from the United States Army."
msgstr "Razem zgłosili patent, a w listopadzie 2000 roku zbudowali mikrowyświetlacz 10 na 10. Napisali, że żadna instytucja finansująca nie chciała wtedy płacić za wyświetlacz sterowany krzemowym chipem, dopóki ich firma III-N Technology nie zdobyła finansowania od Armii Stanów Zjednoczonych."

#: people
#. About Jingyu Lin, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.jingyu-lin.about.4"
msgid "In 2008 she and Jiang moved their group to Texas Tech University. There she held a Horn professorship and the Linda F. Whitacre Chair in Electrical and Computer Engineering, and co-directed the Nano-Photonics Center. She became a National Academy of Inventors fellow in 2018."
msgstr "W 2008 roku ona i Jiang przenieśli swoją grupę na Texas Tech University. Miała tam profesurę Horn i stanowisko Linda F. Whitacre Chair in Electrical and Computer Engineering, a także współkierowała Nano-Photonics Center. W 2018 roku została członkinią (fellow) National Academy of Inventors."

#: people
#. About Vicki Colvin, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.vicki-colvin.about.1"
msgid "She took a degree in chemistry and physics at Stanford University in 1988 and a doctorate in chemistry at the University of California, Berkeley, in 1994. Louisiana State University says she developed there the original technology for using colloidal quantum dots in displays."
msgstr "W 1988 roku uzyskała dyplom z chemii i fizyki na Uniwersytecie Stanforda, a w 1994 roku doktorat z chemii na Uniwersytecie Kalifornijskim w Berkeley. Louisiana State University podaje, że opracowała tam pierwotną technologię wykorzystania koloidalnych kropek kwantowych w wyświetlaczach."

#: people
#. About Vicki Colvin, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.vicki-colvin.about.2"
msgid "In 1994 she, M. C. Schlamp and Paul Alivisatos reported in Nature that the colour of their diode ran from red to yellow with the size of its nanocrystals, at only 4 volts."
msgstr "W 1994 roku ona, M. C. Schlamp i Paul Alivisatos donieśli w „Nature”, że barwa ich diody zmieniała się od czerwonej do żółtej zależnie od rozmiaru jej nanokryształów, przy napięciu zaledwie 4 woltów."

#: people
#. About Vicki Colvin, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.vicki-colvin.about.3"
msgid "At Rice University she was a professor of chemistry and vice provost for research, and directed the National Science Foundation's Center for Biological and Environmental Nanotechnology."
msgstr "Na Rice University była profesorką chemii i wiceprorektorką ds. badań oraz kierowała Center for Biological and Environmental Nanotechnology, ośrodkiem National Science Foundation."

#: people
#. About Vicki Colvin, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.vicki-colvin.about.4"
msgid "She moved to Brown University, where she was provost from July 2015 to July 2016 and directed the Center for Biomedical Engineering. In 2024 Louisiana State University named her dean of its College of Engineering."
msgstr "Przeniosła się na Uniwersytet Browna, gdzie od lipca 2015 do lipca 2016 roku była prorektorką (provost) i kierowała Center for Biomedical Engineering. W 2024 roku Louisiana State University mianował ją dziekanką swojego College of Engineering."

#: people
#. About M. C. Schlamp, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.m-c-schlamp.about.1"
msgid "Schlamp worked with Paul Alivisatos in the Department of Chemistry at the University of California, Berkeley, the affiliation given on their papers of 1994 and 1997."
msgstr "Nazwisko Schlamp widnieje obok nazwiska Paula Alivisatosa w ich artykułach z 1994 i 1997 roku, z afiliacją Wydziału Chemii Uniwersytetu Kalifornijskiego w Berkeley, gdzie trwała ich wspólna praca."

#: people
#. About M. C. Schlamp, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.m-c-schlamp.about.2"
msgid "In 1994 Schlamp, Vicki Colvin and Alivisatos reported in Nature a diode that paired cadmium selenide nanocrystals with the semiconducting polymer PPV. Its colour ran from red to yellow with the size of the nanocrystals, at only 4 volts."
msgstr "Artykuł w „Nature” z 1994 roku, podpisany nazwiskami Schlamp, Vicki Colvin i Alivisatos, opisywał diodę łączącą nanokryształy selenku kadmu z półprzewodzącym polimerem PPV. Jej barwa zmieniała się od czerwonej do żółtej zależnie od rozmiaru nanokryształów, przy napięciu zaledwie 4 woltów."

#: people
#. About M. C. Schlamp, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.m-c-schlamp.about.3"
msgid "In 1997 Schlamp, Xiaogang Peng and Alivisatos reported diodes in the Journal of Applied Physics that paired PPV with cadmium selenide nanocrystals in cadmium sulphide shells. They glowed red to green, from as little as 4 volts."
msgstr "Artykuł w „Journal of Applied Physics” z 1997 roku, podpisany nazwiskami Schlamp, Xiaogang Peng i Alivisatos, opisywał diody łączące PPV z nanokryształami selenku kadmu w otoczkach z siarczku kadmu. Świeciły one od czerwieni do zieleni przy napięciu już od 4 woltów."

#: people
#. About Paul Alivisatos, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.paul-alivisatos.about.1"
msgid "He studied chemistry at the University of Chicago, graduating in 1981, and took a doctorate at the University of California, Berkeley, in 1986. He taught at Berkeley from 1988 to 2021, latterly as executive vice chancellor and provost."
msgstr "Studiował chemię na Uniwersytecie Chicagowskim, który ukończył w 1981 roku, a w 1986 roku uzyskał doktorat na Uniwersytecie Kalifornijskim w Berkeley. Od 1988 do 2021 roku wykładał w Berkeley, w ostatnim okresie jako prorektor wykonawczy i provost."

#: people
#. About Paul Alivisatos, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.paul-alivisatos.about.2"
msgid "From 2009 to 2016 he directed the Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory. His group worked on controlling the size and shape of nanocrystals, and he was a founder of two companies, Quantum Dot Corp and Nanosys."
msgstr "Od 2009 do 2016 roku kierował Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory. Jego grupa pracowała nad kontrolą rozmiaru i kształtu nanokryształów, a on był założycielem dwóch firm, Quantum Dot Corp i Nanosys."

#: people
#. About Paul Alivisatos, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.paul-alivisatos.about.3"
msgid "In 1994 he, Vicki Colvin and M. C. Schlamp reported in Nature a diode of cadmium selenide nanocrystals and a semiconducting polymer, its colour set by the size of the nanocrystals. The University of Chicago says his inventions are used in QLED television displays."
msgstr "W 1994 roku on, Vicki Colvin i M. C. Schlamp opisali w „Nature” diodę z nanokryształów selenku kadmu i półprzewodzącego polimeru, której barwę wyznaczał rozmiar nanokryształów. Uniwersytet Chicagowski podaje, że jego wynalazki są stosowane w wyświetlaczach telewizorów QLED."

#: people
#. About Paul Alivisatos, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.paul-alivisatos.about.4"
msgid "He became the fourteenth president of the University of Chicago on 1 September 2021."
msgstr "1 września 2021 roku został czternastym prezydentem Uniwersytetu Chicagowskiego."

#: people
#. About Aleksey Yekimov, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.aleksey-yekimov.about.1"
msgid "He graduated in physics from Leningrad State University in 1967 and took a doctorate at the Ioffe Physical-Technical Institute in 1974. He then did research at the Vavilov State Optical Institute in Leningrad."
msgstr "W 1967 roku ukończył fizykę na Leningradzkim Uniwersytecie Państwowym, a w 1974 roku uzyskał doktorat w Instytucie Fizyczno-Technicznym im. Ioffego. Następnie prowadził badania w Państwowym Instytucie Optycznym im. Wawiłowa w Leningradzie."

#: people
#. About Aleksey Yekimov, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.aleksey-yekimov.about.2"
msgid "With his doctoral student Alexei Onushchenko he tinted silicate glass with copper chloride. The temperature of the process set the size of the crystals, from a few to tens of nanometres. In 1981 he traced the effect to quantum confinement."
msgstr "Wraz ze swoim doktorantem, Alexeiem Onushchenko, barwił szkło krzemianowe chlorkiem miedzi. Temperatura procesu wyznaczała rozmiar kryształów, od kilku do kilkudziesięciu nanometrów. W 1981 roku wyjaśnił ten efekt kwantowym uwięzieniem."

#: people
#. About Aleksey Yekimov, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.aleksey-yekimov.about.3"
msgid "From 1999 he was chief scientist at Nanocrystals Technology Inc. in New York. He shared the Nobel Prize in Chemistry of 2023 with Louis Brus and Moungi Bawendi, for the discovery and synthesis of quantum dots."
msgstr "Od 1999 roku był głównym naukowcem w Nanocrystals Technology Inc. w Nowym Jorku. Wraz z Louisem Brusem i Moungim Bawendim otrzymał Nagrodę Nobla w dziedzinie chemii z 2023 roku za odkrycie i syntezę kropek kwantowych."

#: people
#. About Aleksey Yekimov, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.aleksey-yekimov.about.4"
msgid "Optica and Britannica spell his name Ekimov."
msgstr "Optica i Britannica zapisują jego nazwisko jako Ekimov."

#: people
#. About Louis Brus, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.louis-brus.about.1"
msgid "Born in Cleveland, he studied at Rice University on a Navy scholarship and took a doctorate in physical chemistry at Columbia University in 1969. He then served as a scientific staff officer at the Naval Research Laboratory in Washington."
msgstr "Urodzony w Cleveland, studiował na Rice University dzięki stypendium marynarki wojennej i w 1969 roku uzyskał doktorat z chemii fizycznej na Uniwersytecie Columbia. Następnie służył jako oficer naukowy w Naval Research Laboratory w Waszyngtonie."

#: people
#. About Louis Brus, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.louis-brus.about.2"
msgid "He worked at Bell Laboratories from 1973 to 1996. There, in 1983, he made the nanocrystals later known as quantum dots."
msgstr "Od 1973 do 1996 roku pracował w Bell Laboratories. Tam w 1983 roku wytworzył nanokryształy, które później nazwano kropkami kwantowymi."

#: people
#. About Louis Brus, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.louis-brus.about.3"
msgid "In 1996 he joined the chemistry department at Columbia University. He shared the Nobel Prize in Chemistry of 2023 with Aleksey Yekimov and Moungi Bawendi."
msgstr "W 1996 roku dołączył do wydziału chemii Uniwersytetu Columbia. Wraz z Alekseyem Yekimovem i Moungim Bawendim otrzymał Nagrodę Nobla w dziedzinie chemii z 2023 roku."

#: people
#. About Moungi Bawendi, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.moungi-bawendi.about.1"
msgid "He took an undergraduate degree at Harvard University in 1982 and a doctorate at the University of Chicago in 1988. As a postdoctoral researcher he worked with Louis Brus at AT&T Bell Laboratories."
msgstr "W 1982 roku ukończył studia licencjackie na Uniwersytecie Harvarda, a w 1988 roku uzyskał doktorat na Uniwersytecie Chicagowskim. Jako stażysta podoktorski pracował z Louisem Brusem w AT&T Bell Laboratories."

#: people
#. About Moungi Bawendi, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.moungi-bawendi.about.2"
msgid "He joined the faculty of the Massachusetts Institute of Technology in 1990 and became the Lester Wolfe Professor of Chemistry. His group grew dots of a chosen size by varying the conditions under which they crystallised."
msgstr "W 1990 roku dołączył do kadry Massachusetts Institute of Technology i został profesorem chemii na stanowisku Lester Wolfe Professor of Chemistry. Jego grupa hodowała kropki o wybranym rozmiarze, zmieniając warunki, w jakich krystalizowały."

#: people
#. About Moungi Bawendi, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.moungi-bawendi.about.3"
msgid "He later found ways to control how efficiently the dots gave off light and to curb their habit of blinking on and off."
msgstr "Później znalazł sposoby kontrolowania wydajności, z jaką kropki emitują światło, oraz ograniczania ich skłonności do migania, czyli naprzemiennego zapalania się i gaśnięcia."

#: people
#. About Xiaogang Peng, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.xiaogang-peng.about.1"
msgid "With M. C. Schlamp and Paul Alivisatos at the University of California, Berkeley, the chemist Xiaogang Peng reported in 1997 diodes made with nanocrystals that had a core and a shell."
msgstr "Chemik Xiaogang Peng, M. C. Schlamp i Paul Alivisatos z Uniwersytetu Kalifornijskiego w Berkeley opisali w 1997 roku diody wykonane z nanokryształów, które miały rdzeń i otoczkę."

#: people
#. About Xiaogang Peng, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.xiaogang-peng.about.2"
msgid "At the University of Arkansas he held the Scharlau professorship of chemistry and biochemistry and worked on ways to grow nanocrystals of high quality in solution. In 2002 he and colleagues founded NN-Labs to sell nanocrystals."
msgstr "Na Uniwersytecie Arkansas zajmował stanowisko Scharlau Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry i pracował nad metodami hodowli wysokiej jakości nanokryształów w roztworze. W 2002 roku on i współpracownicy założyli NN-Labs, by sprzedawać nanokryształy."

#: people
#. About Xiaogang Peng, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.xiaogang-peng.about.3"
msgid "He later moved to the Department of Chemistry at Zhejiang University. There he, Yizheng Jin and others reported in Nature in 2014 a red diode with a thin insulating layer between the dots and the oxide layer that carried electrons."
msgstr "Później przeszedł na Wydział Chemii Uniwersytetu Zhejiang. Tam on, Yizheng Jin i inni opisali w „Nature” w 2014 roku czerwoną diodę z cienką warstwą izolacyjną między kropkami a warstwą tlenkową, która przewodziła elektrony."

#: people
#. About Xiaogang Peng, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.xiaogang-peng.about.4"
msgid "The paper says that he and Jin designed the experiments and supervised the work."
msgstr "Artykuł podaje, że on i Jin zaprojektowali eksperymenty i nadzorowali pracę."

#: people
#. About Yizheng Jin, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.yizheng-jin.about.1"
msgid "A chemist, he was a tenured professor at Zhejiang University and directed the Institute of Advanced Materials Chemistry in its Department of Chemistry. His work covered light-emitting diodes made from solutions, with quantum dots or perovskites, and the oxide layers used in them."
msgstr "Chemik, był profesorem na stałym etacie na Uniwersytecie Zhejiang i kierował Institute of Advanced Materials Chemistry na jego Wydziale Chemii. Jego prace obejmowały diody elektroluminescencyjne wytwarzane z roztworów, z kropkami kwantowymi lub perowskitami, oraz stosowane w nich warstwy tlenkowe."

#: people
#. About Yizheng Jin, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.yizheng-jin.about.2"
msgid "In 2014 he, Xiaogang Peng and others reported in Nature a red diode in which an insulating layer about 6 nanometres thick, between the dots and the oxide, balanced the charge. The paper says he and Peng designed the experiments and supervised the work."
msgstr "W 2014 roku on, Xiaogang Peng i inni opisali w „Nature” czerwoną diodę, w której warstwa izolacyjna o grubości około 6 nanometrów, umieszczona między kropkami a tlenkiem, równoważyła ładunek. Artykuł podaje, że on i Peng zaprojektowali eksperymenty i nadzorowali pracę."

#: people
#. About Yizheng Jin, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.yizheng-jin.about.3"
msgid "A speaker profile for ICDT, a conference of the Society for Information Display, says his research achievements were among the Top 10 Scientific Progresses in China of 2014. China's Ministry of Education named him a Chang Jiang Scholar Distinguished Professor in 2023."
msgstr "Profil prelegenta przygotowany na ICDT, konferencję Society for Information Display, podaje, że jego osiągnięcia badawcze znalazły się wśród Top 10 Scientific Progresses in China of 2014. W 2023 roku chińskie Ministerstwo Edukacji mianowało go Chang Jiang Scholar Distinguished Professor."

#: people
#. About Tuomo Suntola, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.tuomo-suntola.about.1"
msgid "Born in Tampere, he took a doctorate at Helsinki University of Technology. When the medical instrument company Instrumentarium asked him for product ideas, he proposed atomic layer deposition, and he filed a patent on it in 1974."
msgstr "Urodzony w Tampere, uzyskał doktorat na Politechnice Helsińskiej. Gdy firma Instrumentarium, producent aparatury medycznej, poprosiła go o pomysły na produkty, zaproponował osadzanie warstw atomowych i w 1974 roku zgłosił na nie patent."

#: people
#. About Tuomo Suntola, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.tuomo-suntola.about.2"
msgid "According to thisisFINLAND, the first panel made this way showed arriving and departing flights at Helsinki Airport, and commercial production followed in the 1980s. He later worked on the method at Microchemistry, a subsidiary of the energy company Neste."
msgstr "Według thisisFINLAND pierwszy panel wykonany tą metodą wyświetlał przyloty i odloty na lotnisku w Helsinkach, a produkcja komercyjna ruszyła w latach 80. Później pracował nad tą metodą w Microchemistry, spółce zależnej koncernu energetycznego Neste."

#: people
#. About Tuomo Suntola, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.tuomo-suntola.about.3"
msgid "Intel began to use the method in its chips in 2007. Suntola received the Millennium Technology Prize in 2018. He co-owned the ALD company Picosun until it was sold to Applied Materials in 2022."
msgstr "W 2007 roku Intel zaczął stosować tę metodę w swoich układach. W 2018 roku Suntola otrzymał Millennium Technology Prize. Był współwłaścicielem firmy Picosun, zajmującej się ALD, do czasu jej sprzedaży Applied Materials w 2022 roku."

#: people
#. About Dawon Kahng, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.dawon-kahng.about.1"
msgid "He took a bachelor's degree at Seoul National University in 1955 and his master's and doctoral degrees at Ohio State University. He joined Bell Telephone Laboratories in 1959."
msgstr "W 1955 roku uzyskał licencjat na Uniwersytecie Narodowym w Seulu, a stopnie magistra i doktora na Ohio State University. W 1959 roku rozpoczął pracę w Bell Telephone Laboratories."

#: people
#. About Dawon Kahng, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.dawon-kahng.about.2"
msgid "He and Mohamed Atalla built a working transistor of metal, oxide and silicon, using Atalla's method of coating silicon with an insulating layer of silicon oxide. The National Inventors Hall of Fame says they announced the device, now called the MOSFET, in 1960."
msgstr "On i Mohamed Atalla zbudowali działający tranzystor z metalu, tlenku i krzemu, wykorzystując metodę Atalli, polegającą na pokrywaniu krzemu izolującą warstwą tlenku krzemu. National Inventors Hall of Fame podaje, że ogłosili oni to urządzenie, dziś nazywane MOSFET, w 1960 roku."

#: people
#. About Dawon Kahng, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.dawon-kahng.about.3"
msgid "He retired from Bell Laboratories in 1988. The Hall of Fame says he then founded the NEC Research Institute, for basic research in computing and communications. It inducted him in 2009."
msgstr "W 1988 roku przeszedł na emeryturę z Bell Laboratories. Hall of Fame podaje, że następnie założył NEC Research Institute, zajmujący się badaniami podstawowymi w dziedzinie informatyki i komunikacji. W 2009 roku Hall of Fame przyjęła go w swoje szeregi."

#: people
#. About Ibn al-Haytham, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ibn-al-haytham.about.1"
msgid "Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn al-Haytham was born in Basra, in what is now Iraq. In the medieval accounts MacTutor follows, he trained for an official career, was made a minister for Basra and its region, and then turned to science, reading Aristotle above all."
msgstr "Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn al-Haytham urodził się w Basrze, na terenie dzisiejszego Iraku. Według średniowiecznych relacji, za którymi podąża MacTutor, kształcił się do kariery urzędniczej, został ministrem dla Basry i okolic, a następnie zwrócił się ku nauce, czytając przede wszystkim Arystotelesa."

#: people
#. About Ibn al-Haytham, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ibn-al-haytham.about.2"
msgid "The Fatimid caliph al-Hakim, ruler of Egypt, set him to regulate the Nile. Ibn al-Haytham travelled upriver with a team of engineers, judged the plan unworkable and said so. MacTutor and Britannica record that he later feigned madness and was confined to his house."
msgstr "Fatymidzki kalif al-Hakim, władca Egiptu, polecił mu uregulować Nil. Ibn al-Haytham wyruszył w górę rzeki z zespołem inżynierów, uznał plan za niewykonalny i powiedział o tym. MacTutor i Britannica odnotowują, że później udawał szaleństwo i został zamknięty w swoim domu."

#: people
#. About Ibn al-Haytham, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ibn-al-haytham.about.3"
msgid "His Kitab al-Manazir, the Book of Optics, ran to seven books and rested on experiment. MacTutor dates its Latin translation to 1270, Britannica to the early thirteenth century. Latin readers knew him as Alhazen. In Cairo he lived by writing, teaching and copying texts."
msgstr "Jego „Kitab al-Manazir”, czyli Księga optyki, liczyła siedem ksiąg i opierała się na eksperymencie. MacTutor datuje jej łaciński przekład na 1270 rok, Britannica na początek XIII wieku. Łacińscy czytelnicy znali go jako Alhazen. W Kairze utrzymywał się z pisania, nauczania i kopiowania tekstów."

#: people
#. About Ibn al-Haytham, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ibn-al-haytham.about.4"
msgid "Britannica says his treatise On the Shape of the Eclipse discusses the camera obscura. It also reports an argument that the medieval records merge two men of this name, a mathematician who wrote on optics and an astronomer and philosopher who wrote the autobiography."
msgstr "Britannica podaje, że jego traktat O kształcie zaćmienia omawia camera obscura. Odnotowuje też argument, że średniowieczne źródła łączą w jedną postać dwóch mężczyzn o tym imieniu, matematyka, który pisał o optyce, oraz astronoma i filozofa, który napisał autobiografię."

#: people
#. About Gemma Frisius, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.gemma-frisius.about.1"
msgid "Born in Dokkum in Friesland, he entered the University of Leuven in 1526 as a student without money. He studied medicine but stayed on for mathematics and astronomy, practised as a physician in Leuven, and became professor of medicine and mathematics there."
msgstr "Urodzony w Dokkum we Fryzji, w 1526 roku wstąpił na Uniwersytet w Lowanium jako student bez środków. Studiował medycynę, ale pozostał, by zajmować się matematyką i astronomią, praktykował jako lekarz w Lowanium i został tam profesorem medycyny i matematyki."

#: people
#. About Gemma Frisius, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.gemma-frisius.about.2"
msgid "With the goldsmith Gaspard van der Heyden, and Gerardus Mercator as engraver, he made a terrestrial globe in 1536 and a celestial globe in 1537. In 1530 he proposed finding longitude by comparing local time with a carried clock."
msgstr "Wraz ze złotnikiem Gaspardem van der Heydenem i z Gerardusem Mercatorem jako rytownikiem wykonał w 1536 roku globus ziemski, a w 1537 roku globus nieba. W 1530 roku zaproponował wyznaczanie długości geograficznej przez porównanie czasu lokalnego ze wskazaniem przewożonego zegara."

#: people
#. About Gemma Frisius, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.gemma-frisius.about.3"
msgid "MacTutor credits his tract of 1533 with the first proposal to fix places by triangulation. His De radio astronomico of 1545 described a cross staff about one and a half metres long. He died at Leuven."
msgstr "MacTutor przypisuje jego traktatowi z 1533 roku pierwszą propozycję wyznaczania położenia miejsc za pomocą triangulacji. Jego praca „De radio astronomico” z 1545 roku opisywała laskę Jakubową o długości około półtora metra. Zmarł w Lowanium."

#: people
#. About Daniele Barbaro, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.daniele-barbaro.about.1"
msgid "Born in Venice, in 1513 by the Museo Galileo and in 1514 by the Online Books Page, he studied philosophy, mathematics and optics at the University of Padua. He served the Venetian state as ambassador in London."
msgstr "Urodzony w Wenecji, według Museo Galileo w 1513 roku, a według Online Books Page w 1514 roku, studiował filozofię, matematykę i optykę na Uniwersytecie w Padwie. Służył państwu weneckiemu jako ambasador w Londynie."

#: people
#. About Daniele Barbaro, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.daniele-barbaro.about.2"
msgid "He was named patriarch elect of Aquileia in 1550 and died with that title in 1570. In 1561 he represented Venice at the Council of Trent."
msgstr "W 1550 roku został mianowany patriarchą elektem Akwilei i zmarł z tym tytułem w 1570 roku. W 1561 roku reprezentował Wenecję na soborze trydenckim."

#: people
#. About Daniele Barbaro, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.daniele-barbaro.about.3"
msgid "In 1556 he published an Italian translation of Vitruvius on architecture with a long commentary, and a Latin edition in 1567. He was a friend of the architect Andrea Palladio."
msgstr "W 1556 roku opublikował włoski przekład dzieła Witruwiusza o architekturze z obszernym komentarzem, a w 1567 roku wydanie łacińskie. Był przyjacielem architekta Andrei Palladia."

#: people
#. About Daniele Barbaro, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.daniele-barbaro.about.4"
msgid "His treatise on perspective, La pratica della perspettiva, appeared in Venice. The Museo Galileo dates it to 1569 and calls it a treatise on the science of painting. The Online Books Page lists printings of 1568 and 1569."
msgstr "Jego traktat o perspektywie, „La pratica della perspettiva”, ukazał się w Wenecji. Museo Galileo datuje go na 1569 rok i nazywa traktatem o nauce malarstwa. Online Books Page wymienia wydania z 1568 i 1569 roku."

#: people
#. About Johannes Kepler, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.johannes-kepler.about.1"
msgid "Born in Weil der Stadt near Stuttgart, he studied at Tübingen under the Copernican Michael Maestlin and taught at Graz from 1594."
msgstr "Urodzony w Weil der Stadt koło Stuttgartu, studiował w Tybindze u kopernikanina Michaela Maestlina, a od 1594 roku uczył w Grazu."

#: people
#. About Johannes Kepler, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.johannes-kepler.about.2"
msgid "He joined Tycho Brahe in Prague in 1600 and after Brahe died in 1601 succeeded him as mathematician to Emperor Rudolf II. His Astronomiae pars optica of 1604 used reflection and refraction to explain eclipses."
msgstr "W 1600 roku dołączył do Tychona Brahego w Pradze, a po śmierci Brahego w 1601 roku zastąpił go jako matematyk cesarza Rudolfa II. Jego praca „Astronomiae pars optica” z 1604 roku wyjaśniała zaćmienia za pomocą odbicia i załamania światła."

#: people
#. About Johannes Kepler, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.johannes-kepler.about.3"
msgid "Astronomia nova of 1609 set out elliptical orbits and the law of equal areas. His Dioptrice of 1611 described a telescope with two convex lenses. He moved to Linz in 1612. Harmonice mundi of 1619 gave a third law."
msgstr "„Astronomia nova” z 1609 roku przedstawiała orbity eliptyczne i prawo równych pól. Jego „Dioptrice” z 1611 roku opisywała teleskop z dwiema soczewkami wypukłymi. W 1612 roku przeniósł się do Linzu. „Harmonice mundi” z 1619 roku podawała trzecie prawo."

#: people
#. About Ibn Daniyal, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ibn-daniyal.about.1"
msgid "Doctor and poet as well as a man of the theatre, he came from Iraq and settled in Cairo in the years after the Mongols took Baghdad in 1258. He wrote his plays as dialogue with verse and music, and directed the shows himself."
msgstr "Lekarz i poeta, a zarazem człowiek teatru, pochodził z Iraku i osiadł w Kairze w latach po zdobyciu Bagdadu przez Mongołów w 1258 roku. Pisał swoje sztuki jako dialogi z wierszem i muzyką, a przedstawienia reżyserował sam."

#: people
#. About Ibn Daniyal, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ibn-daniyal.about.2"
msgid "The plays are Ṭayf al-Khayāl, which the World Encyclopedia of Puppetry Arts renders as The Shadow Spirit, and two others it calls Strange and Bizarre and The Lover."
msgstr "Sztuki te to „Ṭayf al-Khayāl”, co World Encyclopedia of Puppetry Arts oddaje jako Duch cienia, oraz dwie inne, które encyklopedia nazywa Dziwne i osobliwe oraz Kochanek."

#: people
#. About Ibn Daniyal, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ibn-daniyal.about.3"
msgid "The opening play seems to praise Sultan Baybars and his laws against vice, but the encyclopedia reads it as satire on the Mamluk sultanate that ruled from Cairo."
msgstr "Pierwsza sztuka zdaje się wychwalać sułtana Baybarsa i jego prawa przeciw występkom, ale encyklopedia odczytuje ją jako satyrę na sułtanat mamelucki, który rządził z Kairu."

#: people
#. About Ibn Daniyal, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ibn-daniyal.about.4"
msgid "The texts survive in four manuscripts, the oldest of 1425 in the Süleymaniye Library in Istanbul. Paul Kahle edited two of the plays between 1910 and 1912 and found Mamluk leather figures now in the Islamic Museum in Berlin."
msgstr "Teksty zachowały się w czterech rękopisach, z których najstarszy, z 1425 roku, znajduje się w Bibliotece Sulejmanie w Stambule. Paul Kahle wydał dwie z tych sztuk między 1910 a 1912 rokiem i odnalazł mameluckie skórzane figury, które znajdują się dziś w Muzeum Islamskim w Berlinie."

#: people
#. About François Dominique Séraphin, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.francois-dominique-seraphin.about.1"
msgid "The World Encyclopedia of Puppetry Arts says that at twenty three he opened a theatre behind an inn in the Lannion garden at Versailles, showing shadows with changing scenery. He was called to play for the court three times a week in carnival."
msgstr "World Encyclopedia of Puppetry Arts podaje, że w wieku dwudziestu trzech lat otworzył teatr za gospodą w ogrodzie Lannion w Wersalu, pokazując cienie ze zmieniającymi się dekoracjami. W czasie karnawału wzywano go, by trzy razy w tygodniu grał dla dworu."

#: people
#. About François Dominique Séraphin, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.francois-dominique-seraphin.about.2"
msgid "In Paris he settled in the new galleries of the Palais Royal. His bill mixed comic pieces by Dorvigny and Guillemain with fairy tales such as Cendrillon, or Cinderella."
msgstr "W Paryżu osiadł w nowych galeriach Palais Royal. Jego repertuar łączył komiczne utwory Dorvigny'ego i Guillemaina z baśniami, takimi jak „Cendrillon”, czyli Kopciuszek."

#: people
#. About François Dominique Séraphin, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.francois-dominique-seraphin.about.3"
msgid "In 1790, a year after the fall of the Bastille, he staged La Démonseigneurisation, a title the encyclopedia renders roughly as Bringing Down the Aristocrat. His descendants kept the Séraphin shows going until 1870, moving the theatre to the Passage Jouffroy in 1859."
msgstr "W 1790 roku, rok po upadku Bastylii, wystawił „La Démonseigneurisation”, co encyklopedia oddaje w przybliżeniu jako Obalenie arystokraty. Jego potomkowie prowadzili przedstawienia Séraphina do 1870 roku, a w 1859 roku przenieśli teatr do Passage Jouffroy."

#: people
#. About Henri Rivière, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.henri-riviere.about.1"
msgid "Born in Paris, he went to the Collège Rollin, came to drawing by copying illustrations by Doré and Vierge, and trained for a short time in the studio of Émile Bin."
msgstr "Urodzony w Paryżu, uczęszczał do Collège Rollin, do rysunku doszedł, kopiując ilustracje Doré'a i Vierge'a, i przez krótki czas kształcił się w pracowni Émile'a Bina."

#: people
#. About Henri Rivière, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.henri-riviere.about.2"
msgid "He frequented the Chat Noir from about eighteen and helped start its journal. In 1886 Rodolphe Salis gave him artistic and technical charge of the cabaret's shadow theatre."
msgstr "Od około osiemnastego roku życia bywał w Chat Noir i pomagał założyć jego pismo. W 1886 roku Rodolphe Salis powierzył mu artystyczne i techniczne kierownictwo teatru cieni tego kabaretu."

#: people
#. About Henri Rivière, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.henri-riviere.about.3"
msgid "In the 1890s he made woodcuts after Japanese models, and in 1902 published lithographs, Trente six vues de la Tour Eiffel, as a tribute to Hokusai. He collected about 800 Japanese objects and gave up printmaking for watercolour in 1916."
msgstr "W latach 90. XIX wieku wykonywał drzeworyty według wzorów japońskich, a w 1902 roku opublikował litografie „Trente six vues de la Tour Eiffel” jako hołd dla Hokusaia. Zgromadził około 800 przedmiotów japońskich, a w 1916 roku porzucił grafikę warsztatową na rzecz akwareli."

#: people
#. About Lotte Reiniger, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.lotte-reiniger.about.1"
msgid "Born in Berlin, she loved scherenschnitte, the cutting of paper silhouettes. At seventeen she tried acting at the Max Reinhardt School, and her silhouettes led Paul Wegener to hire her for an animated film, The Pied Piper of Hamelin."
msgstr "Urodzona w Berlinie, kochała scherenschnitte, wycinanie sylwetek z papieru. W wieku siedemnastu lat próbowała aktorstwa w szkole Maxa Reinhardta, a jej wycinanki sprawiły, że Paul Wegener zatrudnił ją przy filmie animowanym Szczurołap z Hameln."

#: people
#. About Lotte Reiniger, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.lotte-reiniger.about.2"
msgid "With Carl Koch, later her husband, she made The Adventures of Prince Achmed from 1923 to 1926. The Library of Congress calls it the oldest surviving animated feature film. Two earlier features made in Argentina are lost."
msgstr "Z Carlem Kochem, później jej mężem, zrobiła w latach 1923 do 1926 Przygody księcia Achmeda. Biblioteka Kongresu nazywa je najstarszym zachowanym pełnometrażowym filmem animowanym. Dwa wcześniejsze filmy zrobione w Argentynie zaginęły."

#: people
#. About Lotte Reiniger, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.lotte-reiniger.about.3"
msgid "Her figures were cut from black cardboard and thin lead, every limb separately, and joined with wire hinges, she wrote in 1936. They lay on an animation table, usually lit from below, and were moved by hand between frames."
msgstr "Jej figury wycinano z czarnego kartonu i cienkiego ołowiu, każdą kończynę osobno, i łączono drucianymi zawiasami, jak pisała w 1936 roku. Leżały na stole animacyjnym, zwykle podświetlonym od spodu, i przesuwano je ręcznie między klatkami."

#: people
#. About Lotte Reiniger, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.lotte-reiniger.about.4"
msgid "To give her scenes depth she laid them on horizontal planes stacked under the camera. The Library of Congress says she was the first to develop multiplane technology. The Stadtmuseum Tübingen keeps her estate, with figures made for Achmed between 1923 and 1926."
msgstr "Aby nadać scenom głębię, układała je na poziomych płaszczyznach ułożonych jedna nad drugą pod kamerą. Biblioteka Kongresu podaje, że jako pierwsza opracowała technikę wieloplanową. Stadtmuseum w Tybindze przechowuje jej spuściznę, z figurami zrobionymi do Achmeda w latach 1923 do 1926."

#: people
#. About Kara Walker, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.kara-walker.about.1"
msgid "From Stockton, California, she took a bachelor's degree at the Atlanta College of Art and a master's degree at the Rhode Island School of Design. In 1994 the Drawing Center in New York showed Gone, her wall installation of black paper silhouettes."
msgstr "Pochodzi ze Stockton w Kalifornii. Uzyskała licencjat w Atlanta College of Art i tytuł magistra w Rhode Island School of Design. W 1994 roku Drawing Center w Nowym Jorku pokazało Gone, jej instalację ścienną z sylwetek z czarnego papieru."

#: people
#. About Kara Walker, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.kara-walker.about.2"
msgid "The Walker Art Center says her work exposes the ongoing psychological injury caused by the legacy of slavery and examines racial and gender stereotypes. She received a MacArthur Fellowship in 1997 and represented the United States at the Bienal de São Paulo in 2002."
msgstr "Walker Art Center podaje, że jej twórczość obnaża wciąż trwającą krzywdę psychiczną spowodowaną dziedzictwem niewolnictwa i bada stereotypy rasowe i płciowe. W 1997 roku otrzymała stypendium MacArthura, a w 2002 roku reprezentowała Stany Zjednoczone na Bienal de São Paulo."

#: people
#. About Kara Walker, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.kara-walker.about.3"
msgid "In 2004 she made Testimony, a silent film on 16mm in which shadow puppets and title cards tell a story of masters and slaves. The Museum of Modern Art holds a puppet from it, of cut black paper with pencil, tape and metal fasteners."
msgstr "W 2004 roku stworzyła Testimony, niemy film na taśmie 16 mm, w którym lalki cieniowe i plansze z napisami opowiadają historię o panach i niewolnikach. Museum of Modern Art przechowuje jedną z lalek z tego filmu, wykonaną z wycinanego czarnego papieru, ołówka, taśmy i metalowych łączników."

#: people
#. About Kara Walker, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.kara-walker.about.4"
msgid "In 2014 she showed A Subtlety, a sphinx-like woman of polystyrene coated with white sugar, in a warehouse on the former Domino Sugar site in Brooklyn. The Walker Art Center ties it to sugar harvested by enslaved people on Caribbean plantations."
msgstr "W 2014 roku pokazała A Subtlety, przypominającą sfinksa postać kobiety z polistyrenu pokrytego białym cukrem, w magazynie na dawnym terenie Domino Sugar na Brooklynie. Walker Art Center wiąże ją z cukrem zbieranym przez zniewolonych ludzi na karaibskich plantacjach."

#: people
#. About James Fergason, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.james-fergason.about.1"
msgid "Born in Wakenda, Missouri, he took a degree in physics at the University of Missouri in 1956. The Lemelson-MIT Program says he organised the first American research team on liquid crystals, at Westinghouse Research Labs from 1957."
msgstr "Urodził się w miejscowości Wakenda w stanie Missouri, a w 1956 roku ukończył fizykę na University of Missouri. Lemelson-MIT Program podaje, że od 1957 roku zorganizował w Westinghouse Research Labs pierwszy amerykański zespół badawczy zajmujący się ciekłymi kryształami."

#: people
#. About James Fergason, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.james-fergason.about.2"
msgid "His patent of 1963 used cholesteric liquid crystals to sense temperature. In 1966 he joined the Liquid Crystal Institute at Kent State University, later as associate director. The Lemelson-MIT Program dates his discovery of the twisted nematic effect to 1967, Kent State to 1969."
msgstr "Jego patent z 1963 roku wykorzystywał cholesteryczne ciekłe kryształy do wykrywania temperatury. W 1966 roku dołączył do Liquid Crystal Institute na Kent State University, gdzie później był zastępcą dyrektora. Lemelson-MIT Program datuje jego odkrycie efektu skręconego nematyka na 1967 rok, a Kent State na 1969."

#: people
#. About James Fergason, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.james-fergason.about.3"
msgid "Kent State notes that Martin Schadt and Wolfgang Helfrich patented similar technology in Europe. He founded ILIXCO to make displays, as early as 1968 by Kent State's account and in 1970 by the Lemelson-MIT Program's."
msgstr "Kent State zauważa, że Martin Schadt i Wolfgang Helfrich opatentowali podobną technologię w Europie. Założył firmę ILIXCO, by produkować wyświetlacze, według Kent State już w 1968 roku, a według Lemelson-MIT Program w 1970."

#: people
#. About James Fergason, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.james-fergason.about.4"
msgid "He held more than 125 United States patents, entered the National Inventors Hall of Fame in 1998 and received the Lemelson-MIT Prize in 2006."
msgstr "Miał ponad 125 patentów amerykańskich, w 1998 roku został przyjęty do National Inventors Hall of Fame, a w 2006 roku otrzymał Lemelson-MIT Prize."

#: people
#. About George Heilmeier, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.george-heilmeier.about.1"
msgid "He studied electrical engineering at the University of Pennsylvania and took a PhD in electronics at Princeton in 1962. He joined RCA Laboratories in 1958 and came to direct its solid state device research."
msgstr "Studiował elektrotechnikę na University of Pennsylvania, a w 1962 roku uzyskał doktorat z elektroniki na Uniwersytecie Princeton. W 1958 roku zaczął pracę w RCA Laboratories i z czasem stanął na czele prowadzonych tam badań nad przyrządami półprzewodnikowymi."

#: people
#. About George Heilmeier, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.george-heilmeier.about.2"
msgid "In 1964 he found that a voltage changed the colour of a nematic liquid crystal doped with dye. RCA showed prototype liquid crystal displays in 1968."
msgstr "W 1964 roku odkrył, że napięcie elektryczne zmienia barwę nematycznego ciekłego kryształu domieszkowanego barwnikiem. RCA pokazała prototypy wyświetlaczy ciekłokrystalicznych w 1968 roku."

#: people
#. About George Heilmeier, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.george-heilmeier.about.3"
msgid "He became a White House Fellow in 1970. The Kyoto Prize dates his appointment as director of the Defense Advanced Research Projects Agency to 1974, the Lemelson-MIT Program to 1975."
msgstr "W 1970 roku został stypendystą programu White House Fellows. Nagroda Kioto datuje jego nominację na dyrektora Defense Advanced Research Projects Agency na 1974 rok, a Lemelson-MIT Program na 1975."

#: people
#. About George Heilmeier, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.george-heilmeier.about.4"
msgid "He joined Texas Instruments in 1977 and from 1991 led Bell Communications Research, known as Bellcore. He received the Kyoto Prize in Advanced Technology in 2005."
msgstr "W 1977 roku przeszedł do Texas Instruments, a od 1991 roku kierował Bell Communications Research, znaną jako Bellcore. W 2005 roku otrzymał Nagrodę Kioto w dziedzinie zaawansowanych technologii."

#: people
#. About Sivaramakrishna Chandrasekhar, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.sivaramakrishna-chandrasekhar.about.1"
msgid "After postgraduate study at the University of Cambridge he joined the University of Mysore with the task of building a school of physics. After a further spell in Britain he moved to the Raman Research Institute in Bangalore in 1971."
msgstr "Po studiach podyplomowych na Uniwersytecie Cambridge podjął pracę na University of Mysore z zadaniem stworzenia szkoły fizyki. Po kolejnym pobycie w Wielkiej Brytanii przeniósł się w 1971 roku do Raman Research Institute w Bangalore."

#: people
#. About Sivaramakrishna Chandrasekhar, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.sivaramakrishna-chandrasekhar.about.2"
msgid "There he set up and led a liquid crystal laboratory. In 1977 he, B. K. Sadashiva and K. A. Suresh reported in the journal Pramana compounds called benzene hexa n alkanoates, whose disc molecules stacked into columns set in a hexagonal array."
msgstr "Tam założył laboratorium ciekłych kryształów i nim kierował. W 1977 roku on, B. K. Sadashiva i K. A. Suresh opisali w czasopiśmie Pramana związki zwane heksa-n-alkanianami benzenu, których cząsteczki w kształcie dysków układały się w kolumny rozmieszczone w sieci heksagonalnej."

#: people
#. About Sivaramakrishna Chandrasekhar, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.sivaramakrishna-chandrasekhar.about.3"
msgid "Suresh recalls that Chandrasekhar took up the disc project, set Suresh to study the samples by X-ray and asked Sadashiva to prepare pure ones."
msgstr "Suresh wspomina, że Chandrasekhar podjął projekt z dyskami, polecił Sureshowi zbadać próbki rentgenowsko, a Sadashivę poprosił o przygotowanie czystych próbek."

#: people
#. About Sivaramakrishna Chandrasekhar, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.sivaramakrishna-chandrasekhar.about.4"
msgid "SciDev.Net records that he never ceased to promote science in India, and that he won international recognition for advancing science in developing countries."
msgstr "SciDev.Net odnotowuje, że nigdy nie przestał propagować nauki w Indiach i że zdobył międzynarodowe uznanie za rozwój nauki w krajach rozwijających się."

#: people
#. About B. K. Sadashiva, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.b-k-sadashiva.about.1"
msgid "A chemist, he took a master's degree in organic chemistry at Bangalore University and a PhD under Sivaramakrishna Chandrasekhar at the Raman Research Institute, where he spent his whole career and retired as a senior professor in 2008."
msgstr "Był chemikiem. Uzyskał tytuł magistra chemii organicznej na Bangalore University, a doktorat pod kierunkiem Sivaramakrishny Chandrasekhara w Raman Research Institute, gdzie spędził całą karierę i skąd w 2008 roku przeszedł na emeryturę jako starszy profesor."

#: people
#. About B. K. Sadashiva, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.b-k-sadashiva.about.2"
msgid "K. A. Suresh recalls that Shyam Singh, a scientist at the institute, took up the synthesis of the disc compounds in 1976, and that the samples proved somewhat impure. Chandrasekhar then asked Sadashiva, a doctoral student, to continue, and Sadashiva prepared pure samples."
msgstr "K. A. Suresh wspomina, że w 1976 roku syntezy związków dyskowych podjęła się osoba z kadry naukowej instytutu, Shyam Singh, i że próbki okazały się nieco zanieczyszczone. Chandrasekhar poprosił wtedy doktoranta Sadashivę o kontynuację prac, a Sadashiva przygotował czyste próbki."

#: people
#. About B. K. Sadashiva, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.b-k-sadashiva.about.3"
msgid "With Chandrasekhar and Suresh he wrote the report of 1977 on these liquid crystals in the journal Pramana. He later worked on metallomesogens, liquid crystals that contain metals, and on chiral layered liquid crystals."
msgstr "Razem z Chandrasekharem i Sureshem napisał raport z 1977 roku o tych ciekłych kryształach w czasopiśmie Pramana. Później zajmował się metalomezogenami, czyli ciekłymi kryształami zawierającymi metale, oraz chiralnymi warstwowymi ciekłymi kryształami."

#: people
#. About B. K. Sadashiva, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.b-k-sadashiva.about.4"
msgid "The obituary in Liquid Crystals records the G. W. Gray Medal of the British Liquid Crystal Society and a fellowship of the National Academy of Sciences. He died in 2020."
msgstr "Nekrolog w Liquid Crystals wymienia G. W. Gray Medal przyznany przez British Liquid Crystal Society oraz tytuł fellow National Academy of Sciences. Zmarł w 2020 roku."

#: people
#. About K. A. Suresh, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.k-a-suresh.about.1"
msgid "Kattera A. Suresh took his doctorate at the Raman Research Institute in Bangalore in 1979."
msgstr "Kattera A. Suresh uzyskał doktorat w Raman Research Institute w Bangalore w 1979 roku."

#: people
#. About K. A. Suresh, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.k-a-suresh.about.2"
msgid "Set by Sivaramakrishna Chandrasekhar to study the new compounds, he examined them by X-ray diffraction and proposed a model of discs stacked in columns, which became accepted as the hexagonal columnar structure."
msgstr "Skierowany przez Sivaramakrishnę Chandrasekhara do badania nowych związków, przebadał je metodą dyfrakcji rentgenowskiej i zaproponował model dysków ułożonych w kolumny, który przyjęto później jako heksagonalną strukturę kolumnową."

#: people
#. About K. A. Suresh, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.k-a-suresh.about.3"
msgid "He held a fellowship at the Collège de France in Paris in 1983, then worked for Dowell Schlumberger in France and at Carnegie Mellon University before returning to the institute in 1989."
msgstr "W 1983 roku był stypendystą Collège de France w Paryżu, następnie pracował dla Dowell Schlumberger we Francji i na Carnegie Mellon University, a w 1989 roku wrócił do instytutu."

#: people
#. About K. A. Suresh, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.k-a-suresh.about.4"
msgid "He became a senior professor there in 2004 and from 2010 was Scientist of Eminence at the Centre for Nano and Soft Matter Sciences in Bangalore."
msgstr "W 2004 roku został tam starszym profesorem, a od 2010 roku był Scientist of Eminence w Centre for Nano and Soft Matter Sciences w Bangalore."

#: people
#. About Mohamed Atalla, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.mohamed-atalla.about.1"
msgid "Born in Port Said, Egypt, he took a master's degree and a doctorate in mechanical engineering at Purdue University in 1947 and 1949, then joined Bell Laboratories. The National Inventors Hall of Fame lists him as Martin (John) M. Atalla, Purdue as John Atalla."
msgstr "Urodził się w Port Saidzie w Egipcie. W 1947 i 1949 roku uzyskał na Purdue University tytuł magistra i doktorat z inżynierii mechanicznej, a następnie zaczął pracę w Bell Laboratories. National Inventors Hall of Fame podaje jego nazwisko jako Martin (John) M. Atalla, a Purdue jako John Atalla."

#: people
#. About Mohamed Atalla, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.mohamed-atalla.about.2"
msgid "There he studied the surface of silicon and grew a layer of silicon dioxide on the wafer to overcome the surface states that blocked current. He proposed a metal, oxide and silicon transistor and assigned it to Dawon Kahng."
msgstr "Tam badał powierzchnię krzemu i wytworzył na płytce warstwę dwutlenku krzemu, by pokonać stany powierzchniowe blokujące przepływ prądu. Zaproponował tranzystor z metalu, tlenku i krzemu i powierzył prace nad nim Dawonowi Kahngowi."

#: people
#. About Mohamed Atalla, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.mohamed-atalla.about.3"
msgid "The National Inventors Hall of Fame says he and Kahng built the working device and announced it in 1960."
msgstr "Według National Inventors Hall of Fame on i Kahng zbudowali działające urządzenie i ogłosili to w 1960 roku."

#: people
#. About Mohamed Atalla, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.mohamed-atalla.about.4"
msgid "In 1962 he co-founded Hewlett-Packard Associates, and in 1972 he founded the Atalla Corporation, whose Atalla Box encrypted PIN and cash machine messages. The National Inventors Hall of Fame inducted him in 2009."
msgstr "W 1962 roku współzałożył Hewlett-Packard Associates, a w 1972 roku założył Atalla Corporation, której urządzenie Atalla Box szyfrowało kody PIN i komunikaty bankomatów. W 2009 roku został przyjęty do National Inventors Hall of Fame."

#: people
#. About Larry Hornbeck, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.larry-hornbeck.about.1"
msgid "Born in St. Louis, he joined Texas Instruments in 1973 and took a doctorate in physics at Case Western Reserve University in 1974."
msgstr "Urodził się w St. Louis, w 1973 roku zaczął pracę w Texas Instruments, a w 1974 roku uzyskał doktorat z fizyki na Case Western Reserve University."

#: people
#. About Larry Hornbeck, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.larry-hornbeck.about.2"
msgid "At the company's Central Research Laboratories he began in 1977 on analogue deformable mirrors, and spent about a decade on them before turning to hinged digital ones."
msgstr "W Central Research Laboratories firmy zaczął w 1977 roku pracę nad analogowymi lustrami odkształcalnymi i poświęcił im około dziesięciu lat, zanim zajął się cyfrowymi lustrami na zawiasach."

#: people
#. About Larry Hornbeck, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.larry-hornbeck.about.3"
msgid "By the count of the University of Texas at Dallas he came to hold 38 United States patents, 34 of them on the mirror device."
msgstr "Według zestawienia University of Texas at Dallas z czasem uzyskał 38 patentów amerykańskich, z czego 34 dotyczyły urządzenia z mikrolustrami."

#: people
#. About Larry Hornbeck, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.larry-hornbeck.about.4"
msgid "He received an Engineering Emmy in 1998, and in 2015 an Academy Award of Merit for the chip as used in cinema projectors. He joined the faculty of the University of Texas at Dallas in 2017."
msgstr "W 1998 roku otrzymał nagrodę Engineering Emmy, a w 2015 roku Academy Award of Merit za ten układ w zastosowaniu do projektorów kinowych. W 2017 roku dołączył do kadry University of Texas at Dallas."

#: people
#. About Elsa Garmire, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.elsa-garmire.about.1"
msgid "Born in Buffalo, New York, she took degrees in physics at Harvard and at MIT, where the optics society SPIE says she was Charles Townes's first graduate student, working on nonlinear effects of strong laser beams."
msgstr "Urodziła się w Buffalo w stanie Nowy Jork i ukończyła fizykę na Uniwersytecie Harvarda i w MIT, gdzie według towarzystwa optycznego SPIE była pierwszą doktorantką Charlesa Townesa i zajmowała się nieliniowymi efektami silnych wiązek laserowych."

#: people
#. About Elsa Garmire, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.elsa-garmire.about.2"
msgid "She came to Caltech in 1966 as a postdoctoral researcher with Amnon Yariv and was a senior research fellow there until 1973. SPIE records that she was the only woman working as a technical professional in Caltech's electrical engineering building."
msgstr "W 1966 roku przyszła do Caltechu jako badaczka podoktorska u Amnona Yariva i do 1973 roku była tam starszą pracowniczką naukową. SPIE odnotowuje, że była jedyną kobietą pracującą jako specjalistka techniczna w budynku elektrotechniki Caltechu."

#: people
#. About Elsa Garmire, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.elsa-garmire.about.3"
msgid "For Experiments in Art and Technology, a project on how light and technology could help artists, she designed the large Mylar mirror of the Pepsi pavilion at Expo 70 in Osaka. She also made new optics for laser shows."
msgstr "Dla Experiments in Art and Technology, projektu poświęconego temu, jak światło i technika mogą pomóc artystom, zaprojektowała duże lustro z Mylaru w pawilonie Pepsi na Expo 70 w Osace. Stworzyła też nową optykę do pokazów laserowych."

#: people
#. About Elsa Garmire, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.elsa-garmire.about.4"
msgid "SPIE says she and Ivan Dryer started Laser Images, with her as president. Dryer recalled that she had it incorporated in February 1971. She gave it to him in 1973, then taught at the University of Southern California and Dartmouth College."
msgstr "Według SPIE ona i Ivan Dryer założyli Laser Images, a ona została prezeską. Dryer wspominał, że w lutym 1971 roku zleciła rejestrację firmy. W 1973 roku przekazała mu firmę, a potem uczyła na University of Southern California i w Dartmouth College."

#: people
#. About Ivan Dryer, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ivan-dryer.about.1"
msgid "From 1956 to 1968 he worked at intervals as a guide at Griffith Observatory in Los Angeles. He also worked as a filmmaker, including as documentary editor on the feature film Executive Action."
msgstr "Od 1956 do 1968 roku z przerwami pracował jako przewodnik w Griffith Observatory w Los Angeles. Pracował też jako filmowiec, między innymi jako montażysta materiałów dokumentalnych przy filmie fabularnym Executive Action."

#: people
#. About Ivan Dryer, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ivan-dryer.about.2"
msgid "In November 1970 he and the filmmaker Dale Pelton saw Elsa Garmire show her laser art at a conference at the University of Southern California, and she invited them to film it. He recalled that she had their company incorporated in February 1971."
msgstr "W listopadzie 1970 roku on i Dale Pelton, z zawodu filmowcy, zobaczyli, jak Elsa Garmire pokazuje swoją sztukę laserową na konferencji na University of Southern California, a ona zaprosiła ich do jej sfilmowania. Wspominał, że w lutym 1971 roku doprowadziła do rejestracji ich wspólnej firmy."

#: people
#. About Ivan Dryer, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ivan-dryer.about.3"
msgid "The optics society SPIE says Garmire and Dryer started the company, Laser Images, with her as president. She gave it to him in 1973, and he always credited her for her part in the technology and the business, SPIE adds."
msgstr "Towarzystwo optyczne SPIE podaje, że Garmire i Dryer założyli firmę Laser Images, a prezeską została ona. W 1973 roku przekazała mu firmę, a on zawsze przyznawał jej zasługi w technologii i w prowadzeniu firmy, dodaje SPIE."

#: people
#. About Ivan Dryer, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ivan-dryer.about.4"
msgid "Laserium ran at Griffith until January 2002. His company took shows to 46 planetariums and other venues. According to Live Design, the International Laser Display Association gave him its first Career Achievement Award in 1989."
msgstr "Laserium wyświetlano w Griffith do stycznia 2002 roku. Jego firma pokazywała spektakle w 46 planetariach i innych miejscach. Według Live Design pierwszą Career Achievement Award przyznaną przez International Laser Display Association otrzymał w 1989 roku."

#: people
#. About Leota Toombs, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.leota-toombs.about.1"
msgid "She began at the Walt Disney Studios in 1940 in the Ink and Paint department and moved to animation. She returned in 1962 to join WED Enterprises."
msgstr "W 1940 roku zaczęła pracę w Walt Disney Studios w dziale tuszowania i malowania (Ink and Paint), a potem przeszła do animacji. W 1962 roku wróciła, by dołączyć do WED Enterprises."

#: people
#. About Leota Toombs, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.leota-toombs.about.2"
msgid "She worked on It's a Small World, Great Moments with Mr. Lincoln and Ford's Magic Skyway for the 1964 to 1965 New York World's Fair, then on Pirates of the Caribbean and the Haunted Mansion."
msgstr "Pracowała przy It's a Small World, Great Moments with Mr. Lincoln i Ford's Magic Skyway na Wystawę Światową w Nowym Jorku, trwającą od 1964 do 1965 roku, a następnie przy Pirates of the Caribbean i Haunted Mansion."

#: people
#. About Leota Toombs, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.leota-toombs.about.3"
msgid "Recalling Madame Leota, she said her eyes were the right distance apart to fit the test model when the work began. She also voiced the bride known as Little Leota at the end of the ride."
msgstr "Wspominając Madame Leotę, mówiła, że gdy zaczynano prace, jej oczy były rozstawione w sam raz, by pasować do modelu testowego. Użyczyła też głosu pannie młodej zwanej Little Leota na końcu przejażdżki."

#: people
#. About Leota Toombs, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.leota-toombs.about.4"
msgid "In 1971 she moved to Walt Disney World to set up the team that kept its shows running. From 1979 she trained figure finishers and artisans for Disneyland in California. She died in December 1991."
msgstr "W 1971 roku przeniosła się do Walt Disney World, by stworzyć zespół dbający o sprawne działanie jego atrakcji. Od 1979 roku szkoliła wykończeniowców figur i rzemieślników dla Disneylandu w Kalifornii. Zmarła w grudniu 1991 roku."

#: people
#. About Michael Naimark, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.michael-naimark.about.1"
msgid "He made Displacements three times between 1980 and 1984, the third at the San Francisco Museum of Modern Art. A 16mm camera on a slow turntable filmed two performers in a living room. Projected back onto the whitened room, the unpainted performers looked ghostlike."
msgstr "W latach od 1980 do 1984 trzykrotnie zrealizował Displacements, za trzecim razem w San Francisco Museum of Modern Art. Kamera 16 mm na wolno obracającej się tarczy filmowała dwie osoby występujące w salonie. Gdy film wyświetlono z powrotem na pobielony pokój, niepomalowane postacie wyglądały jak zjawy."

#: people
#. About Michael Naimark, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.michael-naimark.about.2"
msgid "His Ars Electronica biography puts him on the original design team of the MIT Media Lab in 1980. He was a founding member of the Atari Research Lab, the Apple Multimedia Lab and Lucasfilm Interactive, and joined Interval Research in 1992."
msgstr "Jego biografia na stronie Ars Electronica umieszcza go w pierwotnym zespole projektowym MIT Media Lab w 1980 roku. Był członkiem założycielem Atari Research Lab, Apple Multimedia Lab i Lucasfilm Interactive, a w 1992 roku dołączył do Interval Research."

#: people
#. About Michael Naimark, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.michael-naimark.about.3"
msgid "The same biography listed his art projects in the permanent collections of the Exploratorium in San Francisco, the American Museum of the Moving Image in New York and the Zentrum für Kunst und Medientechnologie in Karlsruhe, Germany."
msgstr "Ta sama biografia wymieniała jego projekty artystyczne w stałych zbiorach Exploratorium w San Francisco, American Museum of the Moving Image w Nowym Jorku oraz Zentrum für Kunst und Medientechnologie w Karlsruhe w Niemczech."

#: people
#. About Ramesh Raskar, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ramesh-raskar.about.1"
msgid "He studied engineering in Pune, India, and took his doctorate at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill. His research at Mitsubishi Electric Research Laboratories produced 40 patents."
msgstr "Studiował inżynierię w Pune w Indiach, a doktorat uzyskał na University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill. Jego badania w Mitsubishi Electric Research Laboratories zaowocowały 40 patentami."

#: people
#. About Ramesh Raskar, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ramesh-raskar.about.2"
msgid "The shader lamps paper, which he wrote at Mitsubishi with Greg Welch, Kok-Lim Low and Deepak Bandyopadhyay, names him first among its authors. It covered a plain object with images from several projectors so that it took on its own or another appearance."
msgstr "Artykuł o shader lamps, który napisał w Mitsubishi z Gregiem Welchem, Kok-Lim Low i Deepakiem Bandyopadhyayem, wymienia go na pierwszym miejscu wśród autorów. Opisana w nim metoda pokrywała zwykły przedmiot obrazami z kilku projektorów, tak że przybierał on własny wygląd lub wygląd czegoś innego."

#: people
#. About Ramesh Raskar, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ramesh-raskar.about.3"
msgid "In 2008 he founded the Camera Culture group at the MIT Media Lab. In 2016 he received the Lemelson-MIT Prize for his body of inventive work, including femto-photography, which the Lemelson-MIT Program says gives the sense of peering around corners."
msgstr "W 2008 roku założył grupę Camera Culture w MIT Media Lab. W 2016 roku otrzymał Lemelson-MIT Prize za całokształt pracy wynalazczej, w tym za femtofotografię, która według Lemelson-MIT Program daje wrażenie zaglądania za róg."

#: people
#. About Greg Welch, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.greg-welch.about.1"
msgid "He worked at NASA's Jet Propulsion Laboratory and at the Defense Systems Division of Northrop Grumman, and was a research professor at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill."
msgstr "Pracował w Jet Propulsion Laboratory NASA i w Defense Systems Division firmy Northrop Grumman, a także był profesorem badawczym na University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill."

#: people
#. About Greg Welch, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.greg-welch.about.2"
msgid "With Ramesh Raskar, Kok-Lim Low and Deepak Bandyopadhyay he wrote the shader lamps paper of 2001, which gives his affiliation as Chapel Hill. It covered a plain object with images from several projectors."
msgstr "Wraz z Rameshem Raskarem, Kok-Lim Low i Deepakiem Bandyopadhyayem napisał artykuł o shader lamps z 2001 roku, który jako jego afiliację podaje Chapel Hill. Opisana w nim metoda pokrywała zwykły przedmiot obrazami z kilku projektorów."

#: people
#. About Greg Welch, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.greg-welch.about.3"
msgid "He moved to the University of Central Florida, where he became a Pegasus Professor, holder of the AdventHealth Endowed Chair in Healthcare Simulation and co-director of the Synthetic Reality Lab."
msgstr "Przeszedł na University of Central Florida, gdzie otrzymał tytuł Pegasus Professor, objął katedrę AdventHealth Endowed Chair in Healthcare Simulation i został współdyrektorem Synthetic Reality Lab."

#: people
#. About Greg Welch, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.greg-welch.about.4"
msgid "A 2026 article from the university says his patented work ranges from projection mapping, of the kind used on Cinderella Castle at Walt Disney World, to tactile telepresence for isolated patients."
msgstr "Artykuł uczelni z 2026 roku podaje, że jego opatentowane prace obejmują zarówno mapping projekcyjny, taki jak na Zamku Kopciuszka w Walt Disney World, jak i dotykową teleobecność dla pacjentów w izolacji."

#: people
#. About Kok-Lim Low, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.kok-lim-low.about.1"
msgid "With Ramesh Raskar, Greg Welch and Deepak Bandyopadhyay he wrote the shader lamps paper of 2001, which gives his affiliation as the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill. He took his doctorate in computer science there in 2006."
msgstr "Wraz z Rameshem Raskarem, Gregiem Welchem i Deepakiem Bandyopadhyayem napisał artykuł o shader lamps z 2001 roku, który jako jego afiliację podaje University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill. W 2006 roku uzyskał tam doktorat z informatyki."

#: people
#. About Kok-Lim Low, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.kok-lim-low.about.2"
msgid "He joined the School of Computing of the National University of Singapore, where he became a senior lecturer. His work there covered computer graphics, real-time rendering and the automated design of papercraft."
msgstr "Dołączył do School of Computing na National University of Singapore, gdzie został starszym wykładowcą. Jego prace obejmowały tam grafikę komputerową, renderowanie w czasie rzeczywistym i automatyczne projektowanie modeli z papieru."

#: people
#. About Deepak Bandyopadhyay, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.deepak-bandyopadhyay.about.1"
msgid "With Ramesh Raskar, Greg Welch and Kok-Lim Low he wrote the shader lamps paper of 2001, which gives his affiliation as the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill."
msgstr "Wraz z Rameshem Raskarem, Gregiem Welchem i Kok-Lim Low napisał artykuł o shader lamps z 2001 roku, który jako jego afiliację podaje University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill."

#: people
#. About Deepak Bandyopadhyay, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.deepak-bandyopadhyay.about.2"
msgid "He took his doctorate there in 2006 under Jack Snoeyink, with a thesis on a geometric framework for nearest neighbour analysis of protein structure and function."
msgstr "W 2006 roku uzyskał tam doktorat pod kierunkiem Jacka Snoeyinka na podstawie rozprawy o geometrycznych podstawach analizy najbliższego sąsiedztwa w badaniu struktury i funkcji białek."

#: people
#. About Lanny Smoot, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.lanny-smoot.about.1"
msgid "Born in New York City, he took degrees in electrical engineering at Columbia University. From 1978 to 1998 he was at Bell Laboratories and Bellcore, with patents in fibre optics, video on demand and video conferencing."
msgstr "Urodził się w Nowym Jorku i ukończył elektrotechnikę na Uniwersytecie Columbia. Od 1978 do 1998 roku pracował w Bell Laboratories i Bellcore, gdzie uzyskał patenty z zakresu światłowodów, wideo na życzenie i wideokonferencji."

#: people
#. About Lanny Smoot, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.lanny-smoot.about.2"
msgid "He joined Disney in 1998 and worked as a research fellow and head of Imagineering research and development. His work included an extendable lightsaber and the HoloTile floor for shared virtual reality. Disney counts 74 of his patents from his 25 years there."
msgstr "W 1998 roku dołączył do Disneya i pracował jako pracownik naukowy (research fellow) oraz szef działu badań i rozwoju Imagineering. Jego prace obejmowały wysuwany miecz świetlny i podłogę HoloTile do wspólnej rzeczywistości wirtualnej. Disney liczy 74 jego patenty z 25 lat pracy w firmie."

#: people
#. About Lanny Smoot, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.lanny-smoot.about.3"
msgid "Disney credits him with inventing the Magic Playfloor game on the Disney Cruise Line and designing interactive koi ponds for the Hong Kong Disneyland Hotel. He also patented ways of creating free floating images. The National Inventors Hall of Fame inducted him in 2024."
msgstr "Disney przypisuje mu wynalezienie gry Magic Playfloor na statkach Disney Cruise Line i zaprojektowanie interaktywnych stawów z karpiami koi dla Hong Kong Disneyland Hotel. Opatentował też sposoby tworzenia obrazów swobodnie unoszących się w powietrzu. W 2024 roku został przyjęty do National Inventors Hall of Fame."

#: people
#. About Barrett Comiskey, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.barrett-comiskey.about.1"
msgid "He studied mathematics at MIT and worked nights and weekends in its Media Lab. Joseph Jacobson, who came to MIT in 1995 with the idea of a book whose content could change at the push of a button, challenged him to build it."
msgstr "Studiował matematykę w MIT i pracował nocami i w weekendy w tamtejszym Media Lab. Joseph Jacobson, który przybył do MIT w 1995 roku z pomysłem książki, której treść mogłaby się zmieniać po naciśnięciu przycisku, rzucił mu wyzwanie, by ją zbudował."

#: people
#. About Barrett Comiskey, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.barrett-comiskey.about.2"
msgid "With J. D. Albert he showed on 23 January 1997 that an electric field could move particles inside a microcapsule. He co-founded E Ink in 1997 and worked with the company for eight years in Cambridge, Massachusetts, and Shanghai, China."
msgstr "Razem z J. D. Albertem 23 stycznia 1997 roku wykazał, że pole elektryczne może przesuwać cząstki wewnątrz mikrokapsułki. W 1997 roku współzałożył E Ink i przez osiem lat pracował z firmą w Cambridge w stanie Massachusetts i w Szanghaju w Chinach."

#: people
#. About Barrett Comiskey, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.barrett-comiskey.about.3"
msgid "He later took an MBA at Stanford and has worked in Asia since 2004. The National Inventors Hall of Fame inducted him in 2016."
msgstr "Później uzyskał tytuł MBA na Uniwersytecie Stanforda, a od 2004 roku pracuje w Azji. W 2016 roku został przyjęty do National Inventors Hall of Fame."

#: people
#. About J. D. Albert, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.j-d-albert.about.1"
msgid "Jonathan Albert was a mechanical engineering student at MIT when Joseph Jacobson recruited him to his laboratory. With Barrett Comiskey he worked on Jacobson's idea of a book whose pages could be changed electronically, and they had a working prototype in January 1997."
msgstr "Jonathan Albert studiował inżynierię mechaniczną w MIT, gdy Joseph Jacobson zwerbował go do swojego laboratorium. Razem z Barrettem Comiskeyem pracował nad pomysłem Jacobsona, książką, której strony można zmieniać elektronicznie, i w styczniu 1997 roku mieli działający prototyp."

#: people
#. About J. D. Albert, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.j-d-albert.about.2"
msgid "Later in 1997 he co-founded E Ink with Comiskey, Jacobson, Russ Wilcox and Jerome Rubin, and he developed the methods used to make electronic ink displays in volume. The National Inventors Hall of Fame inducted him in 2016."
msgstr "Później w 1997 roku współzałożył E Ink, a współzałożycielami byli też Comiskey, Jacobson, Russ Wilcox i Jerome Rubin. Opracował metody masowej produkcji wyświetlaczy z atramentem elektronicznym. W 2016 roku został przyjęty do National Inventors Hall of Fame."

#: people
#. About J. D. Albert, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.j-d-albert.about.3"
msgid "He became director of engineering at Bresslergroup, a product design firm, and taught product design, engineering and entrepreneurship in the Integrated Product Design programme at the University of Pennsylvania."
msgstr "Został dyrektorem ds. inżynierii w Bresslergroup, firmie projektującej produkty, i uczył projektowania produktu, inżynierii i przedsiębiorczości w programie Integrated Product Design na University of Pennsylvania."

#: people
#. About Joseph Jacobson, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.joseph-jacobson.about.1"
msgid "He took a bachelor's degree at Brown University and a doctorate in physics at MIT, and was then a postdoctoral fellow in physics at Stanford University."
msgstr "Uzyskał licencjat na Uniwersytecie Browna i doktorat z fizyki w MIT, a następnie był stażystą podoktorskim w dziedzinie fizyki na Uniwersytecie Stanforda."

#: people
#. About Joseph Jacobson, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.joseph-jacobson.about.2"
msgid "In the mid-1990s he proposed a display of black and white particles held in tiny spheres. At the MIT Media Lab he recruited two students, Barrett Comiskey and J. D. Albert, to build it. In 1997 the three co-founded E Ink with others."
msgstr "W połowie lat dziewięćdziesiątych zaproponował wyświetlacz z czarnych i białych cząstek zamkniętych w maleńkich kulkach. W MIT Media Lab zwerbował dwóch studentów, Barretta Comiskeya i J. D. Alberta, by go zbudowali. W 1997 roku wszyscy trzej współzałożyli E Ink razem z innymi osobami."

#: people
#. About Joseph Jacobson, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.joseph-jacobson.about.3"
msgid "As a professor at the MIT Media Lab he later headed its Molecular Machines group, which works on synthetic biology. The National Inventors Hall of Fame inducted him in 2016."
msgstr "Jako profesor w MIT Media Lab kierował później tamtejszą grupą Molecular Machines, która zajmuje się biologią syntetyczną. W 2016 roku został przyjęty do National Inventors Hall of Fame."

#: people
#. About John Rogers, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.john-rogers.about.1"
msgid "He studied chemistry and physics at the University of Texas at Austin, graduating in 1989, and took a doctorate in physical chemistry at MIT in 1995. He was then a Junior Fellow of the Harvard Society of Fellows until 1997."
msgstr "Studiował chemię i fizykę na University of Texas at Austin, studia ukończył w 1989 roku, a w 1995 roku uzyskał doktorat z chemii fizycznej w MIT. Następnie do 1997 roku był Junior Fellow w Harvard Society of Fellows."

#: people
#. About John Rogers, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.john-rogers.about.2"
msgid "He joined Bell Laboratories in 1997 as a member of technical staff in condensed matter physics research, and directed that department from late 2000 to 2002. He was the lead author of the paper of 2001 in the Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences."
msgstr "W 1997 roku dołączył do Bell Laboratories jako członek personelu technicznego w dziale badań fizyki materii skondensowanej, a od końca 2000 roku do 2002 roku kierował tym działem. Był głównym autorem artykułu z 2001 roku w Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences."

#: people
#. About John Rogers, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.john-rogers.about.3"
msgid "He spent thirteen years on the faculty of the University of Illinois, then moved to Northwestern University in 2016 as professor of materials science and engineering and director of the Querrey Simpson Institute for Bioelectronics. He received a MacArthur Fellowship in 2009."
msgstr "Przez trzynaście lat pracował na University of Illinois, a w 2016 roku przeszedł na Northwestern University jako profesor materiałoznawstwa i inżynierii materiałowej oraz dyrektor Querrey Simpson Institute for Bioelectronics. W 2009 roku otrzymał stypendium MacArthura."

#: people
#. About Zhenan Bao, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.zhenan-bao.about.1"
msgid "She took her doctorate in chemistry at the University of Chicago in 1995 and joined Bell Labs, then part of Lucent Technologies. She became a Distinguished Member of Technical Staff there in 2001, and was second author of that year's paper on the bendable display."
msgstr "W 1995 roku uzyskała doktorat z chemii na Uniwersytecie Chicagowskim i dołączyła do Bell Labs, wówczas części Lucent Technologies. W 2001 roku została tam Distinguished Member of Technical Staff i była drugą autorką opublikowanego w tym roku artykułu o wyświetlaczu elastycznym."

#: people
#. About Zhenan Bao, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.zhenan-bao.about.2"
msgid "She moved to Stanford University in 2004, where she became K.K. Lee Professor and chaired the Department of Chemical Engineering from 2018 to 2022 and in 2025. She founded the Stanford Wearable Electronics Initiative, and her group works on electronics modelled on skin."
msgstr "W 2004 roku przeszła na Uniwersytet Stanforda, gdzie została profesorką z tytułem K.K. Lee Professor i kierowała Wydziałem Inżynierii Chemicznej od 2018 do 2022 roku oraz w 2025 roku. Założyła Stanford Wearable Electronics Initiative, a jej grupa zajmuje się elektroniką wzorowaną na skórze."

#: people
#. About Zhenan Bao, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.zhenan-bao.about.3"
msgid "She co-founded C3 Nano, later acquired by DuPont, and PyrAmes. She became a member of the National Academy of Sciences and the National Academy of Engineering."
msgstr "Współzałożyła C3 Nano, przejętą później przez DuPont, oraz PyrAmes. Została członkinią National Academy of Sciences i National Academy of Engineering."

#: people
#. About Deng-Ke Yang, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.deng-ke-yang.about.1"
msgid "He took a physics degree at Tsinghua University in China in 1984 and a doctorate in physics at the University of Hawaii in 1989, when he joined Kent State University. In 1994 he published on cholesteric reflective displays with J. William Doane and others."
msgstr "W 1984 roku ukończył fizykę na Uniwersytecie Tsinghua w Chinach, a w 1989 roku uzyskał doktorat z fizyki na University of Hawaii i w tym samym roku dołączył do Kent State University. W 1994 roku opublikował wraz z J. Williamem Doane'em i innymi prace o odbiciowych wyświetlaczach cholesterycznych."

#: people
#. About Deng-Ke Yang, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.deng-ke-yang.about.2"
msgid "Kent State gave him its Excellence Award in Invention in 2000 for the bistable reflective cholesteric display and polymer stabilised devices. The Society for Information Display recognised that work in 2005, and made him a Fellow in 2007."
msgstr "W 2000 roku Kent State przyznał mu Excellence Award in Invention za bistabilny odbiciowy wyświetlacz cholesteryczny i urządzenia stabilizowane polimerem. Society for Information Display wyróżniło te prace w 2005 roku, a w 2007 roku nadało mu tytuł Fellow."

#: people
#. About Deng-Ke Yang, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.deng-ke-yang.about.3"
msgid "With S. T. Wu he wrote Reflective Liquid Crystal Displays of 2001 and Fundamentals of Liquid Crystal Devices of 2006. The Society gave him its Slottow-Owaki Prize in 2017 for education and training in liquid crystal displays."
msgstr "Razem z S. T. Wu napisał książki Reflective Liquid Crystal Displays z 2001 roku i Fundamentals of Liquid Crystal Devices z 2006 roku. W 2017 roku Society for Information Display przyznało mu Slottow-Owaki Prize za kształcenie i szkolenie w dziedzinie wyświetlaczy ciekłokrystalicznych."

#: people
#. About J. William Doane, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.j-william-doane.about.1"
msgid "Bill Doane took a doctorate in physics at the University of Missouri-Columbia in 1965 and joined the Kent State University faculty that year."
msgstr "Bill Doane uzyskał doktorat z fizyki na University of Missouri-Columbia w 1965 roku i w tym samym roku dołączył do kadry Kent State University."

#: people
#. About J. William Doane, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.j-william-doane.about.2"
msgid "He became director of the Liquid Crystal Institute in 1983, and in 1991 was the founding director of the ALCOM Center for liquid crystalline optical materials. In 1995 and 1996 he published on reflective cholesteric displays in the SID Digest and Information Display."
msgstr "W 1983 roku został dyrektorem Liquid Crystal Institute, a w 1991 roku był dyrektorem założycielem ALCOM Center, ośrodka badań nad ciekłokrystalicznymi materiałami optycznymi. W 1995 i 1996 roku publikował prace o odbiciowych wyświetlaczach cholesterycznych w SID Digest i Information Display."

#: people
#. About J. William Doane, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.j-william-doane.about.3"
msgid "He co-founded Kent Displays, Inc., where he served as vice president for research and development and chief science officer. He retired from the university in 1996 and was a Fellow of the American Physical Society."
msgstr "Współzałożył Kent Displays, Inc., gdzie był wiceprezesem ds. badań i rozwoju oraz dyrektorem naukowym. W 1996 roku przeszedł na emeryturę na uniwersytecie i był członkiem (Fellow) American Physical Society."

#: people
#. About Gerardo Beni, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.gerardo-beni.about.1"
msgid "He took a degree in physics at the University of Florence, Italy, in 1970 and a doctorate in physics at the University of California, Los Angeles, in 1974."
msgstr "W 1970 roku ukończył fizykę na Uniwersytecie Florenckim we Włoszech, a w 1974 roku uzyskał doktorat z fizyki na Uniwersytecie Kalifornijskim w Los Angeles."

#: people
#. About Gerardo Beni, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.gerardo-beni.about.2"
msgid "At Bell Telephone Laboratories he and Susan Hackwood filed a patent in June 1981 on devices that change the surface tension between two fluids with a voltage. Granted in November 1983, it noted that fluids of different colours give a colour change."
msgstr "W Bell Telephone Laboratories on i Susan Hackwood zgłosili w czerwcu 1981 roku patent na urządzenia, które za pomocą napięcia elektrycznego zmieniają napięcie powierzchniowe między dwoma płynami. Patent, udzielony w listopadzie 1983 roku, wskazywał, że płyny o różnych barwach dają zmianę koloru."

#: people
#. About Gerardo Beni, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.gerardo-beni.about.3"
msgid "In 1981 the two also published a paper on electrowetting displays in Applied Physics Letters, which the Philips paper of 2003 on video-speed electrowetting cites."
msgstr "W 1981 roku oboje opublikowali też w Applied Physics Letters artykuł o wyświetlaczach elektrozwilżających, który cytuje artykuł Philipsa z 2003 roku o elektrozwilżaniu z szybkością wideo."

#: people
#. About Gerardo Beni, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.gerardo-beni.about.4"
msgid "He co-founded the Journal of Robotic Systems in 1982 and joined the faculty of electrical and computer engineering at the University of California, Riverside. He later wrote on swarm intelligence and swarm robotics."
msgstr "W 1982 roku współzałożył Journal of Robotic Systems i dołączył do kadry wydziału elektrotechniki i informatyki Uniwersytetu Kalifornijskiego w Riverside. Później pisał o inteligencji roju i robotyce rojowej."

#: people
#. About Susan Hackwood, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.susan-hackwood.about.1"
msgid "She took a doctorate in solid state ionics in the United Kingdom. At Bell Telephone Laboratories she and Gerardo Beni filed a patent in June 1981 on using a voltage to change the surface tension between two fluids."
msgstr "Doktorat z joniki ciała stałego uzyskała w Wielkiej Brytanii. W Bell Telephone Laboratories ona i Gerardo Beni zgłosili w czerwcu 1981 roku patent na wykorzystanie napięcia elektrycznego do zmiany napięcia powierzchniowego między dwoma płynami."

#: people
#. About Susan Hackwood, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.susan-hackwood.about.2"
msgid "That year the two published a paper on electrowetting displays in Applied Physics Letters. Her biography for the Centre for Science and Policy at Cambridge says she invented and named the electrowetting effect at the laboratory, where she headed device robotics technology research."
msgstr "W tym samym roku oboje opublikowali w Applied Physics Letters artykuł o wyświetlaczach elektrozwilżających. Jej biografia przygotowana dla Centre for Science and Policy w Cambridge podaje, że wynalazła i nazwała zjawisko elektrozwilżania w tym laboratorium, gdzie kierowała badaniami nad technologią robotyki urządzeń."

#: people
#. About Susan Hackwood, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.susan-hackwood.about.3"
msgid "In 1984 she joined the University of California, Santa Barbara, as a professor of electrical and computer engineering. There she founded and directed the National Science Foundation Engineering Research Center for Robotic Systems in Microelectronics."
msgstr "W 1984 roku została profesorką elektrotechniki i informatyki na Uniwersytecie Kalifornijskim w Santa Barbara. Założyła tam i prowadziła jako dyrektorka National Science Foundation Engineering Research Center for Robotic Systems in Microelectronics."

#: people
#. About Susan Hackwood, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.susan-hackwood.about.4"
msgid "In 1990 she became founding dean of the Bourns College of Engineering, University of California, Riverside. The same biography calls her the first woman dean of a major American research university. She later directed the California Council on Science and Technology."
msgstr "W 1990 roku została dziekanką założycielką Bourns College of Engineering na Uniwersytecie Kalifornijskim w Riverside. Ta sama biografia nazywa ją pierwszą kobietą na stanowisku dziekana dużej amerykańskiej uczelni badawczej. Później kierowała California Council on Science and Technology."

#: people
#. About Robert Hayes, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.robert-hayes.about.1"
msgid "A physicist at Philips Research in Eindhoven, he wrote with Johan Feenstra the paper Video-speed electronic paper based on electrowetting, published in Nature in 2003."
msgstr "Fizyk z Philips Research w Eindhoven, napisał wraz z Johanem Feenstrą artykuł Video-speed electronic paper based on electrowetting, opublikowany w Nature w 2003 roku."

#: people
#. About Robert Hayes, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.robert-hayes.about.2"
msgid "In each pixel a voltage made water push aside a coloured oil film about 10 micrometres thick, uncovering a white surface beneath. Physics World reported that a pixel switched in less than 10 milliseconds."
msgstr "W każdym pikselu napięcie sprawiało, że woda odsuwała barwną warstwę oleju o grubości około 10 mikrometrów i odsłaniała białą powierzchnię pod spodem. Physics World podał, że piksel przełączał się w czasie krótszym niż 10 milisekund."

#: people
#. About Robert Hayes, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.robert-hayes.about.3"
msgid "The paper said its colour design was four times brighter than reflective liquid crystal displays, with reflectivity and contrast close to those of paper."
msgstr "Artykuł podawał, że opisana w nim konstrukcja barwna jest cztery razy jaśniejsza od odbiciowych wyświetlaczy ciekłokrystalicznych, a jej współczynnik odbicia i kontrast są zbliżone do papieru."

#: people
#. About Johan Feenstra, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.johan-feenstra.about.1"
msgid "He took a doctorate in solid state physics at the Rijksuniversiteit Groningen in 1997. At Philips Research in the Netherlands he wrote the Nature paper of 2003 on video-speed electrowetting displays with Robert Hayes."
msgstr "W 1997 roku uzyskał doktorat z fizyki ciała stałego na Uniwersytecie w Groningen. W Philips Research w Holandii napisał z Robertem Hayesem artykuł w Nature z 2003 roku o wyświetlaczach elektrozwilżających z szybkością wideo."

#: people
#. About Johan Feenstra, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.johan-feenstra.about.2"
msgid "He co-founded Liquavista, spun out of Philips in 2006, and served as its chief executive and chief technology officer. Samsung Electronics bought the company in 2011, and it was later sold to Amazon."
msgstr "Współzałożył Liquavista, firmę wydzieloną z Philipsa w 2006 roku, i był jej prezesem oraz dyrektorem ds. technologii. W 2011 roku firmę kupił Samsung Electronics, a później sprzedano ją Amazonowi."

#: people
#. About Johan Feenstra, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.johan-feenstra.about.3"
msgid "He joined SMART Photonics, a maker of photonic chips, as chief executive in 2019."
msgstr "W 2019 roku został prezesem SMART Photonics, producenta układów fotonicznych."

#: people
#. About Mark Miles, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.mark-miles.about.1"
msgid "He took a degree in electrical engineering at MIT and spent more than twelve years on development work for clients including the Advanced Research Projects Agency and the National Science Foundation. He founded Etalon, a firm working on MEMS devices and thin film processes."
msgstr "Ukończył elektrotechnikę w MIT i przez ponad dwanaście lat prowadził prace rozwojowe dla klientów, wśród których były Advanced Research Projects Agency i National Science Foundation. Założył Etalon, firmę zajmującą się urządzeniami MEMS i procesami cienkowarstwowymi."

#: people
#. About Mark Miles, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.mark-miles.about.2"
msgid "His 2006 conference biography calls him the inventor of the interferometric modulator, a MEMS device meant for flat panel displays in portable products."
msgstr "Jego biografia konferencyjna z 2006 roku nazywa go wynalazcą modulatora interferometrycznego, urządzenia MEMS przeznaczonego do płaskich wyświetlaczy w urządzeniach przenośnych."

#: people
#. About Mark Miles, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.mark-miles.about.3"
msgid "He co-founded Iridigm Display Corporation in 1997 to develop it and, as chief technology officer, led its technology development for more than five years."
msgstr "W 1997 roku współzałożył Iridigm Display Corporation, by go rozwijać, i jako dyrektor ds. technologii przez ponad pięć lat kierował jej pracami technologicznymi."

#: people
#. About Mark Miles, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.mark-miles.about.4"
msgid "By 2006, after Qualcomm bought Iridigm in 2004, he was advising Qualcomm MEMS Technologies, the subsidiary formed to sell displays built on the modulator. He also ran Mark Miles Consulting in San Francisco and held eleven patents."
msgstr "W 2006 roku, gdy Qualcomm kupił już Iridigm w 2004 roku, doradzał Qualcomm MEMS Technologies, spółce zależnej utworzonej do sprzedaży wyświetlaczy opartych na modulatorze. Prowadził też Mark Miles Consulting w San Francisco i miał jedenaście patentów."

#: people
#. About S. K. Deb, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.s-k-deb.about.1"
msgid "Satyen Deb studied at Dacca University, graduating in 1953 and 1955, and took a doctorate in solid state physics at the Cavendish Laboratory of Cambridge University."
msgstr "Satyen Deb studiował na Dacca University, gdzie uzyskał dyplomy w 1953 i 1955 roku, a doktorat z fizyki ciała stałego zdobył w Cavendish Laboratory Uniwersytetu Cambridge."

#: people
#. About S. K. Deb, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.s-k-deb.about.2"
msgid "He was a corporate research fellow at American Cyanamid in Stamford, Connecticut. His biography at the National Renewable Energy Laboratory says that he discovered the electrochromic phenomenon in transition metal oxides."
msgstr "Był starszym pracownikiem badawczym w American Cyanamid w Stamford w stanie Connecticut. Jego biografia w National Renewable Energy Laboratory podaje, że odkrył zjawisko elektrochromowe w tlenkach metali przejściowych."

#: people
#. About S. K. Deb, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.s-k-deb.about.3"
msgid "A 1995 paper recalling the discovery sets it in the 1960s, in work on thin oxide films for recording information. It says the films could be coloured and bleached by an electric field alone, by reversing the polarity."
msgstr "Artykuł z 1995 roku, wspominający to odkrycie, umieszcza je w latach sześćdziesiątych, w pracach nad cienkimi warstwami tlenków do zapisu informacji. Podaje, że warstwy te można było barwić i odbarwiać samym polem elektrycznym, przez odwrócenie polaryzacji."

#: people
#. About S. K. Deb, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.s-k-deb.about.4"
msgid "He joined what is now the National Renewable Energy Laboratory in 1978, managed its in-house photovoltaic research and directed its Center for Basic Sciences. He was a Fellow of the American Physical Society."
msgstr "W 1978 roku dołączył do instytucji, która jest dziś National Renewable Energy Laboratory, kierował prowadzonymi tam badaniami fotowoltaicznymi i był dyrektorem Center for Basic Sciences. Był członkiem (Fellow) American Physical Society."

#: people
#. About Paula Hammond, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.paula-hammond.about.1"
msgid "She studied chemical engineering at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology, graduating in 1984, took a master's degree at Georgia Tech in 1988 and returned to MIT for her doctorate in 1993. She then held a National Science Foundation postdoctoral fellowship in chemistry at Harvard."
msgstr "Studiowała inżynierię chemiczną w Massachusetts Institute of Technology, gdzie w 1984 roku uzyskała dyplom, w 1988 roku zdobyła tytuł magistra w Georgia Tech, a w 1993 roku obroniła doktorat po powrocie do MIT. Następnie odbyła staż podoktorski z chemii na Uniwersytecie Harvarda w ramach stypendium National Science Foundation."

#: people
#. About Paula Hammond, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.paula-hammond.about.2"
msgid "She supervised Dean DeLongchamp's doctoral thesis of 2003 on films built layer by layer from materials that change colour with voltage. Combining several such materials gave films with higher contrast, faster switching and more than one colour."
msgstr "Była promotorką pracy doktorskiej Deana DeLongchampa z 2003 roku o warstwach budowanych warstwa po warstwie z materiałów zmieniających barwę pod wpływem napięcia. Połączenie kilku takich materiałów dawało warstwy o wyższym kontraście, szybszym przełączaniu i więcej niż jednym kolorze."

#: people
#. About Paula Hammond, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.paula-hammond.about.3"
msgid "In 2002 she co-founded MIT's Institute for Soldier Nanotechnologies. Her group's work has included polymers for solar cells, nanoparticles that carry chemotherapy drugs and a spray coating that helps blood clot."
msgstr "W 2002 roku współzałożyła Institute for Soldier Nanotechnologies w MIT. Prace jej grupy obejmowały polimery do ogniw słonecznych, nanocząstki przenoszące leki chemioterapeutyczne i powłokę w sprayu pomagającą krzepnąć krwi."

#: people
#. About Paula Hammond, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.paula-hammond.about.4"
msgid "She was appointed head of MIT's Department of Chemical Engineering in 2015. The Science History Institute says she was the first woman and the first person of colour to hold that post. It gave her its Othmer Gold Medal in 2024."
msgstr "W 2015 roku została mianowana kierowniczką Wydziału Inżynierii Chemicznej MIT. Science History Institute podaje, że była pierwszą kobietą i pierwszą osobą o kolorze skóry innym niż biały na tym stanowisku. W 2024 roku instytut przyznał jej Othmer Gold Medal."

#: people
#. About Dean DeLongchamp, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.dean-delongchamp.about.1"
msgid "A chemical engineer, he took his doctorate at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology in 2003, with Paula Hammond as adviser."
msgstr "Inżynier chemik, w 2003 roku uzyskał doktorat w Massachusetts Institute of Technology, a jego promotorką była Paula Hammond."

#: people
#. About Dean DeLongchamp, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.dean-delongchamp.about.2"
msgid "His thesis also built polymer electrolyte films layer by layer that conducted ions well and held together mechanically, and it used nanocrystals of the Prussian blue family as electrochromic layers."
msgstr "W jego pracy doktorskiej powstawały też warstwa po warstwie polimerowe błony elektrolityczne, które dobrze przewodziły jony i były mechanicznie spójne, a jako warstwy elektrochromowe posłużyły w niej nanokryształy z rodziny błękitu pruskiego."

#: people
#. About Dean DeLongchamp, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.dean-delongchamp.about.3"
msgid "He moved to the National Institute of Standards and Technology as a postdoctoral fellow in 2003. He later led its Polymer Processing Group and specialised in soft X-ray spectroscopy and scattering. He received a Presidential Early Career Award in 2009."
msgstr "W 2003 roku przeszedł do National Institute of Standards and Technology jako stażysta podoktorski. Później kierował tam Polymer Processing Group i specjalizował się w spektroskopii i rozpraszaniu miękkiego promieniowania rentgenowskiego. W 2009 roku otrzymał Presidential Early Career Award."

#: people
#. About Henry Dircks, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.henry-dircks.about.1"
msgid "Born in Liverpool, he was apprenticed to a merchant house, worked as an engineer on railways, canals and mines, and then set up as a consulting engineer. He took out several patents between 1840 and 1857."
msgstr "Urodził się w Liverpoolu, terminował w domu kupieckim, pracował jako inżynier przy kolejach, kanałach i kopalniach, a następnie otworzył praktykę inżyniera konsultanta. W latach od 1840 do 1857 uzyskał kilka patentów."

#: people
#. About Henry Dircks, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.henry-dircks.about.2"
msgid "Grace's Guide dates his design of the ghost illusion to 1858. Theatre owners declined his models because their stages would have needed rebuilding. John Henry Pepper acquired one around 1862 and adapted it."
msgstr "Grace's Guide datuje jego projekt iluzji ducha na 1858 rok. Właściciele teatrów odrzucali jego modele, ponieważ ich sceny wymagałyby przebudowy. Około 1862 roku John Henry Pepper nabył jeden z nich i go przerobił."

#: people
#. About Henry Dircks, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.henry-dircks.about.3"
msgid "Pepper's book dates his first showing to just before Christmas 1862, the Linda Hall Library to late 1862 or early 1863. By Pepper's account, Pepper then had a provisional patent taken out in both their names. The letters patent were dated 5 February 1863."
msgstr "Książka Peppera datuje jego pierwszy pokaz na tuż przed Bożym Narodzeniem 1862 roku, a Linda Hall Library na koniec 1862 lub początek 1863 roku. Według relacji Peppera to Pepper zlecił następnie zgłoszenie tymczasowego patentu na nazwiska ich obu. Akt patentowy nosił datę 5 lutego 1863 roku."

#: people
#. About Henry Dircks, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.henry-dircks.about.4"
msgid "The library says they agreed that Pepper would take the profits and Dircks the credit, and that Pepper named only himself in public. Pepper wrote that he named Dircks daily as co-inventor. Dircks defended his claim in a book of 1863."
msgstr "Biblioteka podaje, że uzgodnili, iż Pepper weźmie zyski, a Dircks uznanie, oraz że Pepper publicznie wymieniał tylko siebie. Pepper pisał, że codziennie wymieniał Dircksa jako współwynalazcę. Dircks bronił swojego roszczenia w książce z 1863 roku."

#: people
#. About John Henry Pepper, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.john-henry-pepper.about.1"
msgid "A chemist and lecturer on popular science, he joined the staff of the Royal Polytechnic Institution in 1848 and was its director within ten years. He also wrote books, among them The Playbook of Metals."
msgstr "Chemik i wykładowca popularnonaukowy, w 1848 roku dołączył do Royal Polytechnic Institution i w ciągu dziesięciu lat został jej dyrektorem. Pisał też książki, między innymi The Playbook of Metals."

#: people
#. About John Henry Pepper, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.john-henry-pepper.about.2"
msgid "Around 1862 he acquired one of Henry Dircks's models and adapted it, hiding the second actor in the orchestra pit. By his own account he took out a provisional patent the day after his first showing, and at his own request it named them both."
msgstr "Około 1862 roku nabył jeden z modeli Henry'ego Dircksa i przerobił go, ukrywając drugiego aktora w kanale orkiestrowym. Według własnej relacji dzień po pierwszym pokazie zgłosił tymczasowy patent, który na jego własną prośbę wymieniał ich obu."

#: people
#. About John Henry Pepper, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.john-henry-pepper.about.3"
msgid "The letters patent were dated 5 February 1863. The Linda Hall Library dates the first showing to late 1862 or early 1863. It says the two agreed that Pepper would take the profits and Dircks the credit."
msgstr "Akt patentowy nosił datę 5 lutego 1863 roku. Linda Hall Library datuje pierwszy pokaz na koniec 1862 lub początek 1863 roku. Podaje, że obaj uzgodnili, iż Pepper weźmie zyski, a Dircks uznanie."

#: people
#. About John Henry Pepper, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.john-henry-pepper.about.4"
msgid "The library says Pepper used only his own name in public. Pepper wrote that he named Dircks as co-inventor every morning and evening. Dircks protested, the library says, and in 1863 published a book in his own defence."
msgstr "Biblioteka podaje, że Pepper publicznie posługiwał się tylko własnym nazwiskiem. Pepper pisał, że każdego ranka i wieczoru wymieniał Dircksa jako współwynalazcę. Według biblioteki Dircks protestował, a w 1863 roku opublikował książkę w swojej obronie."

#: people
#. About Valerie Thomas, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.valerie-thomas.about.1"
msgid "The Lemelson-MIT Program writes that her all-girls high school did not treat science as a subject for women, and that no one there encouraged her to take the advanced mathematics classes on offer."
msgstr "Lemelson-MIT Program pisze, że w jej szkole średniej dla dziewcząt nie traktowano nauk ścisłych jako przedmiotu dla kobiet i że nikt nie zachęcał jej tam do udziału w dostępnych zajęciach z matematyki na poziomie zaawansowanym."

#: people
#. About Valerie Thomas, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.valerie-thomas.about.2"
msgid "In 1976 she saw an exhibit where a concave mirror made a light bulb appear to glow in an empty socket. She wondered whether such an image could be transmitted, and began experiments with concave mirrors that year."
msgstr "W 1976 roku zobaczyła eksponat, w którym wklęsłe lustro sprawiało, że żarówka zdawała się świecić w pustej oprawce. Zastanawiała się, czy taki obraz można przesłać, i jeszcze w tym samym roku zaczęła eksperymenty z wklęsłymi lustrami."

#: people
#. About Valerie Thomas, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.valerie-thomas.about.3"
msgid "At NASA she managed the development of image processing systems for Landsat satellite data. She filed her patent for the illusion transmitter in December 1978, and it was granted in 1980. It used a parabolic mirror at each end."
msgstr "W NASA kierowała opracowaniem systemów przetwarzania obrazów dla danych z satelitów Landsat. W grudniu 1978 roku zgłosiła patent na przekaźnik iluzji, a patent udzielono jej w 1980 roku. Urządzenie wykorzystywało lustro paraboliczne na każdym końcu."

#: people
#. About Valerie Thomas, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.valerie-thomas.about.4"
msgid "She was later project manager of the Space Physics Analysis Network, and retired from NASA in 1995. NASA gave her its Equal Opportunity Medal. She also mentored young students through the National Technical Association."
msgstr "Później była kierowniczką projektu Space Physics Analysis Network, a w 1995 roku przeszła na emeryturę w NASA. NASA przyznała jej Equal Opportunity Medal. Była też mentorką młodzieży w ramach National Technical Association."

#: people
#. About Karri Palovuori, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.karri-palovuori.about.1"
msgid "A professor at Tampere University of Technology, he worked with Ismo Rakkolainen on the fog screen. The two had described a walk-through virtual environment at the IEEE Virtual Reality conference in Orlando in 2002."
msgstr "Jako profesor Politechniki w Tampere pracował z Ismo Rakkolainenem nad ekranem mgłowym. W 2002 roku obaj opisali na konferencji IEEE Virtual Reality w Orlando wirtualne środowisko, przez które można przejść."

#: people
#. About Karri Palovuori, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.karri-palovuori.about.2"
msgid "At Tampere University he worked in electronics and embedded systems, including the design of custom integrated circuits. His profile there lists more than ten patents."
msgstr "Na Uniwersytecie w Tampere zajmował się elektroniką i systemami wbudowanymi, w tym projektowaniem specjalizowanych układów scalonych. Jego profil na uczelni wymienia ponad dziesięć patentów."

#: people
#. About Ismo Rakkolainen, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ismo-rakkolainen.about.1"
msgid "A senior researcher in the Technology Signal Processing Laboratory at Tampere University of Technology, he worked with Karri Palovuori to create the fog screen."
msgstr "Jako starszy badacz w Technology Signal Processing Laboratory na Politechnice w Tampere stworzył wspólnie z Karrim Palovuorim ekran mgłowy."

#: people
#. About Ismo Rakkolainen, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ismo-rakkolainen.about.2"
msgid "During the 1990s he built early prototypes in his living room from plastic drinking straws, with air pushed up through small nozzles from below."
msgstr "W latach dziewięćdziesiątych budował w swoim salonie wczesne prototypy z plastikowych słomek do picia, a powietrze tłoczono w górę przez małe dysze od spodu."

#: people
#. About Ismo Rakkolainen, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ismo-rakkolainen.about.3"
msgid "The Lemelson-MIT Program dates the first showing to the Turku Science Exhibition in Finland in autumn 2002. The screen was shown at the SIGGRAPH computer graphics conference in San Diego in 2003. FogScreen Inc was founded in 2003 to make and sell it."
msgstr "Lemelson-MIT Program datuje pierwszy pokaz na Turku Science Exhibition w Finlandii jesienią 2002 roku. Ekran pokazano na konferencji grafiki komputerowej SIGGRAPH w San Diego w 2003 roku. W 2003 roku założono FogScreen Inc, by go produkować i sprzedawać."

#: people
#. About Ismo Rakkolainen, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ismo-rakkolainen.about.4"
msgid "He stayed at Tampere University as a university research fellow and adjunct professor in the TAUCHI Research Center, working on user interfaces, virtual reality and new displays."
msgstr "Pozostał na Uniwersytecie w Tampere jako badacz uniwersytecki i docent w TAUCHI Research Center, zajmując się interfejsami użytkownika, rzeczywistością wirtualną i nowymi wyświetlaczami."

#: people
#. About Max Hirsch, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.max-hirsch.about.1"
msgid "He filed the patent in January 1958 in his own name, with no company named as assignee. A cathode-ray tube and its lenses and mirrors turned together with a rear-projection screen, spun by a motor at more than twenty turns a second."
msgstr "W styczniu 1958 roku zgłosił patent na własne nazwisko, bez wskazania firmy jako cesjonariusza. Lampa kineskopowa wraz z soczewkami i lustrami obracała się razem z ekranem do projekcji tylnej, napędzana silnikiem z prędkością ponad dwudziestu obrotów na sekundę."

#: people
#. About Max Hirsch, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.max-hirsch.about.2"
msgid "A second patent, filed in November 1958 and granted in April 1961, let the tube stay still while circuits turned the picture on its face in step with the screen."
msgstr "Drugi patent, zgłoszony w listopadzie 1958 roku i udzielony w kwietniu 1961 roku, pozwalał, by lampa pozostawała nieruchoma, a układy elektroniczne obracały obraz na jej przedniej powierzchni synchronicznie z ekranem."

#: people
#. About Gregg Favalora, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.gregg-favalora.about.1"
msgid "He built his display as his final year project at Yale University in 1996, with laser beams reflected onto a fast rotating screen. He developed it further as a doctoral student in electrical engineering at Harvard, and was on leave by 1998."
msgstr "W 1996 roku zbudował swój wyświetlacz jako projekt dyplomowy na ostatnim roku studiów na Uniwersytecie Yale, z wiązkami laserowymi odbijanymi na szybko obracający się ekran. Rozwijał go dalej jako doktorant elektrotechniki na Uniwersytecie Harvarda, a w 1998 roku był już na urlopie."

#: people
#. About Gregg Favalora, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.gregg-favalora.about.2"
msgid "He co-founded Actuality Systems with two Harvard students, Michael J. Giovinco and Shawn T. Samuel, and won the MIT $50K Entrepreneurship Competition in 1997. MIT Technology Review named him among its innovators under 35 in 1999."
msgstr "Firmę Actuality Systems współzałożyli on i dwie osoby studiujące na Harvardzie, Michael J. Giovinco i Shawn T. Samuel. W 1997 roku wygrał MIT $50K Entrepreneurship Competition. W 1999 roku MIT Technology Review umieścił go wśród innowatorów przed 35. rokiem życia."

#: people
#. About Gregg Favalora, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.gregg-favalora.about.3"
msgid "In 2009 he joined Optics for Hire, an optical design consultancy in Arlington, Massachusetts. By 2011 he was named on nine United States patents."
msgstr "W 2009 roku dołączył do Optics for Hire, firmy konsultingowej zajmującej się projektowaniem optyki w Arlington w stanie Massachusetts. Do 2011 roku jego nazwisko widniało na dziewięciu patentach amerykańskich."

#: people
#. About Elizabeth Downing, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.elizabeth-downing.about.1"
msgid "Before Stanford she worked as an engineer on laser equipment at the FMC Corporation Technology Center in Santa Clara, California."
msgstr "Przed studiami na Uniwersytecie Stanforda pracowała jako inżynierka przy sprzęcie laserowym w FMC Corporation Technology Center w Santa Clara w Kalifornii."

#: people
#. About Elizabeth Downing, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.elizabeth-downing.about.2"
msgid "As a graduate student she spent eight years on the display, with borrowed laboratory space and donated lasers. It had a United States Navy grant of 350,000 dollars. The prototype cube was a stack of three doped glass layers, one for each primary colour."
msgstr "Na studiach podyplomowych poświęciła wyświetlaczowi osiem lat, korzystając z pożyczonej przestrzeni laboratoryjnej i podarowanych laserów. Projekt miał grant Marynarki Wojennej Stanów Zjednoczonych w wysokości 350 000 dolarów. Prototypowa kostka składała się z trzech warstw domieszkowanego szkła, po jednej dla każdej barwy podstawowej."

#: people
#. About Elizabeth Downing, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.elizabeth-downing.about.3"
msgid "She set up 3D Technology Laboratories in Mountain View, California, to sell the patented device, and by 1997 was planning a larger cube of many thin layers."
msgstr "Założyła 3D Technology Laboratories w Mountain View w Kalifornii, by sprzedawać opatentowane urządzenie, a w 1997 roku planowała już większą kostkę z wielu cienkich warstw."

#: people
#. About Lambertus Hesselink, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.lambertus-hesselink.about.1"
msgid "He studied applied physics and mechanics at Twente University and took his doctorate at the California Institute of Technology in 1977. At Stanford University he became professor of electrical engineering. Elizabeth Downing continued her display research with him there from 1988."
msgstr "Studiował fizykę stosowaną i mechanikę na Uniwersytecie Twente, a w 1977 roku uzyskał doktorat w California Institute of Technology. Na Uniwersytecie Stanforda został profesorem elektrotechniki. Od 1988 roku Elizabeth Downing kontynuowała tam u niego badania nad swoim wyświetlaczem."

#: people
#. About Lambertus Hesselink, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.lambertus-hesselink.about.2"
msgid "His research covered ultra high density optical data storage, nonlinear optics and nanophotonics. He founded Siros Technologies in 1997 and co-founded Senvid in 1999. The National Academy of Inventors made him a fellow in 2022."
msgstr "Jego badania obejmowały optyczny zapis danych o ultrawysokiej gęstości, optykę nieliniową i nanofotonikę. W 1997 roku założył Siros Technologies, a w 1999 roku współzałożył Senvid. W 2022 roku National Academy of Inventors nadała mu tytuł fellow."

#: people
#. About John Ralston, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 1. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.john-ralston.about.1"
msgid "In 1996 he worked at SDL, a laser maker in San Jose, California, which supplied the small high power lasers used to draw points inside the glass. He was one of the four authors of the paper in Science."
msgstr "W 1996 roku pracował w SDL, producencie laserów w San Jose w Kalifornii, który dostarczał małe lasery dużej mocy używane do rysowania punktów wewnątrz szkła. Był jednym z czterech autorów artykułu w Science."

#: people
#. About Roger Macfarlane, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.roger-macfarlane.about.1"
msgid "A physicist at the IBM Almaden Research Center, he studied how atoms and molecules behave in solids, with a view to storing data at very high density."
msgstr "Jako fizyk w IBM Almaden Research Center badał, jak atomy i cząsteczki zachowują się w ciałach stałych, z myślą o zapisie danych o bardzo dużej gęstości."

#: people
#. About Roger Macfarlane, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.roger-macfarlane.about.2"
msgid "He was one of the four authors of the paper in Science of 1996 on the three colour display, which drew its light from glass doped with rare earth elements. IBM Research lists the paper among its publications."
msgstr "Był jednym z czterech autorów artykułu w Science z 1996 roku o trójbarwnym wyświetlaczu, którego światło pochodziło ze szkła domieszkowanego pierwiastkami ziem rzadkich. IBM Research wymienia ten artykuł wśród swoich publikacji."

#: people
#. About Roger Macfarlane, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.roger-macfarlane.about.3"
msgid "His papers included laser spectroscopy of rare earth ions in crystals, and in 1985 a report of spectral hole burning in such a crystal. He was still publishing on rare earth doped materials in 2013."
msgstr "Wśród jego prac była spektroskopia laserowa jonów ziem rzadkich w kryształach, a w 1985 roku opis wypalania dziur spektralnych w takim krysztale. W 2013 roku wciąż publikował prace o materiałach domieszkowanych pierwiastkami ziem rzadkich."

#: people
#. About Daniel Smalley, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.daniel-smalley.about.1"
msgid "He studied at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology, with a degree in electrical engineering in 2005 and a doctorate in holography in 2013. At MIT he worked on a low cost holographic video monitor."
msgstr "Studiował w Massachusetts Institute of Technology, gdzie w 2005 roku uzyskał dyplom z elektrotechniki, a w 2013 roku doktorat z holografii. W MIT pracował nad tanim holograficznym monitorem wideo."

#: people
#. About Daniel Smalley, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.daniel-smalley.about.2"
msgid "At Brigham Young University he became professor of electrical and computer engineering. In the display, lasers trapped and heated a single cellulose particle and steered it through the air while red, green and blue light lit it."
msgstr "Na Brigham Young University został profesorem elektrotechniki i inżynierii komputerowej. W wyświetlaczu lasery chwytały i nagrzewały pojedynczą cząstkę celulozy i prowadziły ją w powietrzu, a oświetlało ją światło czerwone, zielone i niebieskie."

#: people
#. About Ryuji Hirayama, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ryuji-hirayama.about.1"
msgid "He studied engineering at Chiba University in Japan and took his doctorate there in 2017, with a thesis on volumetric displays that hold several flat images. He then held research fellowships from the Japan Society for the Promotion of Science."
msgstr "Studiował inżynierię na Uniwersytecie Chiba w Japonii i tam w 2017 roku uzyskał doktorat na podstawie rozprawy o wyświetlaczach objętościowych mieszczących kilka płaskich obrazów. Następnie otrzymywał stypendia badawcze Japan Society for the Promotion of Science."

#: people
#. About Ryuji Hirayama, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ryuji-hirayama.about.2"
msgid "One of those fellowships took him in 2018 to the laboratory of Nobuyuki Masuda at Tokyo University of Science. In 2019 he joined the Interact Lab at the University of Sussex as a Rutherford Fellow, and was lead author of the paper in Nature."
msgstr "Jedno z tych stypendiów zaprowadziło go w 2018 roku do laboratorium Nobuyukiego Masudy na Tokyo University of Science. W 2019 roku dołączył do Interact Lab na Uniwersytecie Sussex jako Rutherford Fellow i był głównym autorem artykułu w Nature."

#: people
#. About Ryuji Hirayama, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ryuji-hirayama.about.3"
msgid "He moved to the computer science department of University College London in 2020, became a lecturer in 2022 and an associate professor in 2026. He leads FabDisp, a project on acoustic holography for display and fabrication, and co-founded the company AcoustoFab in 2023."
msgstr "W 2020 roku przeszedł na wydział informatyki University College London, w 2022 roku został wykładowcą, a w 2026 roku profesorem nadzwyczajnym. Kieruje FabDisp, projektem poświęconym holografii akustycznej w wyświetlaniu i wytwarzaniu, a w 2023 roku współzałożył firmę AcoustoFab."

#: people
#. About Diego Martinez Plasencia, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.diego-martinez-plasencia.about.1"
msgid "He was an assistant lecturer at a university in Spain and a research associate at the University of Bristol before becoming a lecturer in interactive 3D graphics at the University of Sussex. He later moved to University College London as an associate professor."
msgstr "Był asystentem na uczelni w Hiszpanii i pracownikiem naukowym Uniwersytetu w Bristolu, zanim został wykładowcą interaktywnej grafiki 3D na Uniwersytecie Sussex. Później przeszedł na University College London jako profesor nadzwyczajny."

#: people
#. About Diego Martinez Plasencia, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.diego-martinez-plasencia.about.2"
msgid "The University of Sussex named him co-creator of the Multimodal Acoustic Trap Display. He explained that it directed and focused ultrasound, which could stimulate the ears for sound or the skin for touch."
msgstr "Uniwersytet Sussex wskazał go jako współtwórcę multimodalnego wyświetlacza z pułapką akustyczną. Wyjaśniał, że urządzenie kierowało i ogniskowało ultradźwięki, które mogły pobudzać uszy, dając dźwięk, albo skórę, dając wrażenie dotyku."

#: people
#. About Diego Martinez Plasencia, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.diego-martinez-plasencia.about.3"
msgid "At University College London he co-founded the Multi-Sensory Devices Group with Marianna Obrist and Sriram Subramanian. He worked on 3D displays, from tabletop systems with several views to displays made of moving particles."
msgstr "Na University College London współzałożył Multi-Sensory Devices Group, a pozostałymi współzałożycielami byli Marianna Obrist i Sriram Subramanian. Zajmował się wyświetlaczami 3D, od systemów stołowych z kilkoma widokami po wyświetlacze z poruszających się cząstek."

#: people
#. About Nobuyuki Masuda, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.nobuyuki-masuda.about.1"
msgid "He was a professor of applied electronics at Tokyo University of Science, where his laboratory designed special purpose computing circuits on programmable chips (FPGAs) and used graphics processors to speed up numerical work, much of it for computer generated holograms."
msgstr "Był profesorem elektroniki stosowanej na Tokyo University of Science, gdzie jego laboratorium projektowało specjalizowane układy obliczeniowe w układach programowalnych (FPGA) i wykorzystywało procesory graficzne do przyspieszania obliczeń numerycznych, w dużej mierze na potrzeby hologramów generowanych komputerowo."

#: people
#. About Nobuyuki Masuda, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.nobuyuki-masuda.about.2"
msgid "From 2018 to 2021 he led a project that built a dedicated FPGA computer for digital holography, which his team reported to be faster than a PC. Ryuji Hirayama worked in his laboratory as a research fellow in 2018 before going to Sussex."
msgstr "W latach od 2018 do 2021 kierował projektem, w którym powstał dedykowany komputer FPGA do holografii cyfrowej, według jego zespołu szybszy od komputera PC. Ryuji Hirayama pracował w jego laboratorium jako stypendysta badawczy w 2018 roku, zanim przeniósł się na Sussex."

#: people
#. About Sriram Subramanian, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.sriram-subramanian.about.1"
msgid "When the display was published he was Professor of Informatics at Sussex and held a Royal Academy of Engineering Chair in Emerging Technologies. The university named him as leader of the project."
msgstr "Gdy wyświetlacz opublikowano, był profesorem informatyki na Uniwersytecie Sussex i zajmował katedrę Royal Academy of Engineering Chair in Emerging Technologies. Uczelnia wskazała go jako kierownika projektu."

#: people
#. About Sriram Subramanian, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.sriram-subramanian.about.2"
msgid "He moved to University College London, where he leads the Multi-Sensory Devices Group, co-founded with Diego Martinez Plasencia and Marianna Obrist. It works on touch in mid air, levitation and contactless control by ultrasound."
msgstr "Przeszedł na University College London, gdzie kieruje Multi-Sensory Devices Group, której współzałożycielami są on, Diego Martinez Plasencia i Marianna Obrist. Grupa zajmuje się dotykiem w powietrzu, lewitacją i bezdotykowym sterowaniem za pomocą ultradźwięków."

#: people
#. About Sriram Subramanian, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.sriram-subramanian.about.3"
msgid "University College London says his early hardware designs led to the company Ultrahaptics, now Ultraleap. He founded Metasonixx and co-founded AcoustoFab. The university reported his election as a Fellow of the Royal Academy of Engineering in 2025."
msgstr "University College London podaje, że jego wczesne projekty sprzętowe dały początek firmie Ultrahaptics, obecnie Ultraleap. Założył Metasonixx i współzałożył AcoustoFab. Uczelnia poinformowała o jego wyborze na członka (Fellow) Royal Academy of Engineering w 2025 roku."

#: people
#. About Yoichi Ochiai, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.yoichi-ochiai.about.1"
msgid "He studied information media at the University of Tsukuba and took a doctorate in applied computer science at the University of Tokyo in 2015. He then joined Tsukuba's Institute of Library, Information and Media Science, as assistant professor and from 2017 associate professor."
msgstr "Studiował media informacyjne na Uniwersytecie Tsukuba, a w 2015 roku uzyskał doktorat z informatyki stosowanej na Uniwersytecie Tokijskim. Następnie dołączył do Institute of Library, Information and Media Science w Tsukubie jako adiunkt, a od 2017 roku był tam profesorem nadzwyczajnym."

#: people
#. About Yoichi Ochiai, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.yoichi-ochiai.about.2"
msgid "The femtosecond display, called Fairy Lights in Femtoseconds, was shown at SIGGRAPH 2015 with colleagues from Utsunomiya University, the Nagoya Institute of Technology, the University of Tokyo and Sony CSL. The team argued that plasma from femtosecond pulses was safer than from nanosecond pulses."
msgstr "Wyświetlacz femtosekundowy o nazwie Fairy Lights in Femtoseconds pokazano na SIGGRAPH 2015 wraz ze współpracownikami z Utsunomiya University, Nagoya Institute of Technology, Uniwersytetu Tokijskiego i Sony CSL. Zespół dowodził, że plazma z impulsów femtosekundowych jest bezpieczniejsza niż z impulsów nanosekundowych."

#: people
#. About Yoichi Ochiai, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.yoichi-ochiai.about.3"
msgid "He was also chief executive of Pixie Dust Technologies from 2015 and director of Tsukuba's Research and Development Center for Digital Nature from 2020. MIT Technology Review listed him among its Innovators Under 35 for Japan in 2020."
msgstr "Od 2015 roku był też prezesem Pixie Dust Technologies, a od 2020 roku dyrektorem Research and Development Center for Digital Nature w Tsukubie. W 2020 roku MIT Technology Review umieścił go na liście Innovators Under 35 dla Japonii."

#: people
#. About Charles Wheatstone, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.charles-wheatstone.about.1"
msgid "Born near Gloucester, he moved with his family to London and was apprenticed to his uncle's firm of musical instrument makers. In 1834 King's College London made him Professor of Experimental Philosophy."
msgstr "Urodził się niedaleko Gloucester, przeniósł się z rodziną do Londynu i terminował w należącej do wuja firmie wytwarzającej instrumenty muzyczne. W 1834 roku King's College London mianował go profesorem filozofii eksperymentalnej."

#: people
#. About Charles Wheatstone, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.charles-wheatstone.about.2"
msgid "His paper on the stereoscope, Contributions to the Physiology of Vision, appeared in the Philosophical Transactions of the Royal Society. He drew simple line figures to view in it and, in 1840, asked William Henry Fox Talbot for stereoscopic photographs."
msgstr "Jego artykuł o stereoskopie, Contributions to the Physiology of Vision, ukazał się w Philosophical Transactions of the Royal Society. Rysował proste figury z linii do oglądania w nim, a w 1840 roku poprosił Williama Henry'ego Foxa Talbota o fotografie stereoskopowe."

#: people
#. About Charles Wheatstone, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.charles-wheatstone.about.3"
msgid "With William Fothergill Cooke he worked on the electric telegraph, and the Royal Society dates its installation on the Great Western Railway to 1838. He also gave his name to the Wheatstone Bridge for measuring electrical resistance, and was knighted in 1868."
msgstr "Razem z Williamem Fothergillem Cooke'em pracował nad telegrafem elektrycznym, a Royal Society datuje jego instalację na Great Western Railway na 1838 rok. Od jego nazwiska pochodzi też nazwa mostka Wheatstone'a do pomiaru oporu elektrycznego, a w 1868 roku otrzymał tytuł szlachecki."

#: people
#. About Kenneth Dunkley, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.kenneth-dunkley.about.1"
msgid "He took a master's degree in physics and became president of Holospace Laboratories in Camp Hill, Pennsylvania. For several years he ran visual effects workshops at the Museum of Scientific Discovery in Harrisburg, and worked on holography, lasers and electro optics."
msgstr "Uzyskał tytuł magistra fizyki i został prezesem Holospace Laboratories w Camp Hill w Pensylwanii. Przez kilka lat prowadził warsztaty efektów wizualnych w Museum of Scientific Discovery w Harrisburgu i zajmował się holografią, laserami i elektrooptyką."

#: people
#. About Kenneth Dunkley, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.kenneth-dunkley.about.2"
msgid "The National Business League says the idea came while he was demonstrating holography at the Franklin Institute, when tubes with pinholes gave a flat photograph depth. He filed the patent in April 1986. Its pinholes and frames can be moved apart or together."
msgstr "National Business League podaje, że pomysł przyszedł mu do głowy, gdy pokazywał holografię w Franklin Institute, a rurki z otworkami nadały płaskiej fotografii głębię. W kwietniu 1986 roku zgłosił patent. Jego otworki i ramki można od siebie oddalać lub do siebie przybliżać."

#: people
#. About Charles Harrison, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.charles-harrison.about.1"
msgid "Born in Shreveport, Louisiana, he took a degree in industrial design at the School of the Art Institute of Chicago in 1954, served in the United States Army as a mapmaker in Germany, and later earned a master's in art education at night."
msgstr "Urodził się w Shreveport w stanie Luizjana, w 1954 roku ukończył wzornictwo przemysłowe w School of the Art Institute of Chicago, służył w Armii Stanów Zjednoczonych jako kartograf w Niemczech, a później wieczorowo zdobył tytuł magistra edukacji artystycznej."

#: people
#. About Charles Harrison, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.charles-harrison.about.2"
msgid "He took the View-Master job as a freelance designer through Robert Podall Associates, for the maker Sawyer's. He said moulding it in thermoplastic rather than Bakelite would make units ten times faster. The Henry Ford says it took him under two weeks."
msgstr "Zlecenie na View-Master przyjął jako niezależny projektant za pośrednictwem Robert Podall Associates, dla producenta, firmy Sawyer's. Mówił, że formowanie go z termoplastu zamiast z bakelitu pozwoli wytwarzać egzemplarze dziesięć razy szybciej. The Henry Ford podaje, że zajęło mu to niecałe dwa tygodnie."

#: people
#. About Charles Harrison, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.charles-harrison.about.3"
msgid "The Henry Ford records that the design manager at Sears, Roebuck and Company told him of an unwritten policy against hiring Black people, and hired him as a freelancer instead. In 1961 Sears made him a staff designer."
msgstr "The Henry Ford odnotowuje, że osoba kierująca wzornictwem w Sears, Roebuck and Company powiedziała mu o niepisanej zasadzie niezatrudniania osób czarnoskórych i zamiast tego zatrudniła go jako wolnego strzelca. W 1961 roku Sears przyjął go na etat projektanta."

#: people
#. About Charles Harrison, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.charles-harrison.about.4"
msgid "The Henry Ford calls him the first Black executive at Sears headquarters. He became chief of design, and Cooper Hewitt credits him with over 750 products. He retired in 1993, taught in Chicago, and won the National Design Award for Lifetime Achievement in 2008."
msgstr "The Henry Ford nazywa go pierwszym czarnoskórym członkiem kadry kierowniczej w centrali Sears. Został szefem działu wzornictwa, a Cooper Hewitt przypisuje mu ponad 750 produktów. W 1993 roku przeszedł na emeryturę, uczył w Chicago, a w 2008 roku otrzymał National Design Award for Lifetime Achievement."

#: people
#. About Frederic Ives, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.frederic-ives.about.1"
msgid "Born in Litchfield, Connecticut, he was apprenticed as a boy to a printer and, with no formal schooling, was put in charge of the photographic laboratory at Cornell University while still a teenager."
msgstr "Urodził się w Litchfield w stanie Connecticut. Jako chłopiec terminował u drukarza i bez formalnego wykształcenia, jeszcze jako nastolatek, otrzymał kierownictwo laboratorium fotograficznego Uniwersytetu Cornella."

#: people
#. About Frederic Ives, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.frederic-ives.about.2"
msgid "There he worked out a halftone process for printing photographs, in commercial use by 1881, and a crossline screen. He later made the Kromskop, for colour stereo pictures from three pairs of filtered negatives. He held about seventy patents."
msgstr "Tam opracował rastrową metodę druku fotografii, stosowaną komercyjnie już w 1881 roku, oraz raster krzyżowy. Później stworzył Kromskop do kolorowych obrazów stereoskopowych z trzech par negatywów wykonanych przez filtry. Miał około siedemdziesięciu patentów."

#: people
#. About Frederic Ives, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.frederic-ives.about.3"
msgid "Living in Philadelphia, he filed his patent for the parallax stereogram in September 1902 and was granted it in April 1903. A screen of opaque lines with clear spaces, set at a calculated distance, let each eye see only its own picture."
msgstr "Mieszkając w Filadelfii, we wrześniu 1902 roku zgłosił patent na stereogram paralaksowy i uzyskał go w kwietniu 1903 roku. Ekran z nieprzezroczystych linii z przezroczystymi przerwami, umieszczony w obliczonej odległości, pozwalał każdemu oku widzieć tylko jego własny obraz."

#: people
#. About Walter Hess, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.walter-hess.about.1"
msgid "Born in Frauenfeld, Switzerland, he studied medicine at Lausanne, Berlin, Kiel and Zurich and qualified in 1906. He trained in ophthalmology for two years under Otto Haab in Zurich before opening his practice."
msgstr "Urodził się we Frauenfeld w Szwajcarii, studiował medycynę w Lozannie, Berlinie, Kilonii i Zurychu, a dyplom lekarza uzyskał w 1906 roku. Przez dwa lata kształcił się w okulistyce pod kierunkiem Otto Haaba w Zurychu, zanim otworzył własny gabinet."

#: people
#. About Walter Hess, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.walter-hess.about.2"
msgid "His patent described two stereoscopic negatives printed in strips behind a celluloid plate of cylindrical ribs, so no stereoscope or spectacles were needed. C. W. Hess says his plans to sell it came to nothing when the First World War broke out."
msgstr "Jego patent opisywał dwa negatywy stereoskopowe wydrukowane w paskach za celuloidową płytą z cylindrycznymi żeberkami, dzięki czemu nie był potrzebny stereoskop ani okulary. C. W. Hess podaje, że jego plany sprzedaży spełzły na niczym, gdy wybuchła pierwsza wojna światowa."

#: people
#. About Walter Hess, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.walter-hess.about.3"
msgid "In 1912 he joined the Physiological Institute of the University of Zurich, and in 1917 became its professor and head, until 1951. He shared the Nobel Prize with Egas Moniz, for work on the diencephalon as a centre coordinating the internal organs."
msgstr "W 1912 roku podjął pracę w Instytucie Fizjologii Uniwersytetu w Zurychu, a w 1917 roku został jego profesorem i kierownikiem i pozostał nim do 1951 roku. Nagrodę Nobla otrzymał wspólnie z Egasem Monizem za prace nad międzymózgowiem jako ośrodkiem koordynującym narządy wewnętrzne."

#: people
#. About Hank Willis Thomas, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.hank-willis-thomas.about.1"
msgid "He took a degree in fine art at New York University in 1998 and a master's at California College of the Arts in 2004. He began as a photographer and later made sculpture and installations."
msgstr "W 1998 roku uzyskał dyplom ze sztuk pięknych na New York University, a w 2004 roku tytuł magistra w California College of the Arts. Zaczynał jako fotograf, później tworzył rzeźby i instalacje."

#: people
#. About Hank Willis Thomas, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.hank-willis-thomas.about.2"
msgid "Art21 says his work turns on perception and perspective and on brands, logos and icons, and honours the history of Black Americans. In Freedom Riders on Colors for a Large Wall, of 2021, he printed portraits of civil rights activists on coloured retroreflective vinyl."
msgstr "Art21 podaje, że jego twórczość dotyczy percepcji i perspektywy oraz marek, logo i ikon, a także oddaje hołd historii czarnoskórych Amerykanów. W pracy Freedom Riders on Colors for a Large Wall z 2021 roku wydrukował portrety działaczy na rzecz praw obywatelskich na kolorowej folii odblaskowej."

#: people
#. About Hank Willis Thomas, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.hank-willis-thomas.about.3"
msgid "Two of his lenticular prints of 2017, They are Us, Us is Them and Impossibly, hang in Harvey Milk Terminal 1 at San Francisco International Airport. In the second, the words possible, possibly and impossible take turns as the viewer moves."
msgstr "Dwa jego druki lentikularne z 2017 roku, They are Us, Us is Them oraz Impossibly, wiszą w Harvey Milk Terminal 1 na międzynarodowym lotnisku w San Francisco. Na drugim z nich słowa possible, possibly i impossible pojawiają się na zmianę w miarę ruchu osoby oglądającej."

#: people
#. About Dennis Gabor, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.dennis-gabor.about.1"
msgid "Born in Budapest, he studied electrical engineering in Berlin, taking a doctorate in 1927, and then worked in research at Siemens and Halske. In 1934 he joined the British Thomson-Houston Company at Rugby."
msgstr "Urodził się w Budapeszcie, studiował elektrotechnikę w Berlinie, gdzie w 1927 roku uzyskał doktorat, a następnie pracował w dziale badań Siemens and Halske. W 1934 roku zaczął pracę w British Thomson-Houston Company w Rugby."

#: people
#. About Dennis Gabor, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.dennis-gabor.about.2"
msgid "In his Nobel lecture he said the aim was a better electron microscope, sharp enough to resolve atomic lattices. His early optical trials used a mercury lamp, whose short coherence kept objects small. He dated the method's revival, with the laser, to 1963."
msgstr "W wykładzie noblowskim mówił, że celem był lepszy mikroskop elektronowy, na tyle ostry, by rozróżniać sieci atomowe. Jego wczesne próby optyczne wykorzystywały lampę rtęciową, której krótka spójność ograniczała rozmiar obiektów. Odrodzenie metody, dzięki laserowi, datował na 1963 rok."

#: people
#. About Dennis Gabor, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.dennis-gabor.about.3"
msgid "From 1949 to 1967 he taught at Imperial College London, where he became professor of applied electron physics. The Nobel Prize in Physics of 1971 credits him with the invention and development of the holographic method."
msgstr "W latach od 1949 do 1967 wykładał w Imperial College London, gdzie został profesorem stosowanej fizyki elektronowej. Nagroda Nobla w dziedzinie fizyki z 1971 roku przypisuje mu wynalezienie i rozwinięcie metody holograficznej."

#: people
#. About Emmett Leith, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.emmett-leith.about.1"
msgid "Born in Detroit, he studied physics at Wayne State University. In 1952 he joined the Radar Laboratory of the University of Michigan's Willow Run Laboratories, where he worked on synthetic aperture radar."
msgstr "Urodził się w Detroit i studiował fizykę na Wayne State University. W 1952 roku dołączył do Radar Laboratory w Willow Run Laboratories Uniwersytetu Michigan, gdzie pracował nad radarem z syntetyczną aperturą."

#: people
#. About Emmett Leith, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.emmett-leith.about.2"
msgid "He brought Juris Upatnieks onto the holography work in 1960. They called their method lensless photography, and showed a hologram of a toy train at a meeting of the Optical Society of America in 1964."
msgstr "W 1960 roku włączył Jurisa Upatnieksa do prac nad holografią. Swoją metodę nazwali fotografią bezsoczewkową, a w 1964 roku na spotkaniu Optical Society of America pokazali hologram zabawkowej kolejki."

#: people
#. About Emmett Leith, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.emmett-leith.about.3"
msgid "He became a full professor at Michigan in 1968 and received the National Medal of Science in 1979. The Optical Society of America named a medal after him in 2006."
msgstr "W 1968 roku został profesorem zwyczajnym na Uniwersytecie Michigan, a w 1979 roku otrzymał National Medal of Science. W 2006 roku Optical Society of America nazwało jego imieniem medal."

#: people
#. About Juris Upatnieks, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.juris-upatnieks.about.1"
msgid "Born in Riga, he left Latvia in 1944 and reached the United States in 1951. He took a degree in electrical engineering at the University of Akron in 1960."
msgstr "Urodził się w Rydze, w 1944 roku opuścił Łotwę, a w 1951 roku dotarł do Stanów Zjednoczonych. W 1960 roku uzyskał dyplom z elektrotechniki na University of Akron."

#: people
#. About Juris Upatnieks, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.juris-upatnieks.about.2"
msgid "Emmett Leith recruited him that year to Willow Run Laboratories at the University of Michigan. The two patented their holography work jointly as Wavefront Reconstruction Using a Coherent Reference Beam."
msgstr "W tym samym roku Emmett Leith zwerbował go do Willow Run Laboratories na Uniwersytecie Michigan. Obaj wspólnie opatentowali swoje prace nad holografią jako Wavefront Reconstruction Using a Coherent Reference Beam."

#: people
#. About Juris Upatnieks, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.juris-upatnieks.about.3"
msgid "From 1973 to 1993 he worked at the University of Michigan, at the Environmental Research Institute and then in electrical and computer engineering. He held 19 United States patents and received the Emmett N. Leith Medal in 2010."
msgstr "W latach od 1973 do 1993 pracował na Uniwersytecie Michigan, najpierw w Environmental Research Institute, a potem w dziedzinie elektrotechniki i informatyki. Miał 19 patentów amerykańskich, a w 2010 roku otrzymał Emmett N. Leith Medal."

#: people
#. About Margaret Benyon, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.margaret-benyon.about.1"
msgid "Trained as a painter, she began making holograms in 1968, when, the Center for the Holographic Arts says, holography was available only to scientists. Her stated aim was to take it out of the science laboratory and widen what counted as fine art."
msgstr "Z wykształcenia malarka, zaczęła tworzyć hologramy w 1968 roku, gdy, jak podaje Center for the Holographic Arts, holografia była dostępna tylko dla naukowców. Jej deklarowanym celem było wyprowadzenie holografii z laboratorium naukowego i poszerzenie granic tego, co uznawano za sztuki piękne."

#: people
#. About Margaret Benyon, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.margaret-benyon.about.2"
msgid "She lived in Australia in the 1970s. After she returned to Britain in 1980, her holograms dealt with the human body. For 23 years she made most of them in a simple home studio on the south coast of England."
msgstr "W latach siedemdziesiątych mieszkała w Australii. Po powrocie do Wielkiej Brytanii w 1980 roku tworzyła hologramy poświęcone ludzkiemu ciału. Przez 23 lata wykonywała większość z nich w prostej domowej pracowni na południowym wybrzeżu Anglii."

#: people
#. About Margaret Benyon, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.margaret-benyon.about.3"
msgid "Tigirl, of 1985, set a holographic self portrait against a photograph of a tiger. In 1994 the Royal College of Art in London awarded her a doctorate for research in art holography."
msgstr "Praca Tigirl z 1985 roku zestawiała holograficzny autoportret z fotografią tygrysa. W 1994 roku Royal College of Art w Londynie nadał jej doktorat za badania w dziedzinie holografii artystycznej."

#: people
#. About Margaret Benyon, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.margaret-benyon.about.4"
msgid "She was appointed MBE in the New Year Honours of 2000, for services to art, and her work is in the Victoria and Albert Museum and the Australian National Gallery. She was an honorary visiting fellow at the University of New South Wales."
msgstr "W 2000 roku, w noworocznej liście odznaczeń, otrzymała Order Imperium Brytyjskiego klasy MBE za zasługi dla sztuki, a jej prace znajdują się w zbiorach Victoria and Albert Museum i Australian National Gallery. Na University of New South Wales była honorowym gościem naukowym."

#: people
#. About Stephen Benton, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.stephen-benton.about.1"
msgid "Born in San Francisco, he studied electrical engineering at MIT, working with Harold Edgerton, and as a student worked in Edwin Land's vision research laboratory at Polaroid. He took his doctorate at Harvard in 1968."
msgstr "Urodził się w San Francisco, studiował elektrotechnikę w MIT, współpracując z Haroldem Edgertonem, a jako student pracował w laboratorium badań nad widzeniem Edwina Landa w firmie Polaroid. W 1968 roku uzyskał doktorat na Uniwersytecie Harvarda."

#: people
#. About Stephen Benton, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.stephen-benton.about.2"
msgid "MIT News credits him with inventing rainbow holography, which lets a hologram be seen in ordinary white light."
msgstr "MIT News przypisuje mu wynalezienie holografii tęczowej, która pozwala oglądać hologram w zwykłym białym świetle."

#: people
#. About Stephen Benton, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.stephen-benton.about.3"
msgid "He returned to MIT in 1980, founded its Spatial Imaging Group in 1982 and was on the founding faculty of the Media Lab in 1984."
msgstr "W 1980 roku wrócił do MIT, w 1982 roku założył tam Spatial Imaging Group, a w 1984 roku należał do założycielskiej kadry Media Lab."

#: people
#. About Stephen Benton, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.stephen-benton.about.4"
msgid "In 1989 he supervised Mary Lou Jepsen's master's thesis on the design and building of a holographic video display. He later directed the Center for Advanced Visual Studies."
msgstr "W 1989 roku był promotorem pracy magisterskiej Mary Lou Jepsen o projektowaniu i budowie holograficznego wyświetlacza wideo. Później kierował Center for Advanced Visual Studies."

#: people
#. About Mary Lou Jepsen, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.mary-lou-jepsen.about.1"
msgid "She studied electrical engineering and took a doctorate in optical physics at Brown University. As an artist she worked mainly in large scale holography."
msgstr "Studiowała elektrotechnikę i uzyskała doktorat z fizyki optycznej na Uniwersytecie Browna. Jako artystka zajmowała się głównie holografią wielkoformatową."

#: people
#. About Mary Lou Jepsen, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.mary-lou-jepsen.about.2"
msgid "Her master's degree at the MIT Media Lab was in computational holography. Her thesis of 1989, supervised by Stephen Benton, was titled Holographic Video: Design and Implementation of a Display System."
msgstr "Tytuł magistra w MIT Media Lab zdobyła w dziedzinie holografii obliczeniowej. Jej praca z 1989 roku, napisana pod kierunkiem Stephena Bentona, nosiła tytuł Holographic Video: Design and Implementation of a Display System."

#: people
#. About Mary Lou Jepsen, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.mary-lou-jepsen.about.3"
msgid "She was chief technology officer and chief architect of the One Laptop per Child laptop, and chief technology officer of the display division at Intel. She also ran a display company based in Taipei."
msgstr "Była dyrektorką ds. technologii i główną architektką laptopa One Laptop per Child oraz dyrektorką ds. technologii działu wyświetlaczy w Intelu. Prowadziła też firmę produkującą wyświetlacze z siedzibą w Tajpej."

#: people
#. About Mary Lou Jepsen, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.mary-lou-jepsen.about.4"
msgid "She directed engineering at Google X, where she founded and led two programmes, and at Facebook, where her work included virtual reality at Oculus. She founded Openwater, to put imaging of MRI quality into a wearable device."
msgstr "Kierowała pracami inżynieryjnymi w Google X, gdzie założyła i prowadziła dwa programy, oraz w Facebooku, gdzie zajmowała się między innymi rzeczywistością wirtualną w Oculusie. Założyła Openwater, by zmieścić obrazowanie o jakości rezonansu magnetycznego w urządzeniu do noszenia na ciele."

#: people
#. About Ali Javan, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ali-javan.about.1"
msgid "He came to the United States in 1949 and took his doctorate in physics at Columbia University in 1954, under Charles Townes, without a bachelor's or master's degree."
msgstr "W 1949 roku przyjechał do Stanów Zjednoczonych, a w 1954 roku uzyskał doktorat z fizyki na Uniwersytecie Columbia pod kierunkiem Charlesa Townesa, nie mając licencjatu ani tytułu magistra."

#: people
#. About Ali Javan, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ali-javan.about.2"
msgid "He worked out the principle of the helium and neon laser in 1958. At Bell Laboratories, with his colleague William Bennett, he had the laser running on 12 December 1960. The next day it carried a telephone conversation."
msgstr "W 1958 roku opracował zasadę działania lasera na helu i neonie. W Bell Laboratories, pracując razem z Williamem Bennettem, uruchomił laser 12 grudnia 1960 roku. Następnego dnia laser przeniósł rozmowę telefoniczną."

#: people
#. About Ali Javan, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ali-javan.about.3"
msgid "He joined the Massachusetts Institute of Technology in 1961 and held the Francis Wright Davis chair of physics from 1978 to 1996. He was inducted into the National Inventors Hall of Fame in 2006."
msgstr "W 1961 roku przeszedł do Massachusetts Institute of Technology, gdzie w latach od 1978 do 1996 zajmował katedrę fizyki imienia Francisa Wrighta Davisa. W 2006 roku został przyjęty do National Inventors Hall of Fame."

#: people
#. About Nasser Peyghambarian, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.nasser-peyghambarian.about.1"
msgid "He took his doctorate in solid state physics at Indiana University in 1982 and came to the Optical Sciences Center at the University of Arizona as a postdoctoral fellow."
msgstr "W 1982 roku uzyskał doktorat z fizyki ciała stałego na Indiana University i przyszedł do Optical Sciences Center na University of Arizona jako stażysta podoktorski."

#: people
#. About Nasser Peyghambarian, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.nasser-peyghambarian.about.2"
msgid "A professor of optical sciences and of materials science and engineering, he directed a National Science Foundation research centre for integrated access networks and founded two companies, NP Photonics and TIPD."
msgstr "Jako profesor nauk optycznych oraz materiałoznawstwa i inżynierii materiałowej kierował centrum badawczym National Science Foundation zajmującym się zintegrowanymi sieciami dostępowymi i założył dwie firmy, NP Photonics i TIPD."

#: people
#. About Nasser Peyghambarian, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.nasser-peyghambarian.about.3"
msgid "He led the team behind the 2010 telepresence display, a 17 inch screen fed by sixteen cameras, and said it could help in surgery. He was named a fellow of the National Academy of Inventors in 2016."
msgstr "Kierował zespołem, który stworzył wyświetlacz do teleobecności z 2010 roku, ekran o przekątnej 17 cali zasilany obrazem z szesnastu kamer, i mówił, że mógłby on pomagać w chirurgii. W 2016 roku National Academy of Inventors nadała mu tytuł fellow."

#: people
#. About Pierre-Alexandre Blanche, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.pierre-alexandre-blanche.about.1"
msgid "At the University of Arizona's optical sciences college he worked in diffractive optics and holography. He was lead author of the 2010 report on holographic telepresence from the group."
msgstr "W kolegium nauk optycznych University of Arizona zajmował się optyką dyfrakcyjną i holografią. Był głównym autorem raportu tej grupy z 2010 roku o holograficznej teleobecności."

#: people
#. About Pierre-Alexandre Blanche, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.pierre-alexandre-blanche.about.2"
msgid "In that system one computer turned the views of sixteen cameras into data for hogels, which Physics World calls holographic pixels. It sent the data over Ethernet to a second computer, which had a laser write them onto the polymer screen."
msgstr "W tym systemie jeden komputer przetwarzał obrazy z szesnastu kamer na dane dla hogeli, które Physics World nazywa holograficznymi pikselami. Przesyłał je przez Ethernet do drugiego komputera, który za pomocą lasera zapisywał je na ekranie z polimeru."

#: people
#. About Pierre-Alexandre Blanche, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.pierre-alexandre-blanche.about.3"
msgid "In 2021 he won an Optimax grant toward a curved head-up display built on a waveguide. Optica made him a fellow, citing holographic 3D displays and augmented reality combiners."
msgstr "W 2021 roku otrzymał grant Optimax na zakrzywiony wyświetlacz przezierny oparty na falowodzie. Optica nadała mu tytuł fellow, wskazując holograficzne wyświetlacze 3D i kombinery do rzeczywistości rozszerzonej."

#: people
#. About Ivan Sutherland, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ivan-sutherland.about.1"
msgid "Born in Hastings, Nebraska, he studied at the Carnegie Institute of Technology and Caltech and took his doctorate at MIT in 1963 under Claude Shannon, with a thesis on Sketchpad, a graphical system for drawing with a computer."
msgstr "Urodził się w Hastings w stanie Nebraska, studiował w Carnegie Institute of Technology i w Caltechu, a w 1963 roku uzyskał doktorat w MIT pod kierunkiem Claude'a Shannona na podstawie rozprawy o Sketchpadzie, graficznym systemie do rysowania za pomocą komputera."

#: people
#. About Ivan Sutherland, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ivan-sutherland.about.2"
msgid "In 1964 he succeeded J. C. R. Licklider as head of the Information Processing Techniques Office of the Advanced Research Projects Agency, in the United States Department of Defense. From 1965 to 1968 he was an associate professor at Harvard University."
msgstr "W 1964 roku zastąpił J. C. R. Licklidera na stanowisku szefa Information Processing Techniques Office w Advanced Research Projects Agency, agencji Departamentu Obrony Stanów Zjednoczonych. W latach od 1965 do 1968 był profesorem nadzwyczajnym na Uniwersytecie Harvarda."

#: people
#. About Ivan Sutherland, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ivan-sutherland.about.3"
msgid "In 1968, with the student Bob Sproull, he built a headset that hung from the ceiling and was nicknamed the Sword of Damocles. The Association for Computing Machinery calls it the first head-mounted display for virtual and augmented reality."
msgstr "W 1968 roku wraz ze studentem Bobem Sproullem zbudował zestaw nagłowny podwieszony do sufitu, nazywany Mieczem Damoklesa. Association for Computing Machinery nazywa go pierwszym wyświetlaczem nagłownym do rzeczywistości wirtualnej i rozszerzonej."

#: people
#. About Ivan Sutherland, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.ivan-sutherland.about.4"
msgid "He taught at the University of Utah from 1968 to 1974 and co-founded Evans and Sutherland with David Evans. He received the Turing Award in 1988. In 1990 Sun Microsystems bought Sutherland, Sproull and Associates, the consulting firm he founded in 1980."
msgstr "W latach od 1968 do 1974 wykładał na University of Utah i współzałożył z Davidem Evansem firmę Evans and Sutherland. W 1988 roku otrzymał Nagrodę Turinga. W 1990 roku Sun Microsystems kupił Sutherland, Sproull and Associates, firmę konsultingową, którą założył w 1980 roku."

#: people
#. About Bob Sproull, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.bob-sproull.about.1"
msgid "According to the Association for Computing Machinery, he was the student who helped Ivan Sutherland build the head-mounted display of 1968 nicknamed the Sword of Damocles."
msgstr "Według Association for Computing Machinery był studentem, który pomógł Ivanowi Sutherlandowi zbudować wyświetlacz nagłowny z 1968 roku, nazywany Mieczem Damoklesa."

#: people
#. About Bob Sproull, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.bob-sproull.about.2"
msgid "He worked at the Xerox Palo Alto Research Center and was an associate professor of computer science at Carnegie Mellon University, then a principal of Sutherland, Sproull and Associates. He joined Sun Microsystems in 1990."
msgstr "Pracował w Xerox Palo Alto Research Center i był profesorem nadzwyczajnym informatyki na Carnegie Mellon University, a następnie wspólnikiem w Sutherland, Sproull and Associates. W 1990 roku dołączył do Sun Microsystems."

#: people
#. About Bob Sproull, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.bob-sproull.about.3"
msgid "By 1992 he was a vice president and fellow of Sun Microsystems Laboratories, setting up a section of it in Billerica, Massachusetts. He retired as vice president and director of Oracle Labs. That research group began at Sun, which Oracle bought in 2010."
msgstr "W 1992 roku był już wiceprezesem i fellow Sun Microsystems Laboratories i tworzył oddział tych laboratoriów w Billerica w stanie Massachusetts. Przeszedł na emeryturę jako wiceprezes i dyrektor Oracle Labs. Ta grupa badawcza powstała w Sun, kupionym przez Oracle w 2010 roku."

#: people
#. About Bob Sproull, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.bob-sproull.about.4"
msgid "With William Newman he wrote the textbook Principles of Interactive Computer Graphics. He built clipping hardware, a graphics package independent of any one device and laser printing software, and worked on asynchronous circuits. He was elected to the National Academy of Engineering."
msgstr "Razem z Williamem Newmanem napisał podręcznik Principles of Interactive Computer Graphics. Zbudował sprzęt do obcinania grafiki, pakiet graficzny niezależny od konkretnego urządzenia i oprogramowanie do drukowania laserowego, a także zajmował się układami asynchronicznymi. Został wybrany do National Academy of Engineering."

#: people
#. About Carolina Cruz-Neira, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.carolina-cruz-neira.about.1"
msgid "IEEE Spectrum says she was born in Spain and grew up between Spain and Venezuela. Carolina Cruz-Neira took a bachelor's degree in systems engineering at the Universidad Metropolitana in Caracas."
msgstr "IEEE Spectrum podaje, że urodziła się w Hiszpanii i dorastała między Hiszpanią a Wenezuelą. Carolina Cruz-Neira uzyskała licencjat z inżynierii systemów na Universidad Metropolitana w Caracas."

#: people
#. About Carolina Cruz-Neira, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.carolina-cruz-neira.about.2"
msgid "At the University of Illinois at Chicago she took a master's degree in 1991 and a doctorate in 1995, both in electrical engineering and computer science. At Iowa State University she was Litton Assistant Professor of electrical and computer engineering."
msgstr "Na Uniwersytecie Illinois w Chicago uzyskała magisterium w 1991 roku i doktorat w 1995 roku, oba z elektrotechniki i informatyki. Na Iowa State University była adiunktką na stanowisku Litton w dziedzinie elektrotechniki i inżynierii komputerowej."

#: people
#. About Carolina Cruz-Neira, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.carolina-cruz-neira.about.3"
msgid "The University of Central Florida says she founded and led three research centres: the Virtual Reality Applications Center at Iowa State, the Louisiana Immersive Technologies Enterprise, and the Emerging Analytics Center at the University of Arkansas at Little Rock."
msgstr "Uniwersytet Centralnej Florydy podaje, że założyła trzy ośrodki badawcze i nimi kierowała: Virtual Reality Applications Center na Iowa State, Louisiana Immersive Technologies Enterprise oraz Emerging Analytics Center na Uniwersytecie Arkansas w Little Rock."

#: people
#. About Carolina Cruz-Neira, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.carolina-cruz-neira.about.4"
msgid "She was elected to the National Academy of Engineering in 2018, for her contributions to immersive visualization. She joined the University of Central Florida in 2020 and holds its Agere Chair in computer science. In 2026 she received the Virtual Reality Lifetime Achievement Award."
msgstr "W 2018 roku została wybrana do Narodowej Akademii Inżynierii za wkład w wizualizację immersyjną. W 2020 roku przeszła na Uniwersytet Centralnej Florydy i zajmuje tam profesurę Agere w dziedzinie informatyki. W 2026 roku otrzymała Virtual Reality Lifetime Achievement Award."

#: people
#. About Daniel Sandin, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.daniel-sandin.about.1"
msgid "Daniel Sandin took a bachelor's degree in physics at Shimer College and a master's degree in physics at the University of Wisconsin. In 1969 he joined the School of Art and Design at the University of Illinois at Chicago."
msgstr "Daniel Sandin uzyskał licencjat z fizyki w Shimer College i magisterium z fizyki na Uniwersytecie Wisconsin. W 1969 roku dołączył do Szkoły Sztuki i Projektowania Uniwersytetu Illinois w Chicago."

#: people
#. About Daniel Sandin, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.daniel-sandin.about.2"
msgid "In 1973 he built the Sandin Image Processor, an analog computer that altered video pictures in real time. The Museum of Modern Art in New York put his video animation Spiral PTL in its inaugural collection of video art."
msgstr "W 1973 roku zbudował Sandin Image Processor, komputer analogowy, który zmieniał obraz wideo w czasie rzeczywistym. Muzeum Sztuki Nowoczesnej w Nowym Jorku włączyło jego animację wideo Spiral PTL do swojej inauguracyjnej kolekcji sztuki wideo."

#: people
#. About Daniel Sandin, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.daniel-sandin.about.3"
msgid "With Thomas DeFanti he set up the Electronic Visualization Laboratory at the university in 1973. By 1992 the two were its co-directors."
msgstr "Wraz z Thomasem DeFantim założył w 1973 roku na tym uniwersytecie Electronic Visualization Laboratory. W 1992 roku obaj byli już jego współdyrektorami."

#: people
#. About Daniel Sandin, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.daniel-sandin.about.4"
msgid "In later years he worked on displays that show depth without glasses. He is professor emeritus at the university and director emeritus of the laboratory."
msgstr "W późniejszych latach pracował nad wyświetlaczami, które pokazują głębię bez okularów. Jest profesorem emerytowanym uniwersytetu i emerytowanym dyrektorem laboratorium."

#: people
#. About Thomas DeFanti, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.thomas-defanti.about.1"
msgid "Thomas DeFanti took a bachelor's degree in mathematics at Queens College in 1969. At The Ohio State University he took a master's degree in 1970 and a doctorate in 1973, both in computer and information science."
msgstr "Thomas DeFanti uzyskał licencjat z matematyki w Queens College w 1969 roku. Na Ohio State University uzyskał magisterium w 1970 roku i doktorat w 1973 roku, oba z informatyki i nauk o informacji."

#: people
#. About Thomas DeFanti, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.thomas-defanti.about.2"
msgid "He moved to the University of Illinois at Chicago in 1973 and set up the Electronic Visualization Laboratory with Daniel Sandin. In 1992 he was codirector of the laboratory and a professor of electrical engineering and computer science."
msgstr "W 1973 roku przeszedł na Uniwersytet Illinois w Chicago i założył z Danielem Sandinem Electronic Visualization Laboratory. W 1992 roku był współdyrektorem laboratorium i profesorem elektrotechniki i informatyki."

#: people
#. About Thomas DeFanti, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.thomas-defanti.about.3"
msgid "The laboratory's retrospective says he was responsible for Showcase, the event at SIGGRAPH 1992 in Chicago where the CAVE was shown. The conference record names James E. George, of Mesa Graphics, as the chair of its exhibits and Showcase."
msgstr "Retrospektywa laboratorium podaje, że odpowiadał za Showcase, wydarzenie na SIGGRAPH 1992 w Chicago, na którym pokazano CAVE. W materiałach konferencji jako osoba przewodnicząca wystawom i Showcase figuruje James E. George z Mesa Graphics."

#: people
#. About Thomas DeFanti, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.thomas-defanti.about.4"
msgid "The Association for Computing Machinery gave him its Outstanding Contribution Award in 1988 and elected him a fellow in 1994. He is a research scientist at the California Institute for Telecommunications and Information Technology, at the University of California, San Diego."
msgstr "Association for Computing Machinery przyznało mu w 1988 roku Outstanding Contribution Award, a w 1994 roku nadało mu tytuł fellow. Jest badaczem w California Institute for Telecommunications and Information Technology na Uniwersytecie Kalifornijskim w San Diego."

#: people
#. About Greg Dawe, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.greg-dawe.about.1"
msgid "The laboratory's retrospective of 2024 credits Greg Dawe with its later displays derived from the CAVE, among them the ImmersaDesk and Varrier. In the 2000s Dawe joined Thomas DeFanti at the University of California, San Diego, and built room-sized displays of the same kind."
msgstr "Retrospektywa laboratorium z 2024 roku przypisuje Gregowi Dawe późniejsze wyświetlacze laboratorium wywodzące się z CAVE, wśród nich ImmersaDesk i Varrier. W pierwszej dekadzie XXI wieku droga zawodowa zaprowadziła Dawe do Thomasa DeFantiego na Uniwersytet Kalifornijski w San Diego, gdzie spod ręki Dawe wyszły wyświetlacze tego samego rodzaju wielkości pomieszczenia."

#: people
#. About Greg Dawe, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 2. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.greg-dawe.about.2"
msgid "Dawe is the second of nine authors, after DeFanti, of the paper of 2009 on one of them, the StarCAVE."
msgstr "Nazwisko Dawe stoi jako drugie z dziewięciu, po DeFantim, pod artykułem z 2009 roku o jednym z tych wyświetlaczy, StarCAVE."

#: people
#. About Samuel Achilefu, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.samuel-achilefu.about.1"
msgid "After college in Nigeria, a French government scholarship took him to the University of Nancy, where he took a doctorate in molecular and materials chemistry. He trained at Oxford, then joined the discovery research department of Mallinckrodt Medical in St. Louis in 1993."
msgstr "Po studiach w Nigerii stypendium rządu francuskiego zaprowadziło go na Uniwersytet w Nancy, gdzie uzyskał doktorat z chemii molekularnej i materiałowej. Szkolił się w Oksfordzie, a w 1993 roku dołączył do działu badań odkrywczych Mallinckrodt Medical w St. Louis."

#: people
#. About Samuel Achilefu, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.samuel-achilefu.about.2"
msgid "At Washington University he was professor of radiology and of biomedical engineering. A team he led developed the goggles, with Viktor Gruev of the engineering school and Ron Liang of the University of Arizona. The National Cancer Institute funded the work."
msgstr "Na Washington University był profesorem radiologii i inżynierii biomedycznej. Zespół, którym kierował, opracował gogle wraz z Viktorem Gruevem z wydziału inżynierii i Ronem Liangiem z University of Arizona. Prace finansował National Cancer Institute."

#: people
#. About Samuel Achilefu, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.samuel-achilefu.about.3"
msgid "In 2016 he was installed as Michel M. Ter-Pogossian Professor of Radiology. In February 2022 he moved to UT Southwestern Medical Center to chair its department of biomedical engineering."
msgstr "W 2016 roku uroczyście objął stanowisko profesora radiologii imienia Michela M. Ter-Pogossiana. W lutym 2022 roku przeszedł do UT Southwestern Medical Center, by pokierować tamtejszym wydziałem inżynierii biomedycznej."

#: people
#. About J. M. Naish, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.j-m-naish.about.1"
msgid "He worked at the Royal Aircraft Establishment, Farnborough. A technical note of 1962 set out the form of the steering information his head-up display gave the pilot, and weighed how bright it must be against a desert sky."
msgstr "Pracował w Royal Aircraft Establishment w Farnborough. Notatka techniczna z 1962 roku określała postać informacji sterujących, które jego wyświetlacz przezierny przekazywał pilotowi, i rozważała, jak jasny musi być na tle pustynnego nieba."

#: people
#. About J. M. Naish, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.j-m-naish.about.2"
msgid "In a paper of 1965 he reported that the display could be learned easily and used accurately. He proposed it as a monitor for automatic landing, and for the directed take-off."
msgstr "W artykule z 1965 roku podał, że obsługi wyświetlacza można się łatwo nauczyć i że pozwala on na dokładne użycie. Zaproponował go jako monitor do automatycznego lądowania oraz do kierowanego startu."

#: people
#. About J. M. Naish, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.j-m-naish.about.3"
msgid "By 1979 he was at NASA Ames Research Center as a research associate of the National Research Council. His review of head-up display formats there found neither of the two main kinds fully adequate."
msgstr "W 1979 roku pracował w NASA Ames Research Center jako pracownik naukowy National Research Council. Jego przegląd formatów wyświetlaczy przeziernych z tamtego okresu wykazał, że żaden z dwóch głównych rodzajów nie jest w pełni wystarczający."

#: people
#. About Mozi, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.mozi.about.1"
msgid "Scholars call him Mozi, Master Mo, and give his full name as Mo Di. Chris Fraser, in the Stanford Encyclopedia of Philosophy, writes that little is known of him, not even the state he came from."
msgstr "Badacze nazywają go Mozi, czyli Mistrz Mo, i podają jego pełne imię jako Mo Di. Chris Fraser pisze w Stanford Encyclopedia of Philosophy, że niewiele o nim wiadomo, nawet to, z jakiego państwa pochodził."

#: people
#. About Mozi, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.mozi.about.2"
msgid "His dates are uncertain. Matthias Schemmel and William G. Boltz report the traditional dates of about 479 to 381 BCE and say there is little solid record for them. They allow that Mozi may have been an epithet rather than a name."
msgstr "Jego daty życia są niepewne. Matthias Schemmel i William G. Boltz podają tradycyjne daty, od około 479 do 381 roku p.n.e., i piszą, że brakuje dla nich solidnych źródeł. Dopuszczają, że Mozi mogło być przydomkiem, a nie imieniem."

#: people
#. About Mozi, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.mozi.about.3"
msgid "Fraser writes that the Shi Ji records only that he was an official of the state of Song. He conjectures that Mozi began as a craftsman, probably a carpenter."
msgstr "Fraser pisze, że Shi Ji odnotowuje jedynie, iż był urzędnikiem państwa Song. Przypuszcza, że Mozi zaczynał jako rzemieślnik, prawdopodobnie cieśla."

#: people
#. About Mozi, on that person's own page: paragraph 4 of 4. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.mozi.about.4"
msgid "The Canon makes up chapters 40 to 43 of the book Mozi. Schemmel and Boltz say it was put together by an indeterminate number of hands. It explains an inverted image by light running in straight lines and crossing at a pinhole."
msgstr "Kanon obejmuje rozdziały od 40 do 43 księgi Mozi. Schemmel i Boltz piszą, że złożyła go nieokreślona liczba rąk. Kanon wyjaśnia odwrócony obraz tym, że światło biegnie po liniach prostych i krzyżuje się w otworku."

#: people
#. About Kazuo Yoshinaka, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.kazuo-yoshinaka.about.1"
msgid "Kazuo Yoshinaka is the inventor named on Japanese patent application JPS61198892A, Display device, with NEC as applicant. The record gives a filing date of 27 February 1985 and publication on 3 September 1986."
msgstr "Japońskie zgłoszenie patentowe JPS61198892A, Display device, którego zgłaszającym jest NEC, podaje w rubryce wynalazcy nazwisko Kazuo Yoshinaka. Zapis podaje datę zgłoszenia 27 lutego 1985 roku i datę publikacji 3 września 1986 roku."

#: people
#. About Kazuo Yoshinaka, on that person's own page: paragraph 2 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.kazuo-yoshinaka.about.2"
msgid "The application describes a beam of light swept across the retina by a scanner, guided by a detector of eye movement, with no intermediate screen. Two such units could show each eye a different picture for stereoscopic viewing."
msgstr "Zgłoszenie opisuje wiązkę światła przesuwaną po siatkówce przez skaner pod kontrolą czujnika ruchu oka, bez pośredniego ekranu. Dwa takie zespoły mogłyby pokazywać każdemu oku inny obraz, co pozwala na widzenie stereoskopowe."

#: people
#. About Kazuo Yoshinaka, on that person's own page: paragraph 3 of 3. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.kazuo-yoshinaka.about.3"
msgid "A 2017 review by Lin and colleagues in Frontiers of Optoelectronics cites the application in its history of retinal projection displays. Google Patents lists it among documents cited by University of Washington patents for a virtual retinal display."
msgstr "Przegląd z 2017 roku w Frontiers of Optoelectronics, podpisany przez zespół z nazwiskiem Lin na czele, przytacza to zgłoszenie w swojej historii wyświetlaczy z projekcją na siatkówkę. Google Patents wymienia je wśród dokumentów cytowanych w patentach University of Washington na wirtualny wyświetlacz siatkówkowy."

#: people
#. About Auguste Berthier, on that person's own page: paragraph 1 of 1. Plain statements in the past tense, without praise. Keep the names of people, firms and institutions as they are, and the years as numerals.
msgctxt "person.auguste-berthier.about.1"
msgid "Sam H. Kaplan, in the Journal of the Society of Motion Picture Engineers in 1952, said the parallax barrier was generally attributed to Berthier of France, who suggested it in 1896. Kaplan wrote that Frederic Ives applied it to stereoscopic still pictures in 1904."
msgstr "Sam H. Kaplan stwierdził w 1952 roku w Journal of the Society of Motion Picture Engineers, że barierę paralaksy przypisuje się zwykle Berthierowi z Francji, który zaproponował ją w 1896 roku. Kaplan napisał też, że Frederic Ives zastosował ją do stereoskopowych zdjęć nieruchomych w 1904 roku."
